 water that's supposed to replace the Sabbat. From all I have heard about the cults, they are even less interesting than the Anarchs or cam, which takes effort. At least the Cam are decent antagonists and targets, the cults don't even have that, and the Anarchs have so much plot armor, and the devs want me to like them so much, that I just ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-13-2020, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T23:55:29-07:00","id":1396131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396130#post1396130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your right; the two porridge factions and the water that's supposed to replace the Sabbat. <b>From all I have heard about the cults, they are even less interesting than the Anarchs or cam, which takes effort.</b> At least the Cam are decent antagonists and targets, the cults don't even have that, and the Anarchs have so much plot armor, and the devs want me to like them so much, that I just ignore them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you don't know because you haven't read the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Praise Mithras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T02:47:15-07:00","id":1396142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396131#post1396131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet you don't know because you haven't read the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Praise Mithras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because I am have been underwhelmed with every book so far, I am not willing to gamble that the pattern will break for this one, I don't have the money to invest on a vague hope. Also you have been praising the systems in it, and by what you have been saying they don't sound interesting, or use the frankly awful lore sheets, or both,<br /> <br /> But back on topic: they are trying to pull the setting back together, not have warring splats, so expect everywhere to be Cam, anarch or rarely Sabbat, and don't hold out hope of other factions turning up beyond vague mentions for a while (hell the Sabbat aren't even a fleshed out sect yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-13-2020, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T03:43:12-07:00","id":1396146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396130#post1396130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your right; the two porridge factions and the water that's supposed to replace the Sabbat. From all I have heard about the cults, they are even less interesting than the Anarchs or cam, which takes effort. At least the Cam are decent antagonists and targets, the cults don't even have that, and the Anarchs have so much plot armor, and the devs want me to like them so much, that I just ignore them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who HAS read the books, your pretty much on the ball. I'm not sure who it is who has a hard-on for &quot; Vampire Religious Fringe Groups&quot; as a concept but they're really not that interesting and forcing them to be fundamental parts of every single faction now is just grating and boring. If they'd been done in ways similar to Roads I could perhaps see the attraction but the majority of them are just either 'Methusalah fan clubs' or slightly twisted takes on mortal fringe religions. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:15:11-07:00","id":1396175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396146#post1396146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone who HAS read the books, your pretty much on the ball. I'm not sure who it is who has a hard-on for &quot; Vampire Religious Fringe Groups&quot; as a concept but they're really not that interesting and forcing them to be fundamental parts of every single faction now is just grating and boring. If they'd been done in ways similar to Roads I could perhaps see the attraction but the majority of them are just either 'Methusalah fan clubs' or slightly twisted takes on mortal fringe religions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My take on them is they're not fundamental parts of every faction, though Gehenna and Ancestor Cults were always a (secret) part of the Camarilla. Blood Cults are actual factions in their own right with the Hecata being the largest and most powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:23:02-07:00","id":1396190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396175#post1396175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My take on them is they're not fundamental parts of every faction, though Gehenna and Ancestor Cults were always a (secret) part of the Camarilla. Blood Cults are actual factions in their own right with the Hecata being the largest and most powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just hope I can play a Samedi/Harbinger etc who didn't join the Hekata, it makes not a lick of sense, the point was to eradicate the usurpers, not join them. (Plus everyone has painful bite...wut? If they have to have a clan weakness [which also makes very little sense] it should be the Cappadocian one)<br /> <br /> Also is that your take as in your home brew, or an interpretation supported by the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-13-2020, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:40:17-07:00","id":1396191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396142#post1396142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I am have been underwhelmed with every book so far, I am not willing to gamble that the pattern will break for this one, I don't have the money to invest on a vague hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say, if you're interested in running a V5 game, <i>Cults</i> is a better investment than <i>Camarilla</i>, <i>Anarchs</i>, or even <i>Chicago</i> (unless your game is set in Chicago), and most definitely better than <i>Fall of London</i>. It's my favorite of the supplements so far and imo the best-written.<br /> <br /> (But if you're not planning to run or play V5, yeah, none of the books are really worth your money.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:42:02-07:00","id":1396192,"title":"","content":"I'll throw a bone in this thread. The things that could be &quot;riding&quot; the Kindred (who have somehow gotten a foothold in Tokyo of all places despite multiple Uji Kuei-Jin clans holding consolidated domains over the whole city) could be Wraiths from the Jade Kingdom trying to keep tabs on the Camarilla upstarts. Though this could just be hopeful theory-crafting since these new writers seem apt in nuking everything about the old World of Darkness with every opportunity they can muster. Of course this is to assume that maybe Emperor Huang somehow survived (the really hamfisted 6th Maelstorm that conveniently and supposedly wipded &quot;everything&quot; despite the denizens of the Low Umbra surviving multiple other Great Maelstorms before) the 6th GM to resemble his Empire.<br /> <br /> Though it also could be the Kuei-Jin utilizing native Wraiths of the city to spy on the upstart Camarilla- which would make sense since the Low Umbra is very disorganized as of now with the major Underworld Kingdoms being &quot;wiped&quot; if we look from that angle.<br /> <br /> I don't know why you query that Dragon Lines maybe the reason of suppressing the hunger of Kindred in Tokyo, because Dragon Lines have all to do with Chi only and I doubt it would influence Kindred at all. Also Dragon Lines are in more private areas such as gardens, forests, or just generally secluded places in general. It wouldn't be active in the middle of the <i>street</i> where multiple people could disturb the flow of Chi <i>if</i> a Dragon Nest was theoretically active in that random street.<br /> <br /> Also I don't know WHAT clan is this Mayumi chick is from, because the &quot;Old Clan/Dracul&quot; of the Tzimisce are almost all exclusively in East Europe. Not only that there is no incentive for any Old Clan Tzimisce to supposedly embrace some Japanese native. All of them are old, extremely closeted, and most of them live in isolated castle estates. Who the hell was the one to up and decide to make a trip to Tokyo? Especially with the home-ground bane Tzimisce have in general. What incentive would an Old Tzimisce have to achieve to visit Japan at all, enough to put in the work of booking a travel, ensuring they have the right Ghouls for the task of moving his coffin, securing a lodging somehow pre in advance, and making sure to get enough soil to ensure he doesn't begin faltering due to the clan curse. Tell me which of the Old Clan would care enough to do this? Also why is this theoretical Old Clan even Camarilla? They don't care about sect politics at all nor do they cooperate with other Kindred that much at all, even less amongst their own clan even (more so than the current &quot;main&quot; branch of Tzimisce).<br /> <br /> (this is not even to mention the language barrier and he his ghouls would have trying to even communicate with the natives. Sure a very intelligent Tzimisce could attempt to pickup Japanese, but his ghouls? They'd be floundering around the entire city confused making the whole bid to do any activities in Tokyo to be stupid since the Old Tzimisce's servants won't be effective at all)<br /> <br /> It would make more sense for this Mayumi to be a Sabbat Tzimisce since their the one who are more &quot;global&quot; and move around much to claim domain almost anywhere... This doesn't make sense at all and is one of the most bizarre things I've read.<br /> <br /> Also nothing I see here explicitly says the Camarilla has Tokyo secured, just that it has an &quot;influence&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope I can play a Samedi/Harbinger etc who didn't join the Hekata, it makes not a lick of sense, the point was to eradicate the usurpers, not join them. (Plus everyone has painful bite...wut? If they have to have a clan weakness [which also makes very little sense] it should be the Cappadocian one</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is my MAJOR gripe of why I don't like V5 and the additions that they keep making. So many nonsensical things happen with no build up, proper reasoning, or just plain retcon nukes. The Harbingers SOLE purpose was revenge against the Giovanni, that means ERADICATING the entire clan, not &quot;joining a revolt with the young brood of it&quot;. Also the Samedi would NEVER join the Giovanni because of the bad history the clan has with it. Not only that they have no incentive to join it since the Samedi are mostly located in the Americas and don't bother with Europe. Again, more nonsensical stuff. Not to mention the Nagaraja joining this &quot;Sect&quot; (but its really a clan) since their a Necromantic Vampire line that predate almost all of them since in the beginning they were Awakened under the service of Caine who were under his employ- they did a ritual to give themselves Vampirism, so they have NO connection with the Giovanni, Cappodocians, etc. but still get pulled along for some reason.<br /> <br /> Also don't even mention the somehow all consolidated curses they now all suddenly have. Wut, so now the Samedi (same for the Harbingers) are no longer walking corpses? Nagaraja don't need to eat flesh? It's just really transparent they wanted to club out all these clans for this Hecata garbage. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-13-2020, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:51:02-07:00","id":1396194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396190#post1396190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope I can play a Samedi/Harbinger etc who didn't join the Hekata, it makes not a lick of sense, the point was to eradicate the usurpers, not join them. (Plus everyone has painful bite...wut? If they have to have a clan weakness [which also makes very little sense] it should be the Cappadocian one)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Cults</i> doesn't really support playing non-Hecata Samedi/Harbingers, unfortunately. They do still canonically exist, and it doesn't take much homebrew to make them playable (&quot;you have your classic discipline spread, take the classic weakness as a chargen flaw, now go have fun destroying the Venetians!&quot;), but it's not explicitly part of the book.<br /> <br /> As for why they joined the Hecata, the basic idea is that they saw an opportunity to destroy Augustus and his kin by turning their own great-great-whatever-grandchilder against them. The strength of the Giovanni was always their loyalty to the family, and when that loyalty got badly shaken by the Inquisition, the Cappadocian remnants saw an opportunity to get a foot in the door. &quot;Look how your so-called 'family' is willing to let you die en masse to protect their egos. Do they really deserve your devotion at this point? We were once their 'family' too, and here's a long description of all the ways they repaid our trust.&quot;<br /> <br /> (On a meta level, it's based on Luciano's creation of the National Crime Syndicate, where increased pressure and scrutiny from the government led to younger members of the Italian mafia forming tentative alliances with their bitter enemies in the Irish and Jewish mobs, deposing the older Italians, and closing ranks against the outside threat.)<br /> <br /> As for the weakness, agreed. Especially the current mechanical implementation is\u2026not very good. I'm hoping it changes before publication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:53:50-07:00","id":1396195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo#post1396105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Prince of Tokyo is an Old Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <b>2. The city doesn't necessarily answer to the Inner Circle.</b><br /> 3. The Kuei Jin aren't mentioned at all.<br /> 4. SOMETHING spiritual is perhaps riding the Kindred (does that mean Kuei-JIn are spirit-possessed Cainites in canon now?)<br /> 5. Cainites have clearly been in Japan for centuries<br /> 6. Something suppresses the Hunger here (Dragon Lines?)</div> </div> </div> </div>This part in particular, I'm curious how they'll justify. After all, vampires clearly travel to and from the domain (like the narrator does), and I'm pretty sure the Camarilla has enough force on hand to bring them in line if needed. Are they at least paying enough lip service to the Inner Circle that they don't see the need to send Justicars and Archons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T11:48:06-07:00","id":1396197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>I did not feel hunger once. Not once. It\u2019s like something here subdues it. I can\u2019t explain it. I asked my fellow Tremere about it, and even they have no clue.</b> Everything here is measured, calculated, precise. </div> </div> </div>that's reminicent of vampire drones (vampires possessed by the Weaver),<br /> since they're going for the technologically advanced Tokyo, it's fair to assume that some entity like the Weaver or similar (Mikabochi) might have enough power to influence its denizens<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396195#post1396195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part in particular, I'm curious how they'll justify. After all, vampires clearly travel to and from the domain (like the narrator does), and I'm pretty sure the Camarilla has enough force on hand to bring them in line if needed. Are they at least paying enough lip service to the Inner Circle that they don't see the need to send Justicars and Archons?</div> </div> </div> </div>they don't need to pay lip service,<br /> sending Enforcers willy nilly will sets a bad precedent with future princes that would like to join the camarilla<br /> <br /> even if they're the absolute authority, the Jusicars (and Inner circle) still play the game of prestation,<br /> <br /> if the inner circle wants sway over the area,<br /> they need to find an excuse to get their enforcers in,<br /> either the prince asks for help, or there's big enough trouble to send in enforcers (elders getting assassinated, widespread masquerade breaches etc)<br /> <br /> once there, the enforcers can start collecting debts,<br /> if they successfully helped the prince for example, the prince is now indepted to whatever Justicar was involved<br /> <br /> alternatively, the enforcers can locate some rival to the prince and conspire to put them in power,<br /> the new prince now owes the enforcers and, by extension, the inner circle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-13-2020, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:23:50-07:00","id":1396219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396109#post1396109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I wouldn't be surprised if they retconned the Kuei Jin away completely for something else.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're going back to Gaki.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I\u2019m just going throw this out there because this is a PRIME example of why your posts continually get zero likes while Taggie\u2019s comments gets 3-5.<br /> <br /> Every single one of your ideas can be summed up as... take away something that someone enjoys and merge it into fhe same bland soup.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude? Just make it a type of Protean. Dhampirs? Just use Thin-Bloods. Kuei-Jin? Retcon them back to some type of Cainite.<br /> <br /> Every single suggestion you have is to take things away by homogonizing them into a bland stew when the lasting appeal of the original World of Darkness is it\u2019s vivid and spicy unique things that you make the foundation of a character.<br /> <br /> The setting is more compelling when there are unique clan disciplines (i.e. Obtenebration AND Necromancy AND Thanatosis AND Protean AND Serpentis AND Vicissitude), dhampirs that are distinct from thin-blooded vampires and a completely different category of vampire encompassing different aspects of damnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:16:36-07:00","id":1396236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396219#post1396219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I\u2019m just going throw this out there because this is a PRIME example of why your posts continually get zero likes while Taggie\u2019s comments gets 3-5.<br /> <br /> Every single one of your ideas can be summed up as... take away something that someone enjoys and merge it into fhe same bland soup.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude? Just make it a type of Protean. Dhampirs? Just use Thin-Bloods. Kuei-Jin? Retcon them back to some type of Cainite.<br /> <br /> Every single suggestion you have is to take things away by homogonizing them into a bland stew when the lasting appeal of the original World of Darkness is it\u2019s vivid and spicy unique things that you make the foundation of a character.<br /> <br /> The setting is more compelling when there are unique clan disciplines (i.e. Obtenebration AND Necromancy AND Thanatosis AND Protean AND Serpentis AND Vicissitude), dhampirs that are distinct from thin-blooded vampires and a completely different category of vampire encompassing different aspects of damnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris, do me a favor and don't worry about critiquing my posts.<br /> <br /> I'm fine, thanks without your input.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> One thing that I have noticed is the fact people have the weird idea that when I talk about what I think is happening, I automatically support it. I think the Kuei-Jin are gone and are probably not going to be coming back. They're not even the Kuei-Jin anymore since V20 established that such a name was never anything more than a racist portmaneau created by the Camarilla and they were the Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> I should clarify that there's also a difference about speculation, discussing the changes you see happening, and also endorsing them. I don't see much value in complaining about changes that I don't approve of and believe it's rarely helpful. I have done so, of course, and actually started the petition that got the Chechnya section of V5 pulled. I have some regrets about the way that was handled personally.<br /> <br /> If anyone ever wants to ask about what I don't like about V5 then I'm happy to share what my complaints about it are. Since it seems to be that some people don't know what they are, I'll share them:<br /> <br /> * I hate the fact the main book doesn't contain all 13 Clans and Disciplines.<br /> * Touchstones should include more mechanical benefits and be things other than just humans. Also more suggestions than just &quot;throw them off a bridge so Spider-Vamp can angst over it&quot;<br /> * I dislike the fact that there's not a Sabbat book to go with the Camarilla and Anarch guide.<br /> * I felt both the Anarch and Camarilla guides lacked sufficient levels of crunch.<br /> * I really feel like we should have had the Second Inquisition and Players Guide by now. Covid-19 delays a lot but I feel the former should have been handled by now.<br /> * I strongly dislike the Lasombra technology bane.<br /> * I think Quietus should have been folded into Obfuscate not Blood Sorcery. Giving the Banu Haqim Blood Sorcery feels wrong (and it will be doubly so if they don't give the Tzimisce it).<br /> * I think Necromancy should have been folded into Blood Sorcery and the Lasombra should have had Oberternation as a function of Obfuscate.<br /> * I feel like the Web of Knives should have been included in Blood Cults and also at least one Sabbat offshoot.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, I prefer to talk about positive things rather than negative. My love for the game is what drives me rather than my desire to take swipes at something that isn't going to change so I just house rule it and move on. Because other than talking about suggestions for what to do with them, what is the point of discussing it? Everyone's game is different, though, and some people have very different ideas about what the game should be.<br /> <br /> But this is a Tokyo thread so I'm going very off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-13-2020, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:23:45-07:00","id":1396251,"title":"","content":"Well, the answer as to whether or not she is an Old Clan Tzimisce and how she could've been embraced in Japan can be answered by the direction they're taking the Tzimisce in V5, as well as the PC often falling into the category of rare or unique to provide the ability to play the Clan you want in the Sect you want in the locale your Chronicle is set in. SPC/NPCs fitting that criteria to allow it isn't as unusual as you make it sound, one book I've read recently had an Old Clan Tzimisce that was embraced in Sweeden I believe, who was an elder who started his own line from his descendants. I'd have to check which book it is in because I've been binge reading V20 and V5 books, but I know I saw it, and thought it was a great example of how to play one of my favorite clans without too much Sabbat entanglement.<br /> <br /> As for all the Kindred seeming detached, vacant or inside them riding their bodies? Long term exposure to whatever is affecting Hunger, actual possession by spirits or wraiths? Maybe they all devoured the missing Wan Kuei? I remember previous editions mentioning &quot;The Kuei Jin&quot; having difficulties blamed on tainted Chi and Western Corruption in subsisting on anything other than blood and flesh. Maybe the detached, vacant, ridden vampires are the retconned Kuei Jin after being cut off from their Dharmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12527-thearcane","name":"TheArcane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12527_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:46:10-07:00","id":1396263,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. The Old Clan Tzimisce existing outside of the Carpathians is perfectly understandable since the Sabbat didn't bother to go after them and there's a global network of Inconnu that have Watchers in every major city in the world. We also know that plenty of Tzimisce are prone to wanderlust despite their curse due to the fact that the first Tzimisce we've ever read about, Dracula, took his Earth with him to travel the world. Hell, Vlad Dracula could have been the Prince of Tokyo's sire himself.<br /> <br /> 2. It's also possible that Mayumi Shibasaki is part of a much older Old Clan Tzimisce lineage that has been in Japan from the very beginning. In my own games, which I admit prejudices me, Oda Nobunaga was embraced to the Old Clan Tzimisce and the Nobunaga Clan (Tzimisce) are enemies of the Tokugawa Clan (Ventrue).<br /> <br /> 3. I'm pleased to say the Kuei-Jin have always been speaking bullshit about their control over Asia as the Cainites were always there and will always will be. I point to CLANBOOK LASOMBRA REVISED which talked at great length about the Clan's presence in China and their sneering contempt at the idea that the Kuei Jin have ever been able to keep them (or any other Kindred) from Asia. No one puts down the Wan Kuei better than Lasombra.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Controversial</b>: The lack of Hunger in the city combined with the idea of them being Spirit Ridden makes me think that the Kuei-Jin may be retconned as Cainites who have Spirit Thaumaturgy and use Dragon Lines to feed from people without drinking blood. They would follow Paths of Enlightenment and use other methods to rise through the ranks than just Blood Potency. Presumably they would also reject the origins of Caine and Abel.<br /> <br /> 5. Another possibility is the Kuei-Jin just flat out don't control the regions of Asia and there have always been Cainites there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:11:31-07:00","id":1396291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pleased to say the Kuei-Jin have always been speaking bullshit about their control over Asia as the Cainites were always there and will always will be. I point to CLANBOOK LASOMBRA REVISED which talked at great length about the Clan's presence in China and their sneering contempt at the idea that the Kuei Jin have ever been able to keep them (or any other Kindred) from Asia. No one puts down the Wan Kuei better than Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, Vlad Dracula could have been the Prince of Tokyo's sire himself</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility is the Kuei-Jin just flat out don't control the regions of Asia and there have always been Cainites there.</div> </div> </div> </div> ..................lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:24:54-07:00","id":1396295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396291#post1396291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ..................lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem.<br /> <br /> FROM CLANBOOK LASOMBRA REVISED, PAGE 32:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Asia</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>I can establish with some certainty that Lasombra were creating childer in China before 1300 B.C., and that Brujah and Malkavians established broods in the Korean peninsula not later than 1100 B.C. </b>Dating early arrivals by the other clans is difficult. Of course, many of these strangers didn\u2019t last long in the face of opposition by the native Cainite-spirits, whom some of you call Cathayans. It takes great determination and intelligence to flourish amid hostile natives, which of course is why the Lasombra in particular did well for themselves. We have never enjoyed large numbers here, but throughout the recent millennia, a few dozen of us have always made our havens here.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">China</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Traditionally, more Lasombra exist in China than, say, Japan or India, for several reasons. India sees enough Cainite presence from the other clans to make competition both fierce and relatively unchallenging. </b>Little seems distinctive, from our perspective, in grappling once again with Ventrue and Ravnos and so on. No great glory comes to those who survive in such conditions. Further east, matters change. The Cainite-like things who dwell here do afford us great challenges. So do the peculiar mortal hunters with their various preternatural gifts and the fiendish alliances of Lupines and comparable werecreatures of other breeds. Even now, three thousand years after our arrival, much remains mysterious to us. I shouldn\u2019t give the impression that it\u2019s all just fighting other monsters. One can go decades or centuries encountering no other supernatural beings at all, apart from perhaps the occasional ghost. <b>My sire and her sire and his sire and so on back to the Chou dynasty have often exercised power in mortal courts, and half of them never had direct experience with the \u201cCathayans.\u201d</b> </div> </div> </div>Do you think I'm making this up or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-13-2020, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:29:14-07:00","id":1396297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396109#post1396109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I wouldn't be surprised if they retconned the Kuei Jin away completely for something else.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're going back to Gaki.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So they are going back to vampires who are immune to sunlight in smog filled cities who can eat normal food but gain nothing from it and must feed from people balanced in a certain way and have a bunch of powers that no western can use and vice versa....<br /> <br /> Yes Clearly Gaki would be a VAST change from KOTE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:30:46-07:00","id":1396298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396297#post1396297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So they are going back to vampires who are immune to sunlight in smog filled cities who can eat normal food but gain nothing from it and must feed from people balanced in a certain way and have a bunch of powers that no western can use and vice versa....<br /> <br /> Yes Clearly Gaki would be a VAST change from KOTE.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing they SHOULD, just wondering if they ARE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:37:10-07:00","id":1396300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396298#post1396298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not arguing they SHOULD, just wondering if they ARE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am looking right at the Gaki write up in World of Darkness and how different it is than Western vampires. THE only similarity they have is the Embrace. And even that is aparently transferable.<br /> <br /> I don't see how &quot;going back to the Gaki&quot; is at all supported vs... just dropping KJ. That seems to be more in keeping with what is going on.. and even that the Tokyo bit is odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:46:45-07:00","id":1396302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396300#post1396300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am looking right at the Gaki write up in World of Darkness and how different it is than Western vampires. THE only similarity they have is the Embrace. And even that is aparently transferable.<br /> <br /> I don't see how &quot;going back to the Gaki&quot; is at all supported vs... just dropping KJ. That seems to be more in keeping with what is going on.. and even that the Tokyo bit is odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Conceded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T21:17:53-07:00","id":1396309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396295#post1396295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> FROM CLANBOOK LASOMBRA REVISED, PAGE 32:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think I'm making this up or what?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only place Kindred have the greatest influence is in India in Asia. China most of all has the highest concentration and influence of Kuei-Jin in the entirety of that continent. You make it seem as if the Kuei-Jin don't have that, which is hilarious. Sure there are a FEW Vampire clans who have seemed to get some foothold in China, but I believe its mostly due to the part that the Kuei-Jin see these long-term residents as natives practically. Any Camarilla Kindred in China would be promptly done in already if they tried to outright set up domain. It's literally the reason why the only significant presence in China is in Hong Kong if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">direction they're taking the Tzimisce in V5</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What direction for the Tzimisce? They haven't done zilch with them, not even do a book for the Sabbat at all. Y'know its funny that we get an outright mention of the bloodline variation of the Tzimisce in this Camarilla V5 sect book before we even get on the main Tzimisce. Hell there isn't even a V5 Sabbat book at all either too boot, what gives? Camarilla, Anarchs, and a bunch of these &quot;blood cult&quot; thing-a-madigs, but no Sabbat yet? lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-14-2020, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T21:41:42-07:00","id":1396311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396309#post1396309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only place Kindred have the greatest influence is in India in Asia. China most of all has the highest concentration and influence of Kuei-Jin in the entirety of that continent. You make it seem as if the Kuei-Jin don't have that, which is hilarious. Sure there are a FEW Vampire clans who have seemed to get some foothold in China, but I believe its mostly due to the part that the Kuei-Jin see these long-term residents as natives practically. Any Camarilla Kindred in China would be promptly done in already if they tried to outright set up domain. It's literally the reason why the only significant presence in China is in Hong Kong if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying what the official books said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Lasombra had as many members living in China as the Inconnu in Translyavnia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What direction for the Tzimisce? They haven't done zilch with them, not even do a book for the Sabbat at all. Y'know its funny that we get an outright mention of the bloodline variation of the Tzimisce in this Camarilla V5 sect before we even get on the main Tzimisce. Hell there isn't even a V5 Sabbat book at all either too boot, what gives? Camarilla, Anarchs, and a bunch of these &quot;blood cult&quot; thing-a-madigs, but no Sabbat yet? lol. </div> </div> </div>It is weird.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine asked Jason Carl, &quot;Anything coming out on the Sabbat&quot; and he said, &quot;I would be challenged to monomancy if I shared the truth. Which is not anytime soon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T22:05:36-07:00","id":1396313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396311#post1396311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just saying what the official books said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Lasombra had as many members living in China as the Inconnu in Translyavnia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue clan/tribe/kith/tradition/etc books are prone to be from the perspective of well that splat and less from a third person objective perspective on that faction. Unless people do want to buy the idea that all Egyptian Religion was an elaborate social experiment done by the Pooka. Especially the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> So Lasombra claiming they ruled as Godkings of china since whenever, sure why not.. they also believe they successfully diabed their founder!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T22:51:09-07:00","id":1396316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396313#post1396313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue clan/tribe/kith/tradition/etc books are prone to be from the perspective of well that splat and less from a third person objective perspective on that faction. Unless people do want to buy the idea that all Egyptian Religion was an elaborate social experiment done by the Pooka. Especially the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> So Lasombra claiming they ruled as Godkings of china since whenever, sure why not.. they also believe they successfully diabed their founder!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, although Cainites in Middle Kingdom are more numerous than we think, Brujah and Malkavian (deceased long long ago), Ravnos, Anda (deceased in Middle Age), Wu Zao, Lasombra, Giovanni, Cappadocian, Set's Followers, Assamite, Nagaraja, Tremere, Toreador, they always remain secret and relatively rare, well<br /> <br /> Lasombra may be noted in mortal court of Zhou Dynasty due to specially loosen surroundings, but modern? Sorry that's different<br /> <br /> And: It is a pity that Middle Kingdom stuff in Lasombra Revised was never exploited more later, I'm very interested in it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T23:00:30-07:00","id":1396317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396316#post1396316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, although Cainites in Middle Kingdom are more numerous than we think, Brujah and Malkavian (deceased long long ago), Ravnos, Anda (deceased in Middle Age), Wu Zao, Lasombra, Giovanni, Cappadocian, Set's Followers, Assamite, Nagaraja, Tremere, Toreador, they always remain secret and relatively rare, well<br /> <br /> Lasombra may be noted in mortal court of Zhou Dynasty due to specially loosen surroundings, but modern? Sorry that's different<br /> <br /> And: It is a pity that Middle Kingdom stuff in Lasombra Revised was never exploited more later, I'm very interested in it</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they should be the primary supernatural of Asia to reflect the large Asian V:TM fandom in RL.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the Wan Kuei should be wiped away.<br /> <br /> They should continue to exist and have rival feuds between its various groups. They just shouldn't be the Kindred of the East but their own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T00:57:18-07:00","id":1396326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396317#post1396317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should continue to exist and have rival feuds between its various groups. They just shouldn't be the Kindred of the East but their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE has its own shining and unique points, honestly<br /> <br /> Criticism likes racism and stereotypes and so on does hinder its advantages: increasing power with enlightment, fallen heroes who seek to redeem themselves, an united and crossover supernatural world, etc. If it becomes more international and neutral, I think it will be much more popular. Someone used to try writing a &quot;Western&quot; version of them, hailing from the Ancient Greek Legends<br /> <br /> But i<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">t really should be repaired heavily, many things suck hard when in details</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-14-2020, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T01:14:14-07:00","id":1396328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396326#post1396326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KotE has its own shining and unique points, honestly<br /> <br /> Criticism likes racism and stereotypes and so on does hinder its advantages: increasing power with enlightment, fallen heroes who seek to redeem themselves, an united and crossover supernatural world, etc. If it becomes more international and neutral, I think it will be much more popular. Someone used to try writing a &quot;Western&quot; version of them, hailing from the Ancient Greek Legends<br /> <br /> But i<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">t really should be repaired heavily, many things suck hard when in details</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on the Kuei Jin was that it was something worth repairing and making like the Laibon or the Ashirra because I was fond of both things. I was also of the mind that I really liked the Drowned concept and would love to see that expanded more in future supplements. I'm not necessarily against jiangshi as a different type of Vampire that hangs out in Elysium, has Domain, and is a part of Kindred society. China has its own vampire myths and they're pretty awesome as well as a potential source of super-cool stories.<br /> <br /> Intrigue, supernatural hijinks, and horror are perfect for a Chinese setting--quite a few friends in Hong Kong and Tawain have told me about how much they love V:TM. They have....well, mixed feelings about the KOTE.<br /> <br /> My feelings? Well, my personal experiences with the Kuei Jin are the fact that in West Virginia, they were used by some racist players to try and drive out the Asian players in our LARP. It's like Taggie and the Anarchs. I have BAD feelings about the Kuei Jin, not because of the way people played them but a couple of guys went, &quot;Well, they're Asian so my character thinks they're Kuei-Jin infiltrators! An evil race out to destroy good right thinking Kindred!&quot; We fucking banned those guys but there were other nasty stories about it happening with other LARPs. Asian players being &quot;strongly encouraged&quot; to play Kuei Jin because they couldn't be Cainites and white people trying to play Kuei Jin in Live Action that--oh dear God.<br /> <br /> It was a disaster.<br /> <br /> Notably, I've heard it said in interviews that people at Onyx Path have said that they honestly don't know HOW to repair the Kuei Jin without removing what makes them what they are. I also have heard it second-hand that Paradox REALLY does not like them.<br /> <br /> I should also clarify something: <i><b>My college degree is in ASIAN HISTORY and my minor in Chinese Mythology.</b></i><br /> <br /> I should be all over these guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-14-2020, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T02:05:20-07:00","id":1396333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/139