<i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T02:43:37-07:00","id":1396336,"title":"","content":"To me is significant see how most of the LARPS and games announced in Korea and China are played using the cainite clans, not the KotE. This was a book for western fans based on 90s tropes and topics from mangas and movies, but uninteresting for the &quot;easterns&quot;. I enjoyed very much the cathayan part in the Bloodlines 1 and I even played a chronicle based in San Francisco by Night (that is not precisely brilliant) but I am very conscious that it was a very problematic book. The San Francisco by Night cathayans have been removed in V20 in Becket\u00b4s Jyhad Diary, the setting have returned to the Prince Vannevar rulership. And to me, it seems evident that they never will come back. Tokio, Hong Kong and other eastern cities will be retconned as always dominated by cainites. On the other hand, CTPhipps, they say Old Clan, not Old Clan Tzimisce. Old Clan is, probably, the new name of the whole clan as Ministry is now the name for all the Followers of Set. Old Clan are the new Tzimisce, not a bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 06-14-2020, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:31:15-07:00","id":1396350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396336#post1396336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me is significant see how most of the LARPS and games announced in Korea and China are played using the cainite clans, not the KotE. This was a book for western fans based on 90s tropes and topics from mangas and movies, but uninteresting for the &quot;easterns&quot;. I enjoyed very much the cathayan part in the Bloodlines 1 and I even played a chronicle based in San Francisco by Night (that is not precisely brilliant) but I am very conscious that it was a very problematic book. The San Francisco by Night cathayans have been removed in V20 in Becket\u00b4s Jyhad Diary, the setting have returned to the Prince Vannevar rulership. And to me, it seems evident that they never will come back. Tokio, Hong Kong and other eastern cities will be retconned as always dominated by cainites. On the other hand, CTPhipps, they say Old Clan, not Old Clan Tzimisce. Old Clan is, probably, the new name of the whole clan as Ministry is now the name for all the Followers of Set. Old Clan are the new Tzimisce, not a bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it makes sense. People who want to play <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> with all of its conspiracies, prophecies, and archetypal movie clans are going to want to play Cainites. They're the Alliance in our Alliance vs. Horde vs. Expansions comparison. There's a 1000 supplements about Cainites vs. 12 or so Kuei Jin and someone who wants to play a Western vampire game is probably going to do so with the one that represents Western media. The Kuei Jin are far less iconic and a Westerners view of an Easterner's culture whereas, ironically, Cainites are going to have an exotic feel if you're concerned about cultural mythology at all.<br /> <br /> In Warcraft terms, the Kuei Jin are the Pandaren. Some people really love them. Other people just don't think they're worth playing.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Old Clan Tzimisce were ever a Bloodline. Its just the changing nature and role of Vicissitude in the Clan.<br /> <br /> Also, technically the Followers of Set haven't changed names. The Ministry &quot;faction&quot; is revealed to be opposed by the Church of Set so the old Followers of Set are still around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T05:05:05-07:00","id":1396356,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages Vampire Companion, I enjoyed the depiction of Mangalore dominated by a triunvirate or coalition of Ravnos, Danava and Salubri. They achieve a unique setting without introducing new races of vampire or kwe-jin. If I would write the China and Japan settings for 5th, I would try something like that, adapting the Tzimisce, the Salubri and the other cainite clans from the main setting to the eastern culture. The search for enlightment is not exclusive of KotE and a branch of Old Clans and Salubri fighting for supremacy in the East would be a nice way to introduce this bloodlines in the new edition. However, I do not envy the author in charge to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T06:58:58-07:00","id":1396370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kuei Jin are far less iconic</div> </div> </div> </div>Well guess what? Wan Kuei are iconic for fans of the old World of Darkness. Retconning them when they have one of the greatest lore of any of the splats in the franchise would be downright stupid. The only thing that needs to be fixed about them will be taking of the perceived &quot;problematic&quot; things about them (because really, I don't see what is wrong with them at all). The Kuei-Jin are one the reason why I love the World of Darkness (atleast the old variation before all these fiddlements being done to it lately). Its extremely unique and thinks outside its own box, instead of going with the same cliches over and over again. The Kuei-Jin could have been any other Vampire clan at all, but instead whoever thought up the idea of the Wan Kuei and its subsequent lore was brilliant. The Dharma books of the Wan Kuei were one of the best over, the unique Ying and Yang aspect mechanic- to tell whether your &quot;death or life&quot; aspected. All the Shintai techniques? Wondrously amazing.<br /> <br /> The Kuei-Jin/Wan-Kuei, I just don't understand the hate surrounding them. Has anyone even read their corebook at all? They are 100x more interesting than the Kindred. It also doesn't make sense for the Kuei-Jin to be retconned out for Kindred to take over parts of Asia. Wan-Kuei DON'T have generation whatsoever, while the Vampires of the West are constantly shifting to have weaker broods. There is no way they could have adequate shadow wars against the Wan-Kuei when they easily have figures within their spectrum that went toe-to-toe with an Antediluvian. It's an idiotic notion that the Wan-Kuei can be defeated by the Camarilla (because lets face it, as of V5 the Sabbat have been retcon nuked so they wouldn't be fighting for domain in Asia and Anarchs don't have a chance despite V5 going them Plot Armor bones to &quot;establish&quot; themselves more) over CHINA of all places is goobily-poop.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for parts of Japan to be under somesort of Camarilla control because decidedly the mainline of Wan-Kuei don't have control over it- just Japanese Wan-Kuei who call themselves Gaki and organize themselves into Uji (a type of grouping), something that has been wantonly ignored in this lil' Camarilla V5 sect book..<br /> <br /> Not only that retconning the Wan-Kuei WILL mess with other lines- Reckoning, Masquerade (yes because it already IS canon that the Great Leap Forward was a thing in VTM- retconning Kuei-Jin out of nowhere would be dumb. Not only that per the Week of Nightmares- despite me admittedly hating this event because of what it did to Wraith- Kuei Boddhitvas DID fight and held the line against Ravnos. If they are retconned, who fought it?), Werewolf (the Beast Courts thing), and Wraith for the Kuei-Jins heavy connections with Wraith in lieu with the Jade Kingdom of Yu Huang. What will happen to the Yama Kings? They were integral to other splats too, when Voormas had to kill one to further along the plot of Ascension. To put it simply retconning the Kuei-Jin would be MORE trouble than it would be worth- I honestly DON'T know what people find bad about the Wan-Kui/Kuei-Jin at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-14-2020, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:30:25-07:00","id":1396375,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously is subjective, for one Kindred of the East could be the perfect book, but for others it could have some important flaws. Most people I have read agree that the fact that KotE were supremacists and special above all other cultures without their own vampire race was a social problem. But this is a debate that has been argued again and again I do not want to unbury. Above the social matter and the presence or absence of prejudices, the important is if KotE was profitable, I have not meet even a single person who played a Kwe-jin solo campaign. May be it would be interesting to listen your experiences about KotE games and what you believe in practice that made them so interesting and awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:50:43-07:00","id":1396381,"title":"","content":"Wan-Kuei supremacists? Like how the Garou are, Kindred, and Awakened are thinking they are the center of the universe despite multiple other things out there? It isn't anything new. Also how does not having a specific Vampire line not where the Wan-Kuei were a &quot;social problem&quot;? That makes sense since any high presence of Kindred would have been fought down by the Wan-Kuei, only small pockets of Kindred exist in places with the plethora of Wan-Kuei about. Also what can I tell you about what makes them awesome? Their Shintai, the Dharma books they have, the unique entities they fight (Akuma, Bakemoko, the unique Umbral Spirits such as Chih-Chang-Fyu-Ya the rogue archer-general who used to be in service of the August Personage of Jade or Lady Yukio- the spirit attached to a Katana blade and much more), the uniqueness they generally have- honestly its more interesting and original than making up some convoluted reason to be some sort of Jiangshi where they hop around or something (basically not being some weird ethnic Vampire like the Ravnos or the Noiad).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-14-2020, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:53:15-07:00","id":1396382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396316#post1396316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, although Cainites in Middle Kingdom are more numerous than we think, Brujah and Malkavian (deceased long long ago), Ravnos, Anda (deceased in Middle Age), Wu Zao, Lasombra, Giovanni, Cappadocian, Set's Followers, Assamite, Nagaraja, Tremere, Toreador, they always remain secret and relatively rare, well<br /> <br /> Lasombra may be noted in mortal court of Zhou Dynasty due to specially loosen surroundings, but modern? Sorry that's different<br /> <br /> And: It is a pity that Middle Kingdom stuff in Lasombra Revised was never exploited more later, I'm very interested in it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am calling out any statement in any clan book as dubious. They are all about how &quot;We are teh bestest clan ever and we totally beat other groups always!&quot;. I don't think it was expected that we would see any development on the Lasombra in China. The intent was continue a &quot;We are so fucking awesome&quot; narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396350#post1396350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it makes sense. People who want to play <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> with all of its conspiracies, prophecies, and archetypal movie clans are going to want to play Cainites. They're the Alliance in our Alliance vs. Horde vs. Expansions comparison. There's a 1000 supplements about Cainites vs. 12 or so Kuei Jin and someone who wants to play a Western vampire game is probably going to do so with the one that represents Western media. The Kuei Jin are far less iconic and a Westerners view of an Easterner's culture whereas, ironically, Cainites are going to have an exotic feel if you're concerned about cultural mythology at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My limited perspective has been Japanese Media/geeks is... Vampires are a western thing. There AREN'T Asian vampires so of course they will have some sort of Western belief structure. Cainites in the most Cainite sense make well sense from that perspective. There's no concept that they should be a universal thing but rather something born entirely of the West that's spread, like say christianity.<br /> <br /> Also in Monster Mash setups, the Jiang-shi.. is a different creature. They aren't vampires any more than Gangrel are Werewolves. That being Said Masquerade is kind of weird in its whole &quot;vampires and vampire alone&quot; setup. But if you've bought into that offering something that is clearly not a vampire isn't going to change things.<br /> <br /> That being said... Monster Mash was kind of what made Hengeyokai shine. So I would probably invert Jiang-shi as they are sort of the most crossovertastic of WOD creatures having a foot in every game. They are in part why there is a Shen community rather than genocidal hatred between gamelines every night. <br /> <br /> This would Include Kindred, as a creature type but not &quot;all kindred get a pass&quot; since the wounds of colonialism run deep especially for creatures that live centuries and who's formative years were the Century of Shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:00:53-07:00","id":1396384,"title":"","content":"But the umbra, the Dharma/Clan/Tribe/Tradition or whatever books, the entities they fight and even the paths of enlightment are not unique from the KotE, they are very present in other games of World of Darkness. Some of this themes are more central and interconnected in the lore of Mage the Ascension, than in Vampire, where they are completly aside. About the possible racism or fear linked to them, I would recommend to read some of the more old threads about that in this forum. I am not enough fluent in english to explain it with detail. Anyway, their absence it is not a 5th edition choice, they are absent from the whole V20 line too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:25:14-07:00","id":1396391,"title":"","content":"Why would they be present in V20? They are already their own splat by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:29:44-07:00","id":1396393,"title":"","content":"They have been erased from the V20 canon. The Becket\u00b4s Jyhad Diary overwrittes all the San Francisco by Night plots as if they have not existed. Even in Anarchs Unbound they are not barely mentioned in the current state of affairs of the Anarch Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:59:18-07:00","id":1396397,"title":"","content":"They were totally in BJD. The Wan Gui, I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:05:18-07:00","id":1396399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396393#post1396393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have been erased from the V20 canon. The Becket\u00b4s Jyhad Diary overwrittes all the San Francisco by Night plots as if they have not existed. Even in Anarchs Unbound they are not barely mentioned in the current state of affairs of the Anarch Free States.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still remain in V20 and BJD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:10:04-07:00","id":1396401,"title":"","content":"I do not think so, I have read the book and every mentioned to the Kwe Jin is elusive and vague. The authors have rewind the history of the San Francisco by Night as if never happened the invasion. The only kwe-jin mentioned is depicted of an unknown clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:16:09-07:00","id":1396403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396384#post1396384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the umbra, the Dharma/Clan/Tribe/Tradition or whatever books, the entities they fight and even the paths of enlightment are not unique from the KotE, they are very present in other games of World of Darkness. Some of this themes are more central and interconnected in the lore of Mage the Ascension, than in Vampire, where they are completly aside. About the possible racism or fear linked to them, I would recommend to read some of the more old threads about that in this forum. I am not enough fluent in english to explain it with detail. Anyway, their absence it is not a 5th edition choice, they are absent from the whole V20 line too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rites of blood Actively gives a whole secondary explanation for how Spirit manipulation works so as to remove any need to engage with the Umbra at all or any crossover stuff. It can also be used in Crossover obviously. That v20 didn't have KOTE rules rather than off hand remarks to them makes sense because its v20. It also doesn't have more than passing remarks on mages, werewolves, etc. <br /> <br /> But the little lines were referenced if not consistantly often enough in the 20e lines that their existence was still considered even if it wasn't written up.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said retconning out Wan Gui as just a whole bunch of IN universe racism back and forth wouldn't be unreasonable and it wouldn't be the first or last retcon in the setting nor the most extreme. Considering the willingness they were to slaughter actual sacred cows for v5. And converting Wan Gui into theirown full game that is the crossover game would probably do them better than &quot;they keep all the kindred out of Asia&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:19:09-07:00","id":1396404,"title":"","content":"page 118:<br /> <br /> &quot;JIJIE LI<br /> Clan unknown<br /> Ji Leads the New Promise mandarinate in San Francisco and Los \u00c1ngeles, though she seems to be more a diplomat than a warrior...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No mention to dharmas, paths or inner details beyond the name Wan Kei. The plot of having conquered Los \u00c1ngeles and San Francisco it is restarted and there is no evidence that was going to continue further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:20:19-07:00","id":1396406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396401#post1396401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think so, I have read the book and every mentioned to the Kwe Jin is elusive and vague. The authors have rewind the history of the San Francisco by Night as if never happened the invasion. The only kwe-jin mentioned is depicted of an unknown clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are called out explicitly in Da20. The invasion is written up in BJD. They are not treated as Kindred. They are not given much say in V20... but neither are werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:24:08-07:00","id":1396408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396404#post1396404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 118:<br /> <br /> &quot;JIJIE LI<br /> Clan unknown<br /> Ji Leads the New Promise mandarinate in San Francisco and Los \u00c1ngeles, though she seems to be more a diplomat than a warrior...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No mention to dharmas, paths or inner details beyond the name Wan Kei. The plot of having conquered Los \u00c1ngeles and San Francisco it is restarted and there is no evidence that was going to continue further.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sure, they just mention they're &quot;mysterious&quot;, &quot;secret&quot;, but no more. See Black Dragon Princess in Children of Revolution, they also mention them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:26:00-07:00","id":1396410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396404#post1396404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 118:<br /> <br /> &quot;JIJIE LI<br /> Clan unknown<br /> Ji Leads the New Promise mandarinate in San Francisco and Los \u00c1ngeles, though she seems to be more a diplomat than a warrior...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No mention to dharmas, paths or inner details beyond the name Wan Kei. The plot of having conquered Los \u00c1ngeles and San Francisco it is restarted and there is no evidence that was going to continue further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wan Kuei; <b>*unknown, #unknown.</b><br /> Ji leads the New Promise Mandarinate<br /> against San Francisco and Los Angeles,<br /> though she seems to be more of a diplomat<br /> than a warrior. <b>Her diplomacy might be<br /> limited to navigating the politics of her own<br /> kind, however, as she is rumored to look down<br /> on Kindred.</b><br /> <br /> You seem to have left somethings out of your quote.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:27:47-07:00","id":1396411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396404#post1396404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 118:<br /> <br /> &quot;JIJIE LI<br /> Clan unknown<br /> Ji Leads the New Promise mandarinate in San Francisco and Los \u00c1ngeles, though she seems to be more a diplomat than a warrior...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No mention to dharmas, paths or inner details beyond the name Wan Kei. The plot of having conquered Los \u00c1ngeles and San Francisco it is restarted and there is no evidence that was going to continue further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would the western Kindred know about the various Dharmas and structure of Kuei-Jin society at large? They obviously wouldn't. Sure the Great Leap Outward can be retconned, but to say that they Kuei-Jin were outright retconned in BJD or V20 of all things is hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:28:02-07:00","id":1396412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396333#post1396333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lol what? I didn't get the reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> first Anarch players I ever met where basically bullying jocks with difficulty keeping their hands to themselves. (In fact that was the pattern for quite a while, until I stopped doing Vampire larps for the kind I got to wear plate armor and hit people) so yea, they tended to get IC dunked by the local Sabbat fairly fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:30:35-07:00","id":1396413,"title":"","content":"What I am trying to say is that, beyond the name, Wan kei could be anything in BJD, even cainites. They were part of the setting, unlike werewolves, and they received nothing more that a few mentions in the Los \u00c1ngeles chapter, there are no details, no clues about the future of the line, no rules and very lessen importance, they are no more the rulers of California.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:35:03-07:00","id":1396415,"title":"","content":"They were never the &quot;rulers&quot; of California to begin with, having some considerable influence in Los Angeles- one city. Even beyond that of course there isn't that much mention of the Kuei-Jin in a Vampire supplement of all things, it is its own entire splatline already. The whole &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">here are no details, no clues about the future of the line, no rules and very lessen importance&quot; is literally any other splat offhandedly mentioned in another splats book. Just how Werewolf books mention other splats, Mage books mention other splats, and so on. It's ubiquitous. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:43:29-07:00","id":1396417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396415#post1396415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were never the &quot;rulers&quot; of California to begin with, having some considerable influence in Los Angeles- one city. Even beyond that of course there isn't that much mention of the Kuei-Jin in a Vampire supplement of all things, it is its own entire splatline already. The whole &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">here are no details, no clues about the future of the line, no rules and very lessen importance&quot; is literally any other splat offhandedly mentioned in another splats book. Just how Werewolf books mention other splats, Mage books mention other splats, and so on. It's ubiquitous. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend you the lecture of San Francisco by Night book. In there, they are the rulers of SF and soon of LA. They even rise a wall and a guetto to let die slowly the cainites of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:14:21-07:00","id":1396424,"title":"","content":"There's some definite questions of continuity with the Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei and their position in the setting but I think the definitiveness of what has been retconned and not is definitely up in the air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:32:07-07:00","id":1396427,"title":"","content":"At the risk of stepping into a minefield, what I'm personally hoping is that the Wan Gui still exist but there are also Kindred in Asia. The two are fundamentally different things with different themes, and they've never felt like a single unified splat to me. Like how Garou and Kindred and Mummies are fundamentally different types of supernaturals, who deserve separate books and all have different stories to tell.<br /> <br /> In the end, I personally like Kindred the most out of all the OWoD splats, so I like them now existing across the world. One of my online players lives in Japan, for example, and &quot;no you can't build a character who comes from the place you live because there are no Kindred in Tokyo&quot; is a boring answer imo. &quot;Tokyo is ostensibly a Camarilla city but has various strange things and mysteries about it&quot; is much more interesting.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm pretty sure they haven't been retconned out of existence. They're mentioned in at least one of the V5 books.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:09:31-07:00","id":1396439,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> I really Like your answer. I think Wan Gui and Cainites should be able to coexist without killing each other in the same domain in Asia. I also think the invasion of California was retconned in BJD, but not the Wan Gui themselves.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> you mentioned something about the Gaki and the Wan Gui being two different species of Asian vampires. Could you tell me more about that idea? It sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:13:49-07:00","id":1396441,"title":"","content":"For that matter, there\u2019s no reason the Wan Gui couldn\u2019t exist in Western domains. I haven\u2019t actually read them, but I\u2019ve been told there was a Chinese Wan Gui in Boston in the original New England sourcebook and a Japanese Gaki from House Bishamon in Vancouver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:07:36-07:00","id":1396457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396427#post1396427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, I'm pretty sure they haven't been retconned out of existence. They're mentioned in at least one of the V5 books.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What does it say?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:14:34-07:00","id":1396461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396441#post1396441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, there\u2019s no reason the Wan Gui couldn\u2019t exist in Western domains. I haven\u2019t actually read them, but I\u2019ve been told there was a Chinese Wan Gui in Boston in the original New England sourcebook and a Japanese Gaki from House Bishamon in Vancouver.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There was a reason, but was a little strange. The Kwei Jin born from the believers of the far eastern religions, to create a new Kew Jin was necessary that a person who believe in the yomi went to the hell and then escaped. Is not a ethnic matter, but cultural. That was the reason they could not expand far from San Francisco in the old metaplot. There were even some heretic dharmas that were trying to teach their culture with forced marches and then killing their students with the purpose to rise new Kwei Jin. They can not embrace, so they were desperate to extend their influence and strength in California by unorthodox (and heretical) ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:29:01-07:00","id":1396470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396461#post1396461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a reason, but was a little strange. The Kwei Jin born from the believers of the far eastern religions, to create a new Kew Jin was necessary that a person who believe in the yomi went to the hell and then escaped. Is not a ethnic matter, but cultural. That was the reason they could not expand far from San Francisco in the old metaplot. There were even some heretic dharmas that were trying to teach their culture with forced marches and then killing their students with the purpose to rise new Kwei Jin. They can not embrace, so they were desperate to extend their influence and strength in California by unorthodox (and heretical) ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it was the case of overcompensated for perceived player weaknesses. Kuei-Jin can only be made from ethnic Asian peoples and they can only be made in Asian territories because MAGIC [Wastonian].<br /> <br /> [Doyleist] They didn't want players making White American Ninja style characters from America and missing the point of the splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-14-2020, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:31:58-07:00","id":1396472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396457#post1396457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing extensive, just some passing mentions of the invasion of the West Coast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:35:13-07:00","id":1396474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396472#post1396472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing extensive, just some passing mentions of the invasion of the West Coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sadly don't recall that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:41:11-07:00","id":1396477,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1396474I sadly don't recall that.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It's in the Anarch book, in the section about the Free States. As I said, though, just a passing mention, nothing at all extensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:13:12-07:00","id":1396488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396477#post1396477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the Anarch book, in the section about the Free States. As I said, though, just a passing mention, nothing at all extensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about <i>Dee's Blood Guide to the Anarch Free States</i> and Salvador Garcia's loresheet? I just searched for the words &quot;kuei&quot; and &quot;gui &quot; and had no results, but &quot;Chinese&quot; appeared in those two sections:<br /> <br /> &quot;At least two Sabbat invasions, a ton of Camarilla treachery, Chinese vampires trying to establish their own place here.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;She's tried to make deals with everybody from the Camarilla to the Chinese vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They attempt to discredit you by spreading bizarre rumors: You sold out to strange Chinese vampires...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The first two are narrated by Dee, the third is a loresheet point, so pretty much word of God. If that's your reference, it could be about Wan Gui, but it could be about Kindred or even another type of vampire altogether. It doesn't say what's &quot;strange&quot; about them. I assume this is deliberately vague because the writers want to keep the Great Leap Outward in the metaplot of California, but they don't want to confirm or deny that those vampires were Kuei-jin as they were originally written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:19:16-07:00","id":1396491,"title":"","content":"You could easily do Ming Xiao as a Chinese Tzimisce just cultural posturing.<br /> <br /> However, I actually think there's a place for Wan Kuei in V:TM.<br /> <br /> I think the changes needed to be made are:<br /> <br /> * Allow them into the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Blood Cults.<br /> * Have them able to form coteries with Cainites.<br /> * Have them share their own Paths with Kindred<br /> * Simplify the rules for them.<br /> <br /> That way they can be a proper faction in V:TM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T15:54:36-07:00","id":1396510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396375#post1396375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have not meet even a single person who played a Kwe-jin solo campaign. May be it would be interesting to listen your experiences about KotE games and what you believe in practice that made them so interesting and awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. It didn't last very long, but it was quite interesting for the players. However, it's true we are all European and lovers of Asian culture, so maybe we didn't see the flaws in the KotE line...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:15:54-07:00","id":1396516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396510#post1396510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. It didn't last very long, but it was quite interesting for the players. However, it's true we are all European and lovers of Asian culture, so maybe we didn't see the flaws in the KotE line...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've run quite a few successful ones but most of my chronicles are set in SE Asia and Oceania. While I myself am bule, most of my players have been SE Asian, Islander or Indigenous Australian.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why everyone would be suprised at there being Kindred in Asia/Oceania the only place in the past that actively destroyed 'all' Kindred were areas under Quincunx control which was basically just central mainland china. In all other places they were disliked because of the negative effects they had only the local environment and their weird unnatural viral nature but they were there.<br /> <br /> If Hungry Ghosts are gone from V5 I wouldn't be suprised or overly bothered really, V5s trajectory is a long way from the games we enjoy even with the course corrections appearing in the OPP published books.<br /> <br /> If I had my way then, like in my own campaigns, Hungry Ghosts would exist world wide but the systematic destruction of their kind before they emerge from their Cannibal Corpse stage means that in areas where Kindred dominate they are essentially wiped out as they cannot function without an established Ghost Family to help them onto a Dharma/Path.<br /> <br /> In my campaigns Hungry Ghosts were once the dominate form of dead predators, then some muppet had something go terribly wrong with their Second Breath somewhere in Africa ten to twenty thousand years ago....and the Kindred spread across the world like a plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:30:10-07:00","id":1396519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396491#post1396491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I actually think there's a place for Wan Kuei in V:TM.<br /> <br /> I think the changes needed to be made are:<br /> <br /> * Allow them into the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Blood Cults.<br /> * Have them able to form coteries with Cainites.<br /> * Have them share their own Paths with Kindred<br /> * Simplify the rules for them.<br /> <br /> That way they can be a proper faction in V:TM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the changes to the Cam mean that they will never allow them in now, though I could see a few being allowed 'under the umbrella' in various domains in the past as the Camarilla did maintain that all vampires were of the Camarilla....depending on the local reps definition of the word 'vampire'.<br /> Anarchs....who knows? Each cell/group/clique has individual rules and regs so its concievable some would...also conceivable there are Anarch groups featuring Ananasi, Risen, Revenents, Sorcerers etc. Same goes for Cults.<br /> <br /> A Coterie/Wu/Family of Hungry Ghosts and Kindred would be.....difficult...but possible...though I think they would need to forego most of the spiritual component.....though a Vaulderie type ritual could work....spiritual patrons would be of the darker sort.<br /> <br /> Paths/Roads have been removed from V5 so though I believe a Kindred could use a Dharmic Path as a Road or Path with some herculean efforts in the past thats now irrelevant.<br /> <br /> I've never had a problem with the rules myself so I don't have an opinion one way or the other. Though I do find, and it may just be me, find V5s rules way harder to keep straight in my head than the older ones for KotE or other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:43:10-07:00","id":1396522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Allow them into the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Blood Cults.<br /> * Have them able to form coteries with Cainites.<br /> * Have them share their own Paths with Kindred<br /> * Simplify the rules for them.<br /> <br /> That way they can be a proper faction in V:TM.</div> </div> </div> </div>These is one of the most horrible suggestions I've seen for the Kuei-Jin on the short time I've been on this site. They don't NEED to be a cut down like this to be viable for VTM, they're their own splat. Why do they even need to be a faction in VTM when most of V5 is cutting down multiple factions so its only a Camarilla and Anarch slugfest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:47:52-07:00","id":1396524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396470#post1396470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it was the case of overcompensated for perceived player weaknesses. Kuei-Jin can only be made from ethnic Asian peoples and they can only be made in Asian territories because MAGIC [Wastonian].<br /> <br /> [Doyleist] They didn't want players making White American Ninja style characters from America and missing the point of the splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t wanna get off topic, but what does Wastonian and Doyleist mean? Like in game and out of game reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:51:06-07:00","id":1396526,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> I agree with you. I like the Wan Gui as a separate splat, distinct from but coexisting with Cainites in both Asian and (to a lesser extent) Western cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:56:22-07:00","id":1396533,"title":"","content":"I'm stilll working on this project; Real Life threw some wrench in the gears, but soon I will have something to show you...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> The hungry dead - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Strigoi: The hungry dead Why? I have wanted, for a long time, to create European creatures akin to the Wan Kuei. This is the first beta version. A summary: This </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:03:04-07:00","id":1396535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396522#post1396522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These is one of the most horrible suggestions I've seen for the Kuei-Jin on the short time I've been on this site. They don't NEED to be a cut down like this to be viable for VTM, they're their own splat. Why do they even need to be a faction in VTM when most of V5 is cutting down multiple factions so its only a Camarilla and Anarch slugfest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're distinctly and directly involved in Kindred politics?<br /> <br /> That's the way they were presented in Bloodlines and Revised.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:11:51-07:00","id":1396542,"title":"","content":"Apparently from what is being said in this thread per Justycar the whole Great Leap Outward has been softconned, so no, the Kuei-Jin have zilch to do with the bulk of Kindred politics. So that's really a stretch and not an adequate reason for the &quot;suggestions&quot; you've made for them. They have no reason to join the Camarilla, Anarchs, or Sabbat- and they <i>DEFINITELY</i> don't have no motivation to join a Blood Cult at all, that makes zero sense. They also don't need to share their Dharmas with Kindred because the specific purpose of their Dharma is to achieve the same state they had when they were the 10,000 immortals and redeem themselves in the August Personage of Jade- if he's still around of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:15:40-07:00","id":1396545,"title":"","content":"I think the Wan Gui can interact with and even join coteries with Cainites while still remaining a separate splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:35:23-07:00","id":1396555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396542#post1396542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently from what is being said in this thread per Justycar the whole Great Leap Outward has been softconned, so no, the Kuei-Jin have zilch to do with the bulk of Kindred politics. So that's really a stretch and not an adequate reason for the &quot;suggestions&quot; you've made for them. They have no reason to join the Camarilla, Anarchs, or Sabbat- and they <i>DEFINITELY</i> don't have no motivation to join a Blood Cult at all, that makes zero sense. They also don't need to share their Dharmas with Kindred because the specific purpose of their Dharma is to achieve the same state they had when they were the 10,000 immortals and redeem themselves in the August Personage of Jade- if he's still around of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what does any of this have to do with integrating the Kuei Jin into regular vampire games? You've said why they shouldn't. Now please come up with a reason why they would.<br /> <br /> Because it's what benefits the gamers that matters. What inhibits good gameplay experience is bad design. That's what matters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:12:51-07:00","id":1396562,"title":"","content":"That could be said for any other splat or crossover games with multiple splats at once Mr Watson, I don't know why you single out the Kuei-Jin for this. Also how does the Kuei-Jin inhibit gameplay by any margin? Also what do you mean by &quot;come up with a reason why they would&quot;, this doesn't make sense to me. The follow up with my response to you in the first place was that you said that the Kuei-Jin are the bulk of Kindred politics when that isn't the case at all, so I don't know what do you mean by &quot;what does any of this have to do with integrating the Kuei Jin into regular vampire games&quot; because they are their own splat now. If they are to be in any VTM game, proceed how you would with any crossover scenario.. beside that I still don't know you meant because like I explained before Kuei-Jin are zilch to do with Kindred politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:23:24-07:00","id":1396570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396562#post1396562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be said for any other splat or crossover games with multiple splats at once Mr Watson, I don't know why you single out the Kuei-Jin for this. Also how does the Kuei-Jin inhibit gameplay by any margin? Also what do you mean by &quot;come up with a reason why they would&quot;, this doesn't make sense to me. The follow up with my response to you in the first place was that you said that the Kuei-Jin are the bulk of Kindred politics when that isn't the case at all, so I don't know what do you mean by &quot;what does any of this have to do with integrating the Kuei Jin into regular vampire games&quot; because they are their own splat now. If they are to be in any VTM game, proceed how you would with any crossover scenario.. beside that I still don't know you meant because like I explained before Kuei-Jin are zilch to do with Kindred politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've said it like three times that the difference is the Kuei-Jin are part of the Kindred world in a way that other supernaturals aren't. They are a Vampire: The Masquerade group and need to be fully brought in. They weren't treated as their own splat but heavily involved in the metaplot of V:TM so they should be an option for V:TM players.<br /> <br /> And if your argument is, &quot;They shouldn't be in V:TM&quot; then that hits a brick wall because I'm discussing how to incorporate them. If you don't think, fine, that's the end of the conversation but I'm going to continue to talk about how to better integrate the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:52:26-07:00","id":1396574,"title":"","content":"They aren't a mere &quot;VTM&quot; group, they are their own &quot;Beast&quot; so to speak as of now. What you suggest to &quot;integrate&quot; them doesn't make sense at all. I would leave it from here, but you say the Kuei-Jin &quot;<i>need</i>&quot; some sort of convoluted &quot;fix&quot; so I feel it is right to say something. They don't &quot;need&quot; to be incorporated as if they didn't have any agency before or their own meta with their development as a separate line practically. You say they weren't treated as &quot;their own splat&quot; by have been since 1998(?), its standalone. Beside that even as Justycar has mentioned, the Great Leap Outward has supposedly been softconned, even in a book that involved your most beloved sect in Anarchs Unbound.<br /> <br /> Also what do you mean they are involved with VTM Kindred in a way no other splat has? That is decidedly false. The Kuei-Jin literally have more interactions with other supernaturals than the Kindred by their own standalone- the Kuei-Jin interact with the Fera, Wraiths, Hshien, and many others in their own jurisdiction. By that logic they should be merged with them more than the Kindred, lol. What you suggest wouldn't even &quot;improve&quot; them-<br /> <br /> * Allow them into the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Blood Cults. -(Wut? In what way do any of these make sense? Especially Blood Cults- the Kuei-Jin have nothing to do with the Antediluvians, Caine, or Methuselahs, who would they revere and what motivation would a Wan-Kuei join a Blood Cult anyway?)<br /> <br /> * Have them able to form coteries with Cainites. -(I have no gripe with this. I see no reason why some Kuei-Jin and Kindred could set aside their differences to for a common goal..)<br /> <br /> * Have them share their own Paths with Kindred. -(This doesn't make sense for a reason I already explained before. Also I thought you favored Touchstones over Paths to begin with, why would you even bring this up? Even then this would be stupid because the Sabbat basically have no work done into them all into V5 at all.)<br /> <br /> * Simplify the rules for them. -(Eh.. I'm 50/50 on this. Maybe a few touch ups can be good, but going overboard would destroy the splat.)<br /> <br /> Besides I thought Paradox didn't greenlight to work on other splats anyway? I doubt the Kuei-Jin and the many others will get much work soon. Y'know this makes me wonder if they will ever release a &quot;20th&quot; for KotE and Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-14-2020, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:59:00-07:00","id":1396575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396574#post1396574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't a mere &quot;VTM&quot; group, they are their own &quot;Beast&quot; so to speak as of now. What you suggest doesn't to &quot;integrate&quot; them doesn't make sense at all. I would leave it from here, but you say the Kuei-Jin &quot;<i>need</i>&quot; some sort of convoluted &quot;fix&quot; so I feel it is right to say something. They don't &quot;need&quot; to be incorporated as if they didn't have any agency before or their own meta with their development as a separate line practically. You say they weren't treated as &quot;their own splat&quot; by have been since 1998(?), its standalone. Beside that even as Justycar has mentioned, the Great Leap Outward has supposedly been softconned, even in a book that involved your most beloved sect in Anarchs Unbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all well and good but you're arguing a point I have no interest in arguing. The Kuei-Jin were introduced as the Kindred of the East, they were introduced at war with the Cainites, they were introduced as heavily involved in Kindred politics.<br /> <br /> They are finally introduced as the vampires of Asia. If you want to do Asian vampires, you need to deal with the Kuei-Jin. Either the Kuei-Jin have to be incorporated into the larger setting or they no longer can keep Kindred from involvement in Asia.<br /> <br /> It's ruining half the world for play in-canon otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to keep the Kuei-Jin their own splat with Cainites having their own society in Asia and existing in vast numbers. However, that's not what canon has established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:12:08-07:00","id":1396578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396574#post1396574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what do you mean they are involved with VTM Kindred in a way no other splat has? That is decidedly false. The Kuei-Jin literally have more interactions with other supernaturals than the Kindred by their own standalone- the Kuei-Jin interact with the Fera, Wraiths, Hshien, and many others in their own jurisdiction. By that logic they should be merged with them more than the Kindred, lol. What you suggest wouldn't even &quot;improve&quot; them-<br /> <br /> * Allow them into the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Blood Cults. -(Wut? In what way do any of these make sense? Especially Blood Cults- the Kuei-Jin have nothing to do with the Antediluvians, Caine, or Methuselahs, who would they revere and what motivation would a Wan-Kuei join a Blood Cult anyway?<br /> <br /> * Have them able to form coteries with Cainites. -I have no gripe with this. I see no reason why some Kuei-Jin and Kindred could set aside their differences to for a common goal..<br /> <br /> * Have them share their own Paths with Kindred. -This doesn't make sense for a reason I already explained before. Also I thought you favored Touchstones over Paths to begin with, why would you even bring this up? Even then this would be stupid because the Sabbat basically have no work done into them all into V5 at all.<br /> <br /> * Simplify the rules for them. -Eh.. I'm 50/50 on this. Maybe a few touch ups can be good, but going overboard would destroy the splat.<br /> <br /> Besides I thought Paradox didn't greenlight to work on other splats anyway? I doubt the Kuei-Jin and the many others will get much work soon. Y'know this makes me wonder if they will ever release a &quot;20th&quot; for KotE and Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed in regards to &quot;integrating them into VtM, however despite his posts consistently coming off as diminishing, dismissive and reductive I choose to believe CTPhipps when he says thats not his intention. Which is why I answered the way I did.<br /> <br /> Cam I absolutely agree 100%. Anarchs I'm flexible on as they should be grabbing allies whereever they can as they are so disparate that, barring writer fiat, they should be in a constant state of near dissolution. Blood Cults as they currently exist in V5 as Methusalah fan clubs or JW/Scientology knock offs I absolutely agree, but there can be other types.....looking back at DA the way Roads worked could be reinterpreted as a type of 'Blood' Cult.....and Dharmic paths could perhaps be interpreted through that lens....though that would need some work.<br /> <br /> Agreed on Paths....they no longer exist....so even if it were possible its irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Rules. I've said my piece.<br /> <br /> Paradox have killed all future 20th products, they will not be happening. And judging from the way they've treated M20, C20 and Wr20 and the later parts of W20s run they actively want them to go away. We will never see KotE5 or Mummy5.....well, not in the next decade or so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:18:53-07:00","id":1396580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396575#post1396575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all well and good but you're arguing a point I have no interest in arguing. The Kuei-Jin were introduced as the Kindred of the East, they were introduced at war with the Cainites, they were introduced as heavily involved in Kindred politics.<br /> <br /> They are finally introduced as the vampires of Asia. If you want to do Asian vampires, you need to deal with the Kuei-Jin. Either the Kuei-Jin have to be incorporated into the larger setting or they no longer can keep Kindred from involvement in Asia.<br /> <br /> It's ruining half the world for play in-canon otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to keep the Kuei-Jin their own splat with Cainites having their own society in Asia and existing in vast numbers. However, that's not what canon has established.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you keep saying this? THERE ARE CAINITES IN ASIA. There always have been. They are noted in dozens of different books in canon. The only parts of Asia that do not contain numerous Kindred are central mainland China because thats the seat of Quincunx power.<br /> <br /> You consistently argue against your own strawman interpretation which does not match canon at all, the Great Leap Outward, such as it was, was a tiny, tiny, tiny part of of the history of the region and only ever effected a small proportion of the Hungry Ghosts of the region. None of the Hungry Ghosts outside China ever gave toss about it, except as an opportunity to steal Quincunx territory while they were distracted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:19:21-07:00","id":1396581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all well and good but you're arguing a point I have no interest in arguing. The Kuei-Jin were introduced as the Kindred of the East, they were introduced at war with the Cainites, they were introduced as heavily involved in Kindred politics.<br /> <br /> They are finally introduced as the vampires of Asia. If you want to do Asian vampires, you need to deal with the Kuei-Jin. Either the Kuei-Jin have to be incorporated into the larger setting or they no longer can keep Kindred from involvement in Asia.<br /> <br /> It's ruining half the world for play in-canon otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to keep the Kuei-Jin their own splat with Cainites having their own society in Asia and existing in vast numbers. However, that's not what canon has established.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah because it wouldn't make sense. You also act as if their ISN'T any Kindred in Asia when you've already showed a different case with the bit you dug from Lasombra Revised. Also what you says makes no sense since its the same case for the Laibon- any western Kindred would have to deal with them if they wanted to do something in sub-Sahara africa (and the Setites in North Africa), so what makes it different for the Kindred at all? Same with Garou and rural areas/general wilderness. So will they now deal with the Laibon and Garou now just for those little things? Please. Its not &quot;ruining half the world&quot; for play, you could still decidedly go to Asia if the chronicle wishes to be taken that way irregardless. You already shown precedent that the Kuei-Jin don't thrash small groups of Kindred anyway with the Lasombra revised piece and even the opening of this thread shows that the Camarilla as through some nonsense has gotten some influence in Tokyo. Any involvement you want in VTM in Asia can be done, you act as if its impossible. If anything it'd be an interesting plot piece of interaction to try to convince the Kuei-Jin for your reasoning of visitation or trying to do the business one needs while avoiding their outright ire.<br /> <br /> It's just that retcon nuking the Kuei-Jin out of nowhere with no build up, no long-lasting war, or some wacky incorporation doesn't make a zilch of sense. The World of Darkness and most especially VTM should be kept compelling, not with all these nonsensical retcon nukes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-15-2020, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:21:23-07:00","id":1396582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396545#post1396545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Wan Gui can interact with and even join coteries with Cainites while still remaining a separate splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, though depending on consistency of the group 'coterie' may not be the best term. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:24:16-07:00","id":1396584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396578#post1396578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed in regards to &quot;integrating them into VtM, however despite his posts consistently coming off as diminishing, dismissive and reductive I choose to believe CTPhipps when he says thats not his intention. Which is why I answered the way I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>In simple terms, my opinion can best be summarized is the Kuei-Jin will be more popular and more used as members of V:TM than they'll ever be as their own splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396580#post1396580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you keep saying this? THERE ARE CAINITES IN ASIA. There always have been. They are noted in dozens of different books in canon. The only parts of Asia that do not contain numerous Kindred are central mainland China because thats the seat of Quincunx power.<br /> <br /> You consistently argue against your own strawman interpretation which does not match canon at all, the Great Leap Outward, such as it was, was a tiny, tiny, tiny part of of the history of the region and only ever effected a small proportion of the Hungry Ghosts of the region. None of the Hungry Ghosts outside China ever gave toss about it, except as an opportunity to steal Quincunx territory while they were distracted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but I literally argued that a few pages back. I even made a lengthy post about it from Clanbook Lasombra Revised.<br /> <br /> What do you think my argument IS?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396580#post1396580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you keep saying this? THERE ARE CAINITES IN ASIA. There always have been. They are noted in dozens of different books in canon. The only parts of Asia that do not contain numerous Kindred are central mainland China because thats the seat of Quincunx power.<br /> <br /> You consistently argue against your own strawman interpretation which does not match canon at all, the Great Leap Outward, such as it was, was a tiny, tiny, tiny part of of the history of the region and only ever effected a small proportion of the Hungry Ghosts of the region. None of the Hungry Ghosts outside China ever gave toss about it, except as an opportunity to steal Quincunx territory while they were distracted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, what do you think I'm advocating for?<br /> <br /> What do you think I HOPE happens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-14-2020, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:52:25-07:00","id":1396590,"title":"","content":"You literally just wrote that Cainites are locked out of and banned from half the planet and that this was a terrible thing that stopped people from playing them. I give up. I, and apparently many others, can't follow your thought process at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T20:00:20-07:00","id":1396593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396590#post1396590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You literally just wrote that Cainites are locked out of and banned from half the planet and that this was a terrible thing that stopped people from playing them. I give up. I, and apparently many others, can't follow your thought process at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was speaking hyberbole because while they're canonically there, the game is explicit that the Kuei-Jin destroy any and all they find. Which is, IMHO, silly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T20:48:30-07:00","id":1396598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396593#post1396593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I was speaking hyberbole because while they're canonically there, the game is explicit that the Kuei-Jin destroy any and all they find. Which is, IMHO, silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly can't tell what you're advocating for at this point. So you want the Hungry Ghosts to have been Kindred all along and use Kindred mechanics, becoming part of the Camarilla?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:17:59-07:00","id":1396604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396598#post1396598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly can't tell what you're advocating for at this point. So you want the Hungry Ghosts to have been Kindred all along and use Kindred mechanics, becoming part of the Camarilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>What I believe will happen</b>: I believe the Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei will be retconned out of the game and replaced with Cainites. I don't think that any of the people currently publishing the World of Darkness like them or want them in the game. I think they are conspicuous by their absence.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>What I would like them to do</b>: Remake the Wan Kuei to be a group of vampires that can be played in V5 that just so happens to have no relationship to Caine. They would then be able to participate in the setting as established. Adapt their abilities as best can be done to V:TM and have them as a playable faction that isn't portrayed as having Lupine levels of hatred for the undead but is accepted as &quot;vampires but different.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I think hurts the Kuei Jin was the &quot;All Asian cultures are the same&quot; lumping together of mythologies, the exoticizing of them, and making it so they couldn't be played or socialize with Western Kindred. The posters on this forum actually changed my views on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:58:27-07:00","id":1396609,"title":"","content":"1. They can certainly be played, where do you summoned the notion where they can't?<br /> <br /> 2. They can socialize with Western &quot;Kindred&quot; to some degree, why do you act as if they can't? The only thing is that China is mostly off limits because that is the main holding of the Kuei-Jin and even then any Kindred in China aren't KOS on the level of Sabbat and Camarilla sect fighting (before the Sabbat mattered pre-V5). You LITERALLY even showed direct evidence showing that a brood of Lasombra that have been &quot;active&quot; in China for centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a playable faction that isn't portrayed as having Lupine levels of hatred for the undead but is accepted as &quot;vampires but different.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this sentence even MEAN? The Kuei-Jin already ARE undead (what do you mean by this?) and they never had &quot;Garou&quot; levels of hatred for the western Kindred outright at all. Also now we wrangle back to what Chris24601 and Taggie laid out clearly: all the suggestions you make are for retcon nuking all the unique and glorious aspects of the classic World of Darkness for some inane reason. There is no reason for the Kuei-Jin to be Kindred at all. Also if they are going to be not related to Caine as you suggest, why not keep them as they are now with no change? Because that's practically what your levying up anyway. The ONLY Vampires I remember that are 100% not related to the whole Caine spiel were the Nagaraja and Botsam if I remember correctly.. Nagaraja was retnuked into the whole Hecata nonsense... and the Botsam? I'm pretty sure they are a gimmick splat that the current writers don't even remember what that is.<br /> <br /> There is no reason to adapt the Kuei-Jin for VTM at this point. The line even though it was INITIALLY and BRIEFLY a part of VTM (the really strange Gaki Lian had mentioned before.. *shivers*) it has diverged into its own thing and Paradox hasn't even greenlit the other splats to have any work done. Instead of even touching another splat as I said before, if anything something should be done to rectify or bring up the Sabbat- give us ANYTHING. V5 has been out relatively long but integral such aren't even out yet. Even you agree with me in that point- hell, there is NOTHING on the Tzimisce at all as of yet but then we got this Miyakui &quot;Old Clan&quot; such of all things in a Camarilla V5 book.. lmao.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-15-2020, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T22:42:12-07:00","id":1396616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396609#post1396609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. They can certainly be played, where do you summoned the notion where they can't?<br /> <br /> 2. They can socialize with Western &quot;Kindred&quot; to some degree, why do you act as if they can't? The only thing is that China is mostly off limits because that is the main holding of the Kuei-Jin and even then any Kindred in China aren't KOS on the level of Sabbat and Camarilla sect fighting (before the Sabbat mattered pre-V5). You LITERALLY even showed direct evidence showing that a brood of Lasombra that have been &quot;active&quot; in China for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a huge chunk of the Kuei Jin's backstory and incorporation into the metaplot is that they destroy any Cainites they find, consider them abominations, and went to war against them in the Great Leap Outward,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this sentence even MEAN? The Kuei-Jin already ARE undead (what do you mean by this?) </div> </div> </div>No shit, hence why they are something I'd like to incorporate into Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and they never had &quot;Garou&quot; levels of hatred for the western Kindred outright at all. Also now we wrangle back to what Chris24601 and Taggie laid out clearly: all the suggestions you make are for retcon nuking all the unique and glorious aspects of the classic World of Darkness for some inane reason. </div> </div> </div>You have some weird ideas given I want them to be preserved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no reason for the Kuei-Jin to be Kindred at all. </div> </div> </div>It's literally in the name: Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if they are going to be not related to Caine as you suggest, why not keep them as they are now with no change? </div> </div> </div>What change do you think I'm proposing other than they join into Western Kindred society as equals and vice versa?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because that's practically what your levying up anyway. The ONLY Vampires I remember that are 100% not related to the whole Caine spiel were the Nagaraja and Botsam if I remember correctly.. Nagaraja was retnuked into the whole Hecata nonsense... and the Botsam? I'm pretty sure they are a gimmick splat that the current writers don't even remember what that is. </div> </div> </div>Well there's the Drowned now, thankfully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no reason to adapt the Kuei-Jin for VTM at this point. The line even though it was INITIALLY and BRIEFLY a part of VTM (the really strange Gaki Lian had mentioned before.. *shivers*) it has diverged into its own thing and Paradox hasn't even greenlit the other splats to have any work done. Instead of even touching another splat as I said before, if anything something should be done to rectify or bring up the Sabbat- give us ANYTHING. V5 has been out relatively long but integral such aren't even out yet. Even you agree with me in that point- hell, there is NOTHING on the Tzimisce at all as of yet but then we got this Miyakui &quot;Old Clan&quot; such of all things in a Camarilla V5 book.. lmao. </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'll drop discussing the issue. You don't want the Kuei-Jin in the V:TM line and I'm not going to change your mind. Best to move on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"ht