arkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396704#post1396704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's been extremely patient with my excessive fanboyism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>and with my excessive nerd ragism<br /> <br /> Ventrue elder grade patience, for sure<br /> but he's a setite fan...go figure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T12:07:56-07:00","id":1396710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396708#post1396708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and with my excessive nerd ragism<br /> <br /> Ventrue elder grade patience, for sure<br /> but he's a setite fan...go figure</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend his RPGing of Dolph Sheng in Red Moon Roleplaying's The Sacrifice for how to make a terrifying vampire while not being overtly &quot;ho ho ho&quot; evil. Good non-traditional Setite. I wouldn't mind seeing Dolph get a write-up in a future supplement.<br /> <br /> Assuming he's not Blood Hunted in a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T01:20:53-07:00","id":1396832,"title":"","content":"To get back to the original post:<br /> <br /> 0. This is for the sake of the conversation my speculation based on <b>what I believe will happen</b>, <b>what I have observed in the text</b>, and <b>what deductions can be made</b>. There's no house ruling or going off the rails here, it's just fan speculation from what we all have a copy of.<br /> <br /> 1. I think it's implied that the Camarilla has been in control of Tokyo for centuries. I predict it to be a Mithras style situation where the local Cainites have joined the Camarilla [perhaps some unwillingly] with a previous system in place that was run by Japanese vampires. Basically, the Japanese system has probably been in place for centuries but they became part of the Camarilla after Admiral Perry's arrival, possibly after the Mejii Restoration.<br /> <br /> 2. The implication that vampires over the age of 300 must leave Tokyo and go to Kyoto implies that Tokyo is a city that's going to avoid the gerontocracy problems of many other locations. It's still probably dominated by Elders but these Elders are under 300 years old rather than ancients like Tyler, Khalid, and Critias. Kyoto I'm imagining to be full of ancient Old as DirtTM vampires who are scheming against one another and controlling events on a national scale. Notably, no sign of the Beckoning.<br /> <br /> Or IS IT the Beckoning and the ancients summoning them just happen to live in Kyoto versus the Middle East? Maybe all the 300 year old Elders are food for the 1000+ year old Elders in Kyoto.<br /> <br /> 3. The presence of the <b>Old Clan Tzimisce</b> here is a breath of fresh air because it implies that the Old Clan has been in Japan for apparently a pretty long time. I'm inclined to think it's a local branch of the Clan and not something that came anytime soon. She's under 300 years old by the rules of the system but could easily be someone Embraced by a <i>daimyo</i> of the Warring States Period or the Tokugawa Shogunate. There's a potential vast history for local land-owning feudal lords in Japan that are perfect for the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 4. The use of the term &quot;Old Clan&quot; implies to me that the &quot;soft retcon&quot; that the Old Clan Tzimisce were all but nonexistent is gone. For a time, the Old Clan Tzimisce were a bunch of lunatic eccentrics due to their disdain for Vicissitude (as its established the Eldest and most of the Methuselahs use it). The fact the Old Clan is both a Camarilla member here and distinguished as one means I think we'll see the Old Clan Tzimisce play a much bigger role in the setting come V:TM V5. If the Old Clan Tzimisce could become a dominant or THE DOMINANT branch of the Tzimisce, I would be ecstatic.<br /> <br /> 5. A single Nosferatu is able to resist the summoning to Kyoto. I wonder what his story is.<br /> <br /> 6. The lack of the Hunger may be a massive <b>Blood Sorcery</b> ritual like the one in THE FALL OF LONDON where a Nosferatu wizard used the London Underground (which is not a political movement-A Fish called Wanda) to feed from the Cainites there. Maybe Blood Sorcerers in japan made it so that all of the citizens of Tokyo are being fed on to feed the Cainites of the city without feeding. It might explain the constant fatigue and overwork of Japan's salaryman class as they're all just being sucked JUST A LITTLE dry at all times by cainites.<br /> <br /> &quot;The world is a vampire NA NA NA.&quot; Or at least Tokyo as a whole is.<br /> <br /> It could also be the use of Dragon Lines and an homage to the Wan Kuei that fed on Ki energy. Maybe the Kindred here have found a way to feed on something other than blood. It could potentially give Kindred reasons to hunt and kill Lupines for their caerns or mages for their nodes.<br /> <br /> 7. Who or what is <b>Skinriding</b> the majority of Kindred in Tokyo? What is their relationship? I think it's unlikely all of the Kindred are possessed-possessed but it could be that there's a &quot;special&quot; relationship between the <b>Wraiths</b> of Tokyo and the vampires. The <b>Hecata</b> could have a presence here with the Harbingers or Cappadocians having taken refuge here or been beyond the Giovanni's power during the Great Purge.<br /> <br /> If I were to speculate, I could easily see the Kindred making a pact with ghosts to allow them into their bodies in order to help control the Hunger in exchange for allowing them to vicariously experience the joys of undeath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2020, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:57:15-07:00","id":1396894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396832#post1396832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. The use of the term &quot;Old Clan&quot; implies to me that the &quot;soft retcon&quot; that the Old Clan Tzimisce were all but nonexistent is gone. For a time, the Old Clan Tzimisce were a bunch of lunatic eccentrics due to their disdain for Vicissitude (as its established the Eldest and most of the Methuselahs use it). The fact the Old Clan is both a Camarilla member here and distinguished as one means I think we'll see the Old Clan Tzimisce play a much bigger role in the setting come V:TM V5. If the Old Clan Tzimisce could become a dominant or THE DOMINANT branch of the Tzimisce, I would be ecstatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm expecting the <b>mechanical</b> difference between the Old Clan and the Fiends to be gone. Some Elders learn Vicissitude, others abhor it, but mechanically they're a single clan with a single discipline spread and a single clan bane. And the childe of a Vicissitude-user could declare &quot;no I'm not gonna use Vicissitude it's weird and creepy&quot;, or vice versa: it's a personal decision, not determined by the Blood.<br /> <br /> I'm also expecting &quot;The Old Clan&quot; to be a polite term for the Tzimisce (like how their Antediluvian is &quot;the Eldest&quot;) among the Camarilla, because it's socially acceptable to call the Sabbat Tzimisce &quot;Fiends&quot;, but much less acceptable to call your Prince that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T10:00:28-07:00","id":1396895,"title":"","content":"I dunno because they're called the Old Clan because the Sabbat Tzimisce are the &quot;New Clan.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:50:13-07:00","id":1396907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396832#post1396832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. The lack of the Hunger may be a massive <b>Blood Sorcery</b> ritual like the one in THE FALL OF LONDON where a Nosferatu wizard used the London Underground (which is not a political movement-A Fish called Wanda) to feed from the Cainites there. Maybe Blood Sorcerers in japan made it so that all of the citizens of Tokyo are being fed on to feed the Cainites of the city without feeding. It might explain the constant fatigue and overwork of Japan's salaryman class as they're all just being sucked JUST A LITTLE dry at all times by cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>so, a blood sorcery ritual that solves world hunger...in a game about hunger...<br /> <br /> see, that's one of the things I like about KotE,<br /> none of that big blood sorcery deus ex machina that WW devs love so much...though they still had their vinculum<br /> <br /> vinculum was such a mess,<br /> v5 was supposed to fix previous messy blood rituals before making up messy new ones<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> end of rant I guess<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:20:41-07:00","id":1396916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396895#post1396895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno because they're called the Old Clan because the Sabbat Tzimisce are the &amp;quot;New Clan.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't see what the Old Clan do that the Ventrue and Lasombra don't already cover","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:31:47-07:00","id":1396917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396907#post1396907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so, a blood sorcery ritual that solves world hunger...in a game about hunger...<br /> <br /> see, that's one of the things I like about KotE,<br /> none of that big blood sorcery deus ex machina that WW devs love so much...though they still had their vinculum<br /> <br /> vinculum was such a mess,<br /> v5 was supposed to fix previous messy blood rituals before making up messy new ones<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> end of rant I guess</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Web of Hunger</i> in <i>The Fall of London</i> allows the user to gradually remotely feed on everybody in a given area. Consequently, it makes every other vampire who passes through hungrier. CTPhipps suggestion is a more civic minded version of that, so far as kindred are concerned, but so far we know, it doesn't exist in the books.<br /> <br /> Lille Haake, who describes Tokyo in <i>Camarilla</i>, says that her hunger was &quot;subdued&quot; and it came back when she went into a pachinko parlour. Whatever it is, it's not <i>sating</i> hungerand the local Tremere didn't have an explanation for her either. I think it could be some of mass variation of <i>Quell the Beast</i><i>, </i>although that would rather potent and Haake describes her time in the city as &quot;intense&quot; and mentions a &quot;cold heat&quot; rather than lethargy. Of course, it isn't necessarily caused by vampires of any description, although there could kindred who think that keeping their hunger off the streets is in their best interests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396916#post1396916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't see what the Old Clan do that the Ventrue and Lasombra don't already cover</div> </div> </div> </div>They do seem to be as much by their sect alignment i.e. none or the True Black Hand, as their culture or innate traits. I think of them as having more of a folk horror or medieval aesthetic in spite modern norms, but Mayumi Shibasaki sounds much like the standard corporate Ventrue so far. She's even the subject of the Fortitude story example in the V5 corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-16-2020, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:04:43-07:00","id":1396925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396916#post1396916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't see what the Old Clan do that the Ventrue and Lasombra don't already cover</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Taggie it may be one of those things where we're just coming at it from such different angles that we're never going to be able to reconcile. In my case, I love the Old Clan Tzimisce more than I ever love the Lasombra or Ventrue while feeling &quot;ehh&quot; for the mainstream clan that I feel like gets dominated by Vicissitude Flesh Monkeys a bit too much (i.e. people who only care about the Discipline vs. the actual Clan Culture).<br /> <br /> But for me, the Old Clan Tzimisce bring to the table a much grander focus on the feudal lord element than either and make their own. Ventrue characters have all since gone onto be merchants, CEOs, and businessman that are obsessed with accumulating power. They are people who are snobby elites that have a flaw and Disciplines that reflects their removal from the common people as well as power to manipulate. The Lasombra, by contrast, have powers related to the Stygian darkness and controlling people while also being people who represent manipulators that control people through religious devotion (be it church or Sabbat).<br /> <br /> The (Old Clan) Tzimisce, by contrast, are a beautiful encapsulation of &quot;The Lord is the Land and the Land is the Lord.&quot; Their Disciplines give them the ability to control the animals, survey their territory, and impress their will upon the peasantry in a way that makes them the absolute masters of their domains. It is a much more intense relationship to Domain than either the Ventrue or Lasombra have because they can just pack up and leave anytime they want. Tzimisce, by contrast, ARE defined by their love of the land and soil that it might as well be their own flesh.<br /> <br /> Their attitudes towards honor are also completely different. The Ventrue have completely abandoned honor in the 21st century, now defined by slimy weasals like La Croix, Lodin, and Hardestadt (who is a fallen Jurgen as far as I'm concerned). Even Jan Pieterszoon doens't care about the letter OR spirit of his agreements. The Lasombra are a clan of liars and manipulators worse than anyone save maybe the Followers of Set (and I argue they're at least honest among themselves).<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimisce by contrast are people for which the bond of your word, domain, and personal honor are absolute. They may be alien inhuman monsters with Roads dating back to Pre-Christian times but they take this shit seriously. You can expect them to heroically fight off a bunch of your enemies as long as you're their guest but may flay your skin off slowly for a 1000 years if you insult their ghoul dogs.<br /> <br /> A lot of the Old Clan Tzimisce carry a sense of antiquity, responsibility, and power that being a vampire lord should. If you're a fan of Strahd, Dracula, or Carmilla then they are the vampires for you. It's also kind of cool that it's a dying clan like the Salubri as the modern world leaves them behind. They cannot change because their clan is all about the Good Old WaysTM and slavish devotion to ancient tradition but that doesn't make it wrong. They also have all the cool stuff of the mainstream Tzimisce clan like the Revenant families, just without the gross monsters and even then they still have hellhounds and probably summoned Koldunic monsters.<br /> <br /> ====<br /> <br /> \u201cWe Szekelys have a right to be proud, for in our veins flows the blood of many brave races who fought as the lion fights, for lordship. Here, in the whirlpool of European races, the Ugric tribe bore down from Iceland the fighting spirit which Thor and Wodin gave them, which their Berserkers displayed to such fell intent on the seaboards of Europe, ay, and of Asia and Africa too, till the peoples thought that the were-wolves themselves had come. Here, too, when they came, they found the Huns, whose warlike fury had swept the earth like a living flame, till the dying peoples held that in their veins ran the blood of those old witches, who, expelled from Scythia had mated with the devils in the desert. Fools, fools! What devil or what witch was ever so great as Attila, whose blood is in these veins?\u201d He held up his arms. \u201cIs it a wonder that we were a conquering race; that we were proud; that when the Magyar, the Lombard, the Avar, the Bulgar, or the Turk poured his thousands on our frontiers, we drove them back? Is it strange that when Arpad and his legions swept through the Hungarian fatherland he found us here when he reached the frontier; that the Honfoglalas was completed there? And when the Hungarian flood swept eastward, the Szekelys were claimed as kindred by the victorious Magyars, and to us for centuries was trusted the guarding of the frontier of Turkey-land; ay, and more than that, endless duty of the frontier guard, for, as the Turks say, \u2018water sleeps, and enemy is sleepless.\u2019 Who more gladly than we throughout the Four Nations received the \u2018bloody sword,\u2019 or at its warlike call flocked quicker to the standard of the King? When was redeemed that great shame of my nation, the shame of Cassova, when the flags of the Wallach and the Magyar went down beneath the Crescent? Who was it but one of my own race who as Voivode crossed the Danube and beat the Turk on his own ground? This was a Dracula indeed!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2020, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:06:51-07:00","id":1396926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396917#post1396917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Web of Hunger</i> in <i>The Fall of London</i> allows the user to gradually remotely feed on everybody in a given area. Consequently, it makes every other vampire who passes through hungrier. CTPhipps suggestion is a more civic minded version of that, so far as kindred are concerned, but so far we know, it doesn't exist in the books.<br /> <br /> Lille Haake, who describes Tokyo in <i>Camarilla</i>, says that her hunger was &quot;subdued&quot; and it came back when she went into a pachinko parlour. Whatever it is, it's not <i>sating</i> hungerand the local Tremere didn't have an explanation for her either. I think it could be some of mass variation of <i>Quell the Beast</i><i>, </i>although that would rather potent and Haake describes her time in the city as &quot;intense&quot; and mentions a &quot;cold heat&quot; rather than lethargy. Of course, it isn't necessarily caused by vampires of any description, although there could kindred who think that keeping their hunger off the streets is in their best interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice catch, I completely missed that. The Hunger doesn't work in the streets but it happens once you enter a building. I think this means that the &quot;Hunger Suppression&quot; effect is directly related to trying to protect the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If you frenzy in Tokyo's crowded streets, you're fucked and everyone is fucked.<br /> <br /> However, in a nearby building, it's not going to be seen by literally hundreds of people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:31:11-07:00","id":1396931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1396926#post1396926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice catch, I completely missed that. The Hunger doesn't work in the streets but it happens once you enter a building. I think this means that the &quot;Hunger Suppression&quot; effect is directly related to trying to protect the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If you frenzy in Tokyo's crowded streets, you're fucked and everyone is fucked.<br /> <br /> However, in a nearby building, it's not going to be seen by literally hundreds of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>pff, if that's the case, I'll maintain my theory that it's the Weaver doing it,<br /> and that it stops in pachinko parlors because pachinko machines are of the wyrm &lt;.&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:25:29-07:00","id":1396942,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamec