n Resources Tzimisce Archetypes would be:<br /> <br /> * <b>Groundskeeper</b>: You are the lord and master of a nature preserve, city park, or other location that you consider your territory and lord.<br /> <br /> * <b>Brutal Vigilante</b>: You stab people, break fingers, and crack skulls to intimidate the people who threaten &quot;your&quot; neighborhood.<br /> <br /> * <b>Houndmaster</b>: All the strays in the land are your subjects and obey you as well as carr out your will.<br /> <br /> * <b>Rat King</b>: More or less the Houndmaster but the subject of the rats.<br /> <br /> * <b>City Shaman</b>: You listen to the spirits of the city and master them as both their defender and master.<br /> <br /> * <b>Street Knight</b>: You are the warrior of the people who lives like Ghost Dog. Following a code that no longer applies of ancient chivalry, bushido, or other values.<br /> <br /> * <b>Impoverished Patrician</b>: Your blood is blue or at least you believe it is. You have no wealth, though, and rely on Dominate and your fellow Kindred to mooch off of.<br /> <br /> * <b>Miss Havisham</b>: You squat in a decaying building, surrounding yourselves with junk and ghouled slaves. You are half-insane and the other half agrees.<br /> <br /> They're a bit similar to the Gangrel but I always preferred my Tzimisce having the best qualities of them as well as the Ventrue's Dark Age Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-