around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T04:54:34-07:00","id":1397060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397057#post1397057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well why wouldn't they have it?<br /> <br /> They don't have Vicissitude, they have Koldunism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it was tainted as well? (I loose track of whether it's infernalism in disguise anymore)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:03:18-07:00","id":1397061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397057#post1397057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well why wouldn't they have it?<br /> <br /> They don't have Vicissitude, they have Koldunism.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait, then why were we arguing all this time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397058#post1397058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that sounds like a case of Ventrue encroaching on Tzimisce rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair point,<br /> I don't know which one had them first, but the Ventrue had ghoul families in the modern nights,<br /> and they inherited the Grimaldi from the sabbat<br /> <br /> anyway, I wasn't arguing the tzimisce were encorching on Ventrue territory,<br /> I was arguing that there's nothing distinguishing the tzimisce from the ventrue in v5<br /> <br /> since their signature disciplines (their only real distinction) are being retconned,<br /> and because the ventrue are inheriting stuff from the tzimisce and the sabbat in general (revenants, cults, paths etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:12:07-07:00","id":1397062,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue having ghoul families seems weird because the Ghoul Families are unnatural abominations created by sorcery and experimentation.<br /> <br /> They don't have the scientific/thaumaturgy know-how to pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397060#post1397060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it was tainted as well? (I loose track of whether it's infernalism in disguise anymore)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Old Clan Tzimisce aren't NICE people by any stretch of the imagination. They're a bunch of twisted evil psychopaths and inhuman monsters. They just believe Vicissitude possesses you.<br /> <br /> And ironically, they're RIGHT in Revised. It's just not Souleaters but the Eldest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyway, I wasn't arguing the tzimisce were encorching on Ventrue territory, I was arguing that there's nothing distinguishing the tzimisce from the ventrue in v5</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we don't know what the Tzimisce will be like but I find this to be ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> since their signature disciplines (their only real distinction) are being retconned </div> </div> </div>I think this is ridiculous. Vicissitude was nifty but in what world was this the most distinguishing element. The Tzimisce's culture, traditions, and personalities are some of the best defined in all of V:TM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and because the ventrue are inheriting stuff from the tzimisce and the sabbat in general (revenants, cults, paths etc) </div> </div> </div>When have the Ventrue gotten Revenant families?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-17-2020, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:18:37-07:00","id":1397064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397062#post1397062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ventrue having ghoul families seems weird because the Ghoul Families are unnatural abominations created by sorcery and experimentation.<br /> <br /> They don't have the scientific/thaumaturgy know-how to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>pretty sure they do,<br /> <br /> the Grimaldi defection was helped by a ventrue ghoul family,<br /> the mexico brench of the grimaldi would joing that ghoul family in...Texas I think? I don't remember correctly<br /> <br /> well, even if I'm remembering wrongly, they have the Grimaldi now,<br /> if they didn't have revenants before, they have them now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:43:29-07:00","id":1397067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397064#post1397064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pretty sure they do,<br /> <br /> the Grimaldi defection was helped by a ventrue ghoul family,<br /> the mexico brench of the grimaldi would joing that ghoul family in...Texas I think? I don't remember correctly<br /> <br /> well, even if I'm remembering wrongly, they have the Grimaldi now,<br /> if they didn't have revenants before, they have them now</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, that makes sense. Defecting ghoul families are a different kettle of fish.<br /> <br /> When did this happen? I literally thought I knew almost everything in the Modern Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:48:19-07:00","id":1397068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397067#post1397067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, well, that makes sense. Defecting ghoul families are a different kettle of fish.<br /> <br /> When did this happen? I literally thought I knew almost everything in the Modern Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>it happened in revised, it was one of the set ups for the 4th sabbat civil war in Mexico by Night<br /> <br /> I don't know if they kept it for BJD and V5,<br /> they retconned alot of revised, so they might have retconned that too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:23:57-07:00","id":1397077,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons that revenant families exist is to do Ventrue work for Tzimisce who can focus on less worldly, temporal and anthropocentric pursuits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:30:53-07:00","id":1397079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397048#post1397048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Koldunism is something I supported as having a bigger role in the Clan with Vicissitude transformations being made into Rituals for it. This was an unpopular idea, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently had thoughts about this, and I am a bit frustrated by bad (faith?) arguments that Tzimisce without flesh-warping don't have a niche to fill that isn't covered by other clans like the Ventrue, so I am going to pipe in here a bit. I have to leave for work soon, so I may not get all my ideas written out right away. Also, I am not especially familiar with V5, mostly just following discussions as they pertain to things that interest me, like the Tzimisce, and to get ideas for metaplot progression that I may or may not want to incorporate into my V20 games.<br /> <br /> As CTPhipps has noted before, the Tzimisce, between their in-clan Disciplines, clan flaw, and clan culture, are uniquely set up to represent the &quot;lord of the land&quot; archetype in ways that other &quot;High&quot; clans like the Ventrue or Lasombra just aren't. They aren't just the masters of the mortal herd, they are the masters of the beasts (Animalism) and the secrets of their domain (Auspex). Having the shamanic blood magic of Koldunism as a tradition of the clan further reinforces this. Yes, you can have other clans imitate this by taking on the appropriate Disciplines and behaviours, but you could turn that argument around on the culture and Disciplines of any other clan; who needs the Ventrue when anyone can learn mind-influencing Disciplines and focus their attention on controlling mortal society?<br /> <br /> I think that CTPhipps is right that the Tzimisce are uniquely set up to serve as the archetypical &quot;Dracula&quot; clan. I disagree that this is necessarily the best use for them, because I fell in love with the Tzimisce more for their dark mystical side, their pursuit of perfection and transcending the flaws of the Curse of Caine (I came to the Tzimisce by way of the Ordo Dracul in VtR). But one of the things that I think is awesome about the Tzimisce is how they manage to fit so many archetypes under one cultural tent so well; the dark shaman, the lord of the land, the creep-show.<br /> <br /> P.S. I don't see the Dominate/Old Clan Tzimisce as the &quot;original/natural&quot; state from which the rest of the clan &quot;degenerated.&quot; I see them more as akin to a separate &quot;caste&quot; of the clan, like the Banu Haqim, who chose to specialize in lordship over self-transformation. I think Dracula not being a canon member of the Old Clan, given the utter lack of fleshwarping in his pre-VtM mythos AFAIK, is due to their status as the paranoid fruit bats of the clan; doesn't really fit his mystique if he's seen mostly as a weird kook.<br /> <br /> As for Vicissitude...<br /> <br /> As someone who loves the Tzimisce as monsters who embrace being monsters, and want to become *better* monsters, I love Vicissitude. I love the Path of Metamorphosis. A lot of what is done with Vicissitude works; self-improvement, or improving ghouls (as extensions of the self).<br /> <br /> But a lot of it seems to lose sight of that cool mystical, transcendent, focus, in favour of cheap gory thrills. I get turning people into chairs as a scare tactic, and as a way for new Metamorphosists to practice fleshwarping skills. But when one example of a serious Metamorphosist is just obsessed with turning kids into furniture, I'm left wondering if they have lost track of the Big Picture, the Point.<br /> <br /> Which leads us to the Mother of All Flesh-Chairs: the Cathedral of Flesh.<br /> <br /> What was The Point of the Cathedral of Flesh, from a Metamorphosist point of view? I'm not saying there isn't one, I can imagine several. But most depictions of it seem to focus on it as this feat of monstrous fleshwarping, a source of horror, rather than a means of transcending the vampiric condition. Vicissitude/fleshwarping should just be a means, not the end unto itself.<br /> <br /> Regarding Vicissitude in V5, I had an idea for how to keep fleshwarping and Metamorphosis as a significant aspect of all Tzimisce while not having to replace any other part of their Discipline spread:<br /> <br /> &quot;Self-Modification&quot; Vicissitude could be a subset of Protean powers. Vicissitude that affects others, however, would require an Amalgam with Blood Sorcery. Blood Sorcery would not be an in-clan Discipline, but a common subculture within the clan (fitting previous portrayals of Koldunism).<br /> <br /> I do agree that having Blood Sorcery replace Quietus for all Banu Haqim is a bad move for V5. But I prefer retconning the bad decision, by making that just the Sorcerer caste, over making the same mistake with the Tzimisce by removing one of their current Disciplines; all of them are too good to lose! Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  I think I'm finished editing... 06-17-2020, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:03:02-07:00","id":1397091,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> it is not a bad faith argument, I genuinely do not see anything that the Old Clan offers that Ventrue and Lasombra don't do better. On the Cathedral of Flesh: it was the womb of the Eldest, it's rebirth was coming. Also Kuapula had something to do with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:19:20-07:00","id":1397094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397068#post1397068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it happened in revised, it was one of the set ups for the 4th sabbat civil war in Mexico by Night<br /> <br /> I don't know if they kept it for BJD and V5,<br /> they retconned alot of revised, so they might have retconned that too</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure it is the Grimaldi? I may also be missing something but I hadn't seen them defecting. They are one of the younger of the revenant families and do serve as the main intermediaries between the vampires/other revenant families and the humans, since they are the newest of them and have stronger ties to the mortal world. The wiki entry does mention they are scared of the Sabbat and their inhuman ways, and may be looking for a way to defect, but I hadn't seen anything else expanding upon that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397079#post1397079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regarding Vicissitude in V5, I had an idea for how to keep fleshwarping and Metamorphosis as a significant aspect of all Tzimisce while not having to replace any other part of their Discipline spread:</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Self-Modification&quot; Vicissitude could be a subset of Protean powers. Vicissitude that affects others, however, would require an Amalgam with Blood Sorcery. Blood Sorcery would not be an in-clan Discipline, but a common subculture within the clan (fitting previous portrayals of Koldunism).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do agree that having Blood Sorcery replace Quietus for all Banu Haqim is a bad move for V5. But I prefer retconning the bad decision, by making that just the Sorcerer caste, over making the same mistake with the Tzimisce by removing one of their current Disciplines; all of them are too good to lose! Lol</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can agree that the &quot;self modification&quot; powers would be a subset of Protean. I would posit that most any discipline could have some access to a variation on rituals. With Protean, you could then take your personal flesh crafting powers and apply them to someone else over a long, sustained &quot;surgery&quot;/ritual. In this way, the &quot;dot&quot; powers are the immediate/passive abilities and the rituals are the more convoluted/involved powers, there by also allowing for more powers than just the standard 5. I could see something where Dominate/Auspex would be adjusted to have a ritual that would allow for possession of a mortal through out the day.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:39:45-07:00","id":1397096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SarcasticJazzHands</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397094#post1397094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure it is the Grimaldi? I may also be missing something but I hadn't seen them defecting. They are one of the younger of the revenant families and do serve as the main intermediaries between the vampires/other revenant families and the humans, since they are the newest of them and have stronger ties to the mortal world. The wiki entry does mention they are scared of the Sabbat and their inhuman ways, and may be looking for a way to defect, but I hadn't seen anything else expanding upon that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yes, it was in the Mexico city by night scenario if memory serves me right<br /> <br /> the head of the grimaldi in mexico city was supposed to talk about business with the regent, and was thus one of the first to realize the regent was a fake and the real one might be dead,<br /> he prepared for the grimaldi to sell sabbat property (alot of which was on grimaldi name) and defect to the cam in exchange for service before shit hit the fan<br /> <br /> not all of them could defect, as some of them were blood bond to the sabbat and would have to be left behind<br /> <br /> it was a set up for triggering conflict in the sect, and also to give more space to sabbat characters that prefered to handle mortal affairs themselves instead of relying on the grimaldi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:12:30-07:00","id":1397102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397091#post1397091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> it is not a bad faith argument, I genuinely do not see anything that the Old Clan offers that Ventrue and Lasombra don't do better. On the Cathedral of Flesh: it was the womb of the Eldest, it's rebirth was coming. Also Kuapula had something to do with it</div> </div> </div> </div>You've said this multiple times. Could you explain why a Ventrue or Lasombra does a inhuman feudal lord better than the Tzimisce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:24:43-07:00","id":1397106,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll agree that \u201cOld Lord\u201d is really not distinct enough an area to make Tzmisce distinctive from the other \u2018lord\u2019 clans like Ventru or Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Conversely, Vampire Transcendentalist IS something unique and, if you\u2019re bound and determined to change things around, then making the distinction between the actual transcendentalist of the Old Clan whose use of disciplines is to personally transcend their current state vs. the degenerates in the Sabbat who\u2019ve lost sight of the ends (Vicissitude as a tool for transcendence) for the means (i.e. Vicissitude for its own sake).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:26:54-07:00","id":1397107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397102#post1397102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've said this multiple times. Could you explain why a Ventrue or Lasombra does a inhuman feudal lord better than the Tzimisce?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sure. The Ventrue have it fairly easy, they use of Dominate and Presence to create Renfeld type servants, cause terror and awe, use mental abuse on opponents etc, the mob running in supernatural terror, the brain washed thralls, the compulsion to go investigate the dark castle etc. The Lasombra can also do the Dominate addled weird village thing, as well as the brain washed servants etc, but hits harder on the esoteric themes with Obtenerbration/Oblivion, and is more physically powerful due to potence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-17-2020, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:34:07-07:00","id":1397108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397107#post1397107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. The Ventrue have it fairly easy, they use of Dominate and Presence to create Renfeld type servants, cause terror and awe, use mental abuse on opponents etc, the mob running in supernatural terror, the brain washed thralls, the compulsion to go investigate the dark castle etc. The Lasombra can also do the Dominate addled weird village thing, as well as the brain washed servants etc, but hits harder on the esoteric themes with Obtenerbration/Oblivion, and is more physically powerful due to potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just speaking in terms of pure mechanics, the discipline I see representing the Tzimisce's unique control over their servants is Animalism rather than Vicissitude. Dominate can rewrite memories or turn someone into a mindless shell, and Presence can induce infatuation, but Animalism functions on the level of base instincts and emotions, removing, altering, and rewriting them freely\u2014and I think it's no coincidence that it was the Animalism-users who created the first revenant families, not the Presence-users.<br /> <br /> Now, they're definitely not creating szlachta and vozhd without Vicissitude, but in terms of &quot;how do they differ from the Ventrue?&quot; I think Animalism versus Presence is the more relevant point of comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T10:06:55-07:00","id":1397109,"title":"","content":"animalism is not strong enough<br /> <br /> with koldunism/vicissitude, tzimisce make for decent feudal lords,<br /> koldunism suffers a bit in the modern age however as there are no techno shamans among koldun (even though Tremere got technomancy...figures)<br /> <br /> in v5, vicissitude is gonna turn into protean,<br /> koldunism is either gonna be turned into blood sorcery or nerfed, otherwise it would be too strong compared to other disciplines<br /> <br /> so, ventrue with presence + dominate wins","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T11:14:21-07:00","id":1397115,"title":"","content":"Ah.. so we're back to this conversation with the Tzismisce.. If that's the case I'll go back on the original tangent I had whenever this is brought up: Tzimisce without Vicissitude aren't the Tzimisce anymore. Leave the Koldunism for the Old Clan- that's what their for, the niche portion of the Tzimisce who don't use Vicissitude. However the entirety of the Tzimisce are literally shaped by Vicissitude (no pun intended) and pre-V5 (because we don't even know the status of Paths) had entire Vampiric philosophy cascading around it- for thousands of years at this point. They aren't going to just *abandon* it (with V5 nonsensical events and softcons though, you'll be definite they will find a way for this to happen) out of nowhere for no REASON whatsoever at all.<br /> <br /> Sure a nil portion of Tzimisce are steeped in magic, but for the most part I've always seen them as inhuman biologists and sadistic warpers of flesh&amp;bone. Why would they need all these magical niches for? Especially when we consider the fact that they are probably going to do an asspull where somehow the Tzimisce aren't even the Sabbat and get shoved into the Camarilla (and to the Gods, please let this only be theoretical), what BASIS is them to be a keyed-in &quot;magic&quot; clan when that point was LITERALLY the Tremere, which is now stolen by the Assamites who- just as you guessed- has been totally assed into the Camarilla with no sense. There doesn't NEED to be three magical clans in one Sect all at once. Beside that I sincerely doubt them ever going to the Anarchs (they wouldn't go that far.. right?) so that's out the window.<br /> <br /> This is all assuming that they're going 100% in the way of clobbering down the Sabbat into dust (which is idiotic because they are Sect that IS and WAS the best foil for the Camarilla than the Anarchs by any decided margin possible). The shift back to &quot;Camarilla vs Anarchs&quot; again has been the biggest devolution so far. The reason why I even mention the Sabbat is because you CAN'T have the Tzimisce without this sect- which makes sense to why they have been ungracefully not been around all V5 along with their premiere sect, with no stats, updates since V20/Revised, NOTHING. Its the reason why this topic has been derailed to &quot;Old Clan&quot; Tzimisce at all because this write-up in the Camarilla book for whatever reason has gone to mention this bloodline of the Tzimisce, when we have NOTHING on the main branch for this long.<br /> <br /> The reason why Old Clan is even mentioned for whatever reason (and in JAPAN of all places?) even when we have zilch on the main fan favorite one, because the writing is on the wall- they want to systemically remove all the fun things of VTM little by little. I fully believe CTPhipps predictions/push for the Old Clan to become the forefront, because they definitely don't want Vicissitude to be brought back into VTM for whatever reason with how V5 is taking the franchise.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense for them to even dislike Vicissitude, I thought the reason why they are making all these changes is because they want the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; spiel and that's why they want to take out all the perceived &quot;DnD-esque/Supher with Fangs&quot; aspects of what made VTM fun (its always a notion I always hated. Just because your PC, NPC, or generally high powers in the setting- DOES NOT MAKE THEM SUPERHEROES, who is the idiot in the fanbase who came up this idiom?!), even with that considered Vicissitude never was campy- it was downright horrifying with how you could nab and morph your victim in any you so pleased- or with YOU on the receiving end because you blundered and got caught and is now in the manor basement of a Tzimisce Elder waiting for operation. The Tzimisce ARE a cult classic among the fanbase because of the crazy shit they can pull of Vicissitude and the general alieness of how far they can descend post-embrace by their sire. That's what MAKES the Sabbat- they are the epiphany of the Sabbat philosophy in the end... beings who have fully assimilated into the fact they are now something else entirely removed from humanity and act as such, but not propagandized like how CTPhipps say they are all inane &quot;crazies&quot;, they are vampiric inhuman in a controlled diabolical way. Its not that they are &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;good&quot; anymore by &quot;Human&quot; standards, because the Tzimisce don't even recognize that anymore, they are entities who only care about the 1000 ways they can morph some poor sod into a flesh n' bone broom-handle. THAT'S what makes the Tzimisce fun.<br /> <br /> Nuking them down for them to have Protean or... Animalism? (Animalism... Animalism... ... ... LOOOOOOOOOL!) would be a horrible blunder. They would be plain soup as Chris put it in page 2. There is no reason to shove the Tzimisce this route because the Venture already have the niche people want to lambast this beloved clan into. Sure the Tzimisce are &quot;lords&quot; and yes this clan is mostly from Eastern Europe, but to morph the Tzimisce more into their supposed &quot;archetype&quot; (..Dracula?) for the sake of it is garbage and cliche. What makes the Tzimisce is Vicissitude and will break them if they are removed.<br /> <br /> /end rant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-17-2020, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:23:38-07:00","id":1397124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397107#post1397107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sure. The Ventrue have it fairly easy, they use of Dominate and Presence to create Renfeld type servants, cause terror and awe, use mental abuse on opponents etc, the mob running in supernatural terror, the brain washed thralls, the compulsion to go investigate the dark castle etc. The Lasombra can also do the Dominate addled weird village thing, as well as the brain washed servants etc, but hits harder on the esoteric themes with Obtenerbration/Oblivion, and is more physically powerful due to potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've still failed to address the central thrust of my argument, that &quot;Lords&quot; who focus more on animals or the land itself are somehow less valid. Again, to use CTPhipps favourite example, Dracula: summoning a pack of wolves to murder the woman demanding you return her child. Another example, a murder of ghoul-crows that spy on your domain during the day, Saruman-style. A Ventrue or Lasombra *can't* do that better, unless I'm allowed to say a Tzimisce can take Dominate out-of-clan and be better than either of the other &quot;noble&quot; clans (ignoring Old Clan on purpose here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> More to add, again, but back to work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:31:51-07:00","id":1397125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397124#post1397124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you've still failed to address the central thrust of my argument, that &quot;Lords&quot; who focus more on animals or the land itself are somehow less valid. Again, to use CTPhipps favourite example, Dracula: summoning a pack of wolves to murder the woman demanding you return her child. Another example, a murder of ghoul-crows that spy on your domain during the day, Saruman-style. A Ventrue or Lasombra *can't* do that better, unless I'm allowed to say a Tzimisce can take Dominate out-of-clan and be better than either of the other &quot;noble&quot; clans (ignoring Old Clan on purpose here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> More to add, again, but back to work!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and I'll turn the question on you: why do you want to destroy everything interesting about the Tzim and turn them into bad movie cliches? (and CTPhipps has said that, he wants Old Clan as the Dominant Tzim, the only way to do that is obliteration of the 'not a terrible copy of a venture with animalism' that the old clan are.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:33:27-07:00","id":1397127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397115#post1397115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah.. so we're back to this conversation with the Tzismisce.. If that's the case I'll go back on the original tangent I had whenever this is brought up: Tzimisce without Vicissitude aren't the Tzimisce anymore. Leave the Koldunism for the Old Clan- that's what their for, the niche portion of the Tzimisce who don't use Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, koldunism was done for the tzimisce, not just the old clan, for several reasons:<br /> <br /> - ghouls, revenants and war ghouls:<br /> they require both vicissitude and koldunism<br /> <br /> - metamophosis:<br /> the path of metamorphosis seeks transandence in both the material and the spriritual,<br /> Vicissitude allows them to break their material limits<br /> Koldunism (or thaumaturgy, depending on tzimisce) allows them to expend their spiritual presence/power<br /> <br /> - history with lupines:<br /> koldunism is how they managed to beat the shadow lords<br /> <br /> - how they keep their territories:<br /> in the Dark Ages, koldunism was used to keep track of people moving in and out of their territories,<br /> elliminate enemies, sink their ships, but also culling the mortals under their rule (some of it was done with vicissitide as well),<br /> and...well, lupines<br /> <br /> koldunism is definitely not an old clan specific gimmick,<br /> or at least it wasn't...until v20 complicated things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:37:26-07:00","id":1397128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397115#post1397115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when we consider the fact that they are probably going to do an asspull where somehow the Tzimisce aren't even the Sabbat and get shoved into the Camarilla (and to the Gods, please let this only be theoretical), what BASIS is them to be a keyed-in &quot;magic&quot; clan when that point was LITERALLY the Tremere, which is now stolen by the Assamites who- just as you guessed- has been totally assed into the Camarilla with no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Assamites joining the Camarilla has been a thing since Revised and was revisited in BJD. Out of all the changes V5's made, this one's probably had the most foreshadowing of all\u2014I would have been disappointed if they <i>hadn't</i> finally given us some new lore on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397115#post1397115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why Old Clan is even mentioned for whatever reason (and in JAPAN of all places?) even when we have zilch on the main fan favorite one, because the writing is on the wall- they want to systemically remove all the fun things of VTM little by little. I fully believe CTPhipps predictions/push for the Old Clan to become the forefront, because they definitely don't want Vicissitude to be brought back into VTM for whatever reason with how V5 is taking the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Chicago By Night</i> has passing references to Tzimisce flesh-shaping. This is also about as much material as we got about the Hecata before <i>Cults</i>, and about as much material as we got about the Lasombra before <i>CbN</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397115#post1397115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuking them down for them to have Protean or... Animalism? (Animalism... Animalism... ... ... LOOOOOOOOOL!) would be a horrible blunder. They would be plain soup as Chris put it in page 2. There is no reason to shove the Tzimisce this route because the Venture already have the niche people want to lambast this beloved clan into. Sure the Tzimisce are &quot;lords&quot; and yes this clan is mostly from Eastern Europe, but to morph the Tzimisce more into their supposed &quot;archetype&quot; (..Dracula?) for the sake of it is garbage and cliche. What makes the Tzimisce is Vicissitude and will break them if they are removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026haven't the Tzimisce <i>always</i> had Animalism, going back to their very first appearance? Hasn't their discipline spread always, since the very beginning, been Vicissitude, Auspex, Animalism? I understand you don't like V5, but if giving the Tzimisce in-clan Animalism would be a horrible mistake, it's a mistake that's been made in every single edition so far.<br /> <br /> Again, we already know the Tzimisce are still going to have flesh-shaping powers. That's been confirmed in the printed books. I legitimately don't understand where all this anger is coming from. I don't think anyone, at any point, has suggested taking flesh-shaping away from the Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:43:06-07:00","id":1397131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397128#post1397128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, we already know the Tzimisce are still going to have flesh-shaping powers. That's been confirmed in the printed books. I legitimately don't understand where all this anger is coming from. I don't think anyone, at any point, has suggested taking flesh-shaping away from the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>it was suggested that Vici were gonna turn into protean or a blood sorcery amalgam<br /> <br /> though, that's not what sparked the debate,<br /> the debate started when someone in another thread asked if people believed Tzimisce were all about Vicissitude,<br /> the debate just found its way in this thread<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:52:15-07:00","id":1397133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397128#post1397128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026haven't the Tzimisce <i>always</i> had Animalism, going back to their very first appearance? Hasn't their discipline spread always, since the very beginning, been Vicissitude, Auspex, Animalism? I understand you don't like V5, but if giving the Tzimisce in-clan Animalism would be a horrible mistake, it's a mistake that's been made in every single edition so far.<br /> <br /> Again, we already know the Tzimisce are still going to have flesh-shaping powers. That's been confirmed in the printed books. I legitimately don't understand where all this anger is coming from. I don't think anyone, at any point, has suggested taking flesh-shaping away from the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did have animalism, they should have Viscititude, not a half assed options on protean, but Viscititude, as a separate and distinct thing, no merger of disciplines so far has been anything but a trai wreck, and it needs to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:59:07-07:00","id":1397135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397128#post1397128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Chicago By Night</i> has passing references to Tzimisce flesh-shaping. This is also about as much material as we got about the Hecata before <i>Cults</i>, and about as much material as we got about the Lasombra before <i>CbN</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also &quot;the Butterfly&quot; in <i>Anarch</i>, running around shaping ears on people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T13:07:07-07:00","id":1397136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397133#post1397133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did have animalism, they should have Viscititude, not a half assed options on protean, but Viscititude, as a separate and distinct thing, no merger of disciplines so far has been anything but a trai wreck, and it needs to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part I think the mergers have gone pretty well. Did we really need to separate out the Discipline of Turning Into Snakes from the Discipline of Turning Into Animals That Are Not Snakes? Setites can still turn into snakes, remove their hearts, have hypnotic eyes; Gangrel can still meld into the dirt, grow claws, turn into wolves or mist; there's just more versatility and less wasted wordcount now.<br /> <br /> (I do have to say &quot;for the most part&quot;. I don't like the way Oblivion's been handled and very much hope that one changes. But I think the concept of discipline mergers is fine.)<br /> <br /> Vicissitude, in the past (using V20 as an example), has been a strange mix of powers that don't all quite connect to each other. The first three dots are the creepy flesh-shaping surgery ones\u2026then the fourth dot is an instantaneous transformation, Protean-style, and the fifth dot is instant discorporation, also Protean-style.<br /> <br /> What I'm hoping for instead is that the mechanics get cleaned up so that you don't need to buy two roadblock powers before you can actually do full flesh-shaping, and the &quot;instant change into another form&quot; powers get put into normal Protean instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T14:05:59-07:00","id":1397148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397125#post1397125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I'll turn the question on you: why do you want to destroy everything interesting about the Tzim and turn them into bad movie cliches? (and CTPhipps has said that, he wants Old Clan as the Dominant Tzim, the only way to do that is obliteration of the 'not a terrible copy of a venture with animalism' that the old clan are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Taggie, is it possible for you to have a debate without insulting every argument of your opponents?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T14:26:17-07:00","id":1397151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397148#post1397148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taggie, is it possible for you to have a debate without insulting every argument of your opponents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that you consistently call the Tzim as they are in V20 and previous editions, degerates, and your attack on Viscititude, turn about is fair play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T14:26:33-07:00","id":1397152,"title":"","content":"To address some of @Taggie's points:<br /> <br /> 1. If you can't appreciate the classic literary Bram Stoker's Dracula with its depth of characterization, use of history, and variety of powers as well as occult references than you are the one in the wrong. The dismissing of a desire to have a clan that PROPERLY respresents Dracula is nothing to be ashamed of and your dismissal of it is flat out disappointing. I also have read Necroscope and while they're fine, Stoker obviously 100 percent trumps Lumley. Dracula got improperly broken up among Gangrel, Ventrue, and Tremere.<br /> <br /> 2. I think the Old Clan Tzimisce should be available as options for the Camarilla and Anarchs because they're a fascinating bunch of people. The Dark Ages Tzimisce were a bunch of awesome characters and the Old Clan Tzimisce are the ones who carry their spirit into Modern Times. They should also be part of the Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> 3. I mentioned I have a distaste for <b>&quot;Flesh Monkeys&quot;</b> over in another thread. Those are people who don't have any real respect for the Tzimisce's feudal lord status, honor codes, or inhuman ideologies beyond Vicissitude. I basically referred to them as Fishmalks for Tzimisce. I don't think that's the case here but it's very irritating that you keep putting down the idea that Vicissitude somehow is more important than actual WRITING for the Clan and makes me think you have a somewhat shallow view of them.<br /> <br /> 4. I have no interest in getting rid of the Sabbat Tzimisce and I don't even dislike Vicissitude or its effects. I think the Old Clan Tzimisce lose a lot of their flavor if they don't have the Modern Tzimisce to contrast themselves against. I've stated repeatedly I want the Sabbat to return and be detailed in ways beyond &quot;they're off fighting the Gehenna Crusade.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397151#post1397151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that you consistently call the Tzim as they are in V20 and previous editions, degerates, and your attack on Viscititude, turn about is fair play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...they're SABBAT. Since 2nd Edition, the Sabbat have been portrayed as the barbarian horde at the Camarilla's gates.<br /> <br /> And spare me the argument that I attack Vicissitude because that holds no water.<br /> <br /> <b>How I feel about Vicissitude</b><br /> <br /> Vicissitude is probably the third or fourth most important element of the Tzimsice. It's important to the clan and allows a lot of philosophical and interesting elements. It's overused, overpowered, and is in dire need of a rules update. Nothing makes my eyes roll more than the idea of a guy who envisions a Tzimisce as a guy who makes bone and flesh chairs without explaining how this relates to his desire to transcend his vampiric weaknesses, scholarship, or Feudal Lord status (Tzimisce are scholars and scientists every bit as much as feudal lords). Flesh Monkeys are a problem that has resulted in the Clan getting Flanderized (see TV tropes) into a parody of itself.<br /> <br /> Tzimsice should absolutely have all of the powers that they had from Vicissitude as an option for them because a huge chunk of lore is related to Vicissitude. Revenant families can only be created by a combination of Blood Sorcery and Vicissitude (probably) rather than just breeding ghouls. Also, while deformed evil monsters are not the most important part of the Tzimisce, they WERE a part of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think that Vicissitude is getting chopped up. They mentioned Tzimisce as having Protean in Chicago by Night and the context is that a trans woman used that to complete her transition prior to medical advances (and post-Embrace). In effect, that she used Protean the same way a Tzimsice used Vicissitude. I don't think there's any point discussing whether this is a good idea because I think it's going to happen whether people like it or not. So the only thing to do is discuss how to implement it rather than complain about it. It's been there, done, and now it's time to follow up on the effects.<br /> <br /> If you don't understand what I mean by this, <b>I think Vicissitude is not getting removed, I think Vicisstiude is getting nerfed.</b> I think the Protean replacement will probably mean that Tzimisce will be able to change their bodies but won't be able to change the bodies of others save at higher levels or with some combination Discipline. I recommended Blood Sorcery/Protean for warping others because I think Tzimisce should have Blood Sorcery as a Clan Discipline in place of Auspex. I really think they need to adapt all of the Path of Bio-Thaumaturgical Experimentation to Tzimisce and allow them to have access to it. They always should have had it rather than the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> But yes, without the ability to warp flesh of themselves and others, the Tzimisce lose a lot.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this is for V5 because none of he matters here apply to previous Editions and if you don't love V5 why would you care?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-17-2020, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T14:50:49-07:00","id":1397158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397115#post1397115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah.. so we're back to this conversation with the Tzismisce.. If that's the case I'll go back on the original tangent I had whenever this is brought up: Tzimisce without Vicissitude aren't the Tzimisce anymore. Leave the Koldunism for the Old Clan- that's what their for, the niche portion of the Tzimisce who don't use Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is wrong because a large chunk of the lore is that Koldunism is required to make a lot of the higher-end Vicissitude monsters. You can't make a vozhd with Vicissitude alone. You need to be an incredibly Thaumaturge. Mind you, I think you misunderstand what they're PROBABLY going to do with Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However the entirety of the Tzimisce are literally shaped by Vicissitude (no pun intended) and pre-V5 (because we don't even know the status of Paths) had entire Vampiric philosophy cascading around it- for thousands of years at this point. They aren't going to just *abandon* it (with V5 nonsensical events and softcons though, you'll be definite they will find a way for this to happen) out of nowhere for no REASON whatsoever at all. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I felt like the Path of Metamorphisis was fine but it should never have dominated the Clan so completely as some fans made it so. They shouldn't forget the Path of Honorable Accord (my favorite for the Tzimisce), The Path of Death and Soul (for Vykos), the Road of Chivalry, and various Slavic Pagan influenced Roads. But you're also just making up shit because there's no sign that they'd abandon Vicissitude anymore than the Banu Haqim abandoned Quietus or the Lasombra/Giovanni lost Obternation or Necromancy. They didn't lose any of their powers or abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure a nil portion of Tzimisce are steeped in magic, but for the most part I've always seen them as inhuman biologists and sadistic warpers of flesh&amp;bone. Why would they need all these magical niches for? </div> </div> </div>Because all of their inhuman biological experiments and upper tier transformations require magic, duh. You can make some ugly deformed ghouls with bone knives but you can't make the REAL shit without Thaumaturgy/Blood Sorcery. Bio-Thaumaturgical Experimentation is one of my all time favorite Thaumaturgy Paths and should have been extremely common among the Tzimisce. They need their Doctor Frankenstein-esque magitech labs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially when we consider the fact that they are probably going to do an asspull where somehow the Tzimisce aren't even the Sabbat and get shoved into the Camarilla (and to the Gods, please let this only be theoretical), what BASIS is them to be a keyed-in &quot;magic&quot; clan when that point was LITERALLY the Tremere, which is now stolen by the Assamites who- just as you guessed- has been totally assed into the Camarilla with no sense. There doesn't NEED to be three magical clans in one Sect all at once. Beside that I sincerely doubt them ever going to the Anarchs (they wouldn't go that far.. right?) so that's out the window. </div> </div> </div>There's no need for the Tremere to have a monopoly on blood magic. Previous editions had the Tzimisce, Assamites, Setites, and Giovanni all as wizards [albeit necromancy for the Giovanni].<br /> I assume the Tzimisce will always be in the Sabbat and it's just the Old Clan members that have moved into the Camarilla or started Embracing. The Anarchs can certainly gain Tzimisce Barons as anyone who stands against the Camarilla is an Anarch as long as they're not Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The shift back to &quot;Camarilla vs Anarchs&quot; again has been the biggest devolution so far. The reason why I even mention the Sabbat is because you CAN'T have the Tzimisce without this sect </div> </div> </div>The Old Clan Tzimisce belonged to the Inconnu and Black Hand in addition to the Sabbat. Anarchs Unbound also established that there were Tzimisce in the Anarchs--mostly Sabbat defectors but far more present there than among the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason why Old Clan is even mentioned for whatever reason (and in JAPAN of all places?) even when we have zilch on the main fan favorite one, because the writing is on the wall- they want to systemically remove all the fun things of VTM little by little. </div> </div> </div>The Old Clan is fucking awesome and you're just nuts if you feel otherwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fully believe CTPhipps predictions/push for the Old Clan to become the forefront, because they definitely don't want Vicissitude to be brought back into VTM for whatever reason with how V5 is taking the franchise. </div> </div> </div>Oh that's bullshit. You actually think they're going to remove any of the powers? I don't think they'll remove a single power of Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what MAKES the Sabbat- they are the epiphany of the Sabbat philosophy in the end... beings who have fully assimilated into the fact they are now something else entirely removed from humanity and act as such, but not propagandized like how CTPhipps say they are all inane &quot;crazies&quot;, they are vampiric inhuman in a controlled diabolical way. Its not that they are &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;good&quot; anymore by &quot;Human&quot; standards, because the Tzimisce don't even recognize that anymore, they are entities who only care about the 1000 ways they can morph some poor sod into a flesh n' bone broom-handle. THAT'S what makes the Tzimisce fun. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the Old Clan's philosophy too. None of the Tzimisce have any use for humanity.<br /> <br /> Also, the Tzimisce are mostly immmune to the degeneration. I think of them as the smartest and most dangerous of all Sabbat as well as some of the few who &quot;get it.&quot; There's some Flesh Monkeys among the shovelheads but I think only a handful of Tzimisce are failures.<br /> <br /> Just the Antitribu mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T15:56:37-07:00","id":1397165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397125#post1397125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> and I'll turn the question on you: why do you want to destroy everything interesting about the Tzim and turn them into bad movie cliches? (and CTPhipps has said that, he wants Old Clan as the Dominant Tzim, the only way to do that is obliteration of the 'not a terrible copy of a venture with animalism' that the old clan are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel CTPhipps covered it, but I'll respond so my position is clear.<br /> <br /> I also generally don't bother to do more than skim Shaka's posts because they tend to be pretty the same, but extra wordy. Maybe I'll give him a fair look in a bit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do you want to destroy everything interesting about the Tzimisce?&quot;<br /> <br /> Clarification: what is &quot;everything interesting&quot; about the Tzimisce?<br /> <br /> ONE interesting thing about the Tzimisce is Vicissitude. One. Thing. One thing that I very much don't want to get rid of or destroy, because I think it plays an important part of what *I think* is the most interesting thing, the pursuit of monstrous transcendence.<br /> <br /> You might want to say &quot;That's Vicissitude!&quot; But I would argue that you're wrong. On my phone, so I'll find the link later, but there was a thread a while back titled &quot;Path of Metamorphosis for Vampires who know Disciplines other than Vicissitude Exist&quot; which perfectly demonstrated what I mean. Before that thread, I would have agreed with CTPhipps about giving V5 Tzimisce Blood Sorcery, only I would have thrown Animalism away instead. But having the importance of Animalism as a Discipline for controlling the Beast pointed out changed my mind.<br /> <br /> (P.S. Here's the link: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1365619-path-of-metamorphis-except-you-know-other-disciplines-besides-vicissitude-exist\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...issitude-exist</a>)<br /> <br /> So, acknowledging that *I do not want to get rid of Vicissitude,* I would still disagree that I want to take &quot;everything interesting&quot; away from them. That you and those who agree with you aren't interested in ANYTHING Tzimisce except Vicissitude isn't the same as saying nothing else IS interesting, for anyone.<br /> <br /> And that's why I suggested earlier that the arguments being made are bad faith, or just bad; the utter inability to consider the other position is so extreme that it comes across as willful ignorance. And no, the reverse is not true, because I *can* understand why some people are into creep-show &quot;Flesh Monkey&quot; Tzimisce. But while CTPhipps and I generally clarify that we are offering personal opinions, you and Shaka make absolute statements about the clan being &quot;completely ruined&quot; just because your personal flavour is getting less emphasis.<br /> <br /> P.P.S.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397091#post1397091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>On the Cathedral of Flesh: it was the womb of the Eldest, it's rebirth was coming. Also Kuapula had something to do with it</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a citation for that? Not trying to be difficult, I am genuinely interested if there's material supporting that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> AFAIK, it was the Dracon that served as the &quot;womb&quot; for the rebirth of the Eldest; it stayed with Yorak in the Cathedral after its &quot;birth.&quot; And that again doesn't mean that Yorak didn't make the Cathedral due to the subconscious manipulations of the Eldest, but I haven't seen any material stating it. Everything I have read suggests that the Cathedral of Flesh was Yorak's personal project. Regarding how it might have aided a Metamorphosist, my best hunch so far has to do with the depiction from TC2 where Yorak's name is repeated as a psychic mantra over and over, perhaps having some spiritual effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-17-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:24:44-07:00","id":1397235,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> damn right I want to leave the racist 19th century stereotypes of Eastern Europeans behind, for exactly the same reason the Ravnos need a rewrite,and the Banu Haqim did. Metamorphosis is what the Clan had apart from that, (and Necroscope is guilty of mixing cold war stereotypes with 19th century ones, and is by no means perfect), and that relies on Viscititude being its own thing, free and clear.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_of_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_of_Flesh</a> has the argument that the Cathedral was part of the rebirth process, with citations, basically the Dracon birthed part of the Eldest, but another 'seed' was in the Cathedral, and was also needed. The assumption that Kuapula was up to something is based on it being in the Transylvania Chronicles, and involving Koldunism, which was at least tainted by him at the time. I might be wrong (or badly our of date) but given that a cathedral shows up in New York (maybe two, depending on how canon Redemption is) I think it at least worth thinking about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-18-2020, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:29:40-07:00","id":1397238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397235#post1397235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> damn right I want to leave the racist 19th century stereotypes of Eastern Europeans behind, for exactly the same reason the Ravnos need a rewrite,and the Banu Haqim did. Metamorphosis is what the Clan had apart from that, (and Necroscope is guilty of mixing cold war stereotypes with 19th century ones, and is by no means perfect), and that relies on Viscititude being its own thing, free and clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claiming the other side is racist when talking about undead versions of aristocrats that died out centuries ago isn't an argument. It's in fact trivializing of real life prejudice. In real life, there's a damned big difference between saying the Hapsburgs were vampires and a real life ethnic minority are a bunch of magical people turned into vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, have you read Necroscope? Because the Necroscope vampires don't have a philosophy about their metamorphosis abilities. That's just one of their powers because bodycrafting how their pseudo-scientific vampirism works. They actually have a adopted philosophy based on Eastern European nobility. In other words, Lumley thought the Old World element was more interesting than their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:52:38-07:00","id":1397243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397235#post1397235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> damn right I want to leave the racist 19th century stereotypes of Eastern Europeans behind, for exactly the same reason the Ravnos need a rewrite,and the Banu Haqim did. Metamorphosis is what the Clan had apart from that, (and Necroscope is guilty of mixing cold war stereotypes with 19th century ones, and is by no means perfect), and that relies on Viscititude being its own thing, free and clear.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_of_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_of_Flesh</a> has the argument that the Cathedral was part of the rebirth process, with citations, basically the Dracon birthed part of the Eldest, but another 'seed' was in the Cathedral, and was also needed. The assumption that Kuapula was up to something is based on it being in the Transylvania Chronicles, and involving Koldunism, which was at least tainted by him at the time. I might be wrong (or badly our of date) but given that a cathedral shows up in New York (maybe two, depending on how canon Redemption is) I think it at least worth thinking about</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read that entry plenty of times, and I specifically checked the wiki page before asking, but I totally forgot. That's what I get for posting on the run. Thanks for humouring me!<br /> <br /> Regarding 'racist' stereotypes, I can definitely agree that you probably don't want players or Storytellers engaging in horrible accents with excessive 'v's and 'ah-ahahahs,' but are you really trying to argue that the 'Dracula' archetype is racist in a sense that it is harmful in the modern day? Has that conversation been had previously in this forum? Might be worth a thread, but has larger implications on the setting than just defending Vicissitude. Nor does the &quot;lord of the land&quot; archetype that is being defended necessarily rely on those stereotypes. That's baked much deeper into the Tzimisce cultural identity and history.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Metamorphosis needs Vicissitude to be its own Discipline separate from everything else for the Tzimisce to work,&quot; see my previous post. In my opinion, someone who reduces the majesty of the Path of Metamorphosis to just Vicissitude, or even just the Tzimisce clan Disciplines, is the one who is missing out. And to reiterate, I am someone who is trying to get a game of DAV20 set up, where Vicissitude gets to remain it's own thing, and I'm content.* But I cannot understand why Vicissitude needs to be its own special-snowflake-Discipline separate from Protean for the Path of Metamorphosis to work; it only makes sense if you think Necroscope-fleshwarping deserves a Discipline unto itself, which I find arguable. Without arguing for or against consolidating the Disciplines like they did for V5, <b>if</b> they were going to do it, <b>then</b> Vicissitude &gt; Protean makes sense, which is why I proposed the &quot;this is how to make all this work with previous canon with relatively little fuss and muss&quot; earlier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Admitting ignorance about V5, are Agg-damage-claws still a Protean thing? Acknowledging the 1-power-per-Discipline-level thing that everyone seems to hate with the new multi-power Discipline setup creates problems, having Protean claws potentially be on the same Discipline track as Zulo-form is a big hell-yes from me.<br /> <br /> * &quot;Content&quot; = &quot;tinkering on homebrew systems for various Vicissitude modifications for the self or others in the past&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-18-2020, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T01:28:40-07:00","id":1397251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397243#post1397243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admitting ignorance about V5, are Agg-damage-claws still a Protean thing? Acknowledging the 1-power-per-Discipline-level thing that everyone seems to hate with the new multi-power Discipline setup creates problems, having Protean claws potentially be on the same Discipline track as Zulo-form is a big hell-yes from me.<br /> <br /> * &quot;Content&quot; = &quot;tinkering on homebrew systems for various Vicissitude modifications for the self or others in the past&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, in 5th there are no combat disciplines with aggravated until level 4 or 5. Now, Protean does +2 basic damages that can not be reduced. It is a very strong level 2 power compared with the other disciplines, but not the overpowered choice it was. About Vicissitud, as Dementation is a combo power Dominate+Obfuscate, could be implemented as an amalgam of Protean+Auspex or Protean+Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 06-18-2020, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T01:50:47-07:00","id":1397252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397243#post1397243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've read that entry plenty of times, and I specifically checked the wiki page before asking, but I totally forgot. That's what I get for posting on the run. Thanks for humouring me!<br /> <br /> Regarding 'racist' stereotypes, I can definitely agree that you probably don't want players or Storytellers engaging in horrible accents with excessive 'v's and 'ah-ahahahs,' but are you really trying to argue that the 'Dracula' archetype is racist in a sense that it is harmful in the modern day? Has that conversation been had previously in this forum? Might be worth a thread, but has larger implications on the setting than just defending Vicissitude. Nor does the &quot;lord of the land&quot; archetype that is being defended necessarily rely on those stereotypes. That's baked much deeper into the Tzimisce cultural identity and history.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Metamorphosis needs Vicissitude to be its own Discipline separate from everything else for the Tzimisce to work,&quot; see my previous post. In my opinion, someone who reduces the majesty of the Path of Metamorphosis to just Vicissitude, or even just the Tzimisce clan Disciplines, is the one who is missing out. And to reiterate, I am someone who is trying to get a game of DAV20 set up, where Vicissitude gets to remain it's own thing, and I'm content.* But I cannot understand why Vicissitude needs to be its own special-snowflake-Discipline separate from Protean for the Path of Metamorphosis to work; it only makes sense if you think Necroscope-fleshwarping deserves a Discipline unto itself, which I find arguable. Without arguing for or against consolidating the Disciplines like they did for V5, <b>if</b> they were going to do it, <b>then</b> Vicissitude &gt; Protean makes sense, which is why I proposed the &quot;this is how to make all this work with previous canon with relatively little fuss and muss&quot; earlier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Admitting ignorance about V5, are Agg-damage-claws still a Protean thing? Acknowledging the 1-power-per-Discipline-level thing that everyone seems to hate with the new multi-power Discipline setup creates problems, having Protean claws potentially be on the same Discipline track as Zulo-form is a big hell-yes from me.<br /> <br /> * &quot;Content&quot; = &quot;tinkering on homebrew systems for various Vicissitude modifications for the self or others in the past&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Book Dracula Invades England by Christina Artenie (which I have on order, so have not got more than the blurbs for yet) makes the argument that Dracula with it's focus on Romanians coming to pollute the blood of England was a direct reference to the marriage of Princess Mary of Teck to the future George V, she was a descendant of Vlad Tepes, and Stoker had reported on, and met her, as well as his brother Major George Stoker having served in the Ottoman Army as a surgeon, and took part in Russo-Turkish war, of 1878-79 (aka the Romanian war of Independence), Bram Stoker was well aware of this, and versed in the impressions his brother had of what had at that time been the enemy, as he had helped write George's memoirs. Their was also the realpolitik of England's Opposition to Romanian independence as they defacto controlled the Lower Danube and Romania after the Crimean war, and wanted to maintain that influence, as Romanian grain was cheap and plentiful, as long as that control lasted, which, after the Russo-Turkish war was at risk to say the least. Dracula was written in that environment, and cast Transylvania and Romania as backwards, and barbaric. <a href=\"https://thegothicwanderer.wordpress.com/2020/02/26/racism-in-dracula-the-romanian-perspective/\" target=\"_blank\">https://thegothicwanderer.wordpress....n-perspective/</a> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Dracula-Invades-England-Context-Readers/dp/0993995101/ref=sr_1_1?keywords=dracula+invades+england&amp;qid=1582739092&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-1&amp;pldnSite=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Dracula-Invad...1-1&amp;pldnSite=1</a><br /> <br /> The 'Old Clan' draw directly and explicitly on those stereotypes, as do the DA Tzimisce, the archetypes can be done fine, but you have to steer well clear of Dracula to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":".  EDIT: Withdrew a statement shown to be false 06-18-2020, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T02:09:51-07:00","id":1397253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397252#post1397252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Book Dracula Invades England by Christina Artenie (which I have on order, so have not got more than the blurbs for yet) makes the argument that Dracula with it's focus on Romanians coming to pollute the blood of England was a direct reference to the marriage of Princess Mary of Teck to the future George V, she was a descendant of Vlad Tepes, and Stoker had reported on, and met her, as well as his brother Major George Stoker having served in the Ottoman Army as a surgeon, and took part in Russo-Turkish war, of 1878-79 (aka the Romanian war of Independence), Bram Stoker was well aware of this, and versed in the impressions his brother had of what had at that time been the enemy, as he had helped write George's memoirs. Their was also the realpolitik of England's Opposition to Romanian independence as they defacto controlled the Lower Danube and Romania after the Crimean war, and wanted to maintain that influence, as Romanian grain was cheap and plentiful, as long as that control lasted, which, after the Russo-Turkish war was at risk to say the least. Dracula was written in that environment, and cast Transylvania and Romania as backwards, and barbaric. <a href=\"https://thegothicwanderer.wordpress.com/2020/02/26/racism-in-dracula-the-romanian-perspective/\" target=\"_blank\">https://thegothicwanderer.wordpress....n-perspective/</a> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Dracula-Invades-England-Context-Readers/dp/0993995101/ref=sr_1_1?keywords=dracula+invades+england&amp;qid=1582739092&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-1&amp;pldnSite=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Dracula-Invad...1-1&amp;pldnSite=1</a><br /> <br /> The 'Old Clan' draw directly and explicitly on those stereotypes, as do the DA Tzimisce, the archetypes can be done fine, but you have to steer well clear of Dracula to do it. (Fun fact Romania prior to Dracula didn't really have Vampire myths, they had dragons, demons, fae etc, but not a notable vampire tradition, they will take the tourist dollars tho)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, there's a lot to unpack here, Taggie but you've been extremely misinformed about a lot of things. Not the least of which being that you seem to be ignoring the existence of the Strigoi and moroi. The moroi are especially notable because they're actually the sexy vampire that English people claim to have invented but are certainly not. The vampire legends of Romanian were combined with witches but while living strigoi existed, so did undead strigoi with one becoming the latter.<br /> <br /> Believe me, I spent years investigating this stuff and almost did my dissertation on it.<br /> <br /> As for the claims about Bram Stoker here, you're making an elaborate series of justifications that all fall apart under a judicious application of Occam's Razor. Which is the fact that Bram Stoker's Dracula is not actually the origin of any of the Old Clan Tzimisce's ideas or the subject of some great conspiracy of political theory. In fact, it's basically just a rewrite and combination of Polidori's THE VAMPYRE and Le Fanu's CARMILLA. This is pretty much confirmed by Dracula's Guest where it's ABUNDANTLY obvious that he's just combining the two stories.<br /> <br /> However, we actually DO get the politics of Dracula in the OTHER edition of Dracula. Which is THE POWERS OF DARKNESS which is effectively Dracula when it was written originally before switching around the locations, removing the sex, and removing the anti-racist anti-militarist anti-Social Darwinist politics. Dracula is then described as a German supremacist and a believer of the mass murder of inferior races as well as the creation of a massive ethnostate with himself at the head of it. Dracula's Romanian heritage doesn't matter because he's already taken over vast amounts of Germany's nobility with his secret cult. Dracula's Guest references that the vampires are vast in number in Germany and he's turned much of their nobility.<br /> <br /> Stoker removed all of the politics of DRACULA for the purposes of sales, probably, and to avoid being overtly political under the censorship of the time but was making a early anti-fascist anti-racist screed.<br /> <br /> If you don't believe me: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powers_of_Darkness#Differences_between_Dracula_and_Powers_of_Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powers...rs_of_Darkness</a><br /> <br /> There's also notes that Dracula may not have originally been Romanian at all but was actually a Bavarian leader before he moved it further East. Dracula's Guest, which was the original opening to Dracula, depicts the modern German military being fully aware of the existence of vampires and how to fight them. The fact that Carmilla takes place in Austria may have been an influence.<br /> <br /> I recommend the Maven of the Eventide's discussion of DRACULA'S GUEST, though she's more concerned with the sex than the politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/56d1WGEQ-jU\" data-code=\"56d1WGEQ-jU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/56d1WGEQ-jU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T03:42:19-07:00","id":1397258,"title":"","content":"Tzmisce without vicissitude don't really have an identity beyond &quot;Ventrue but with racism&quot; although they occasionally get into an interesting territory of &quot;Ventrue but with racism and magic&quot;. Old clan Tzmisce are &quot;Ventrue with racism that like animals and aren't really that good with people&quot; or perhaps you can look at it as &quot;Tremere but with animals and nobody else in his chantry&quot; <br /> <br /> I've said it before and I'll say it again but I think the &quot;Old Clan&quot; is a misguided bit of writing by authors who read &quot;Dracula is a Tzmisce&quot; and got a bit carried away there. I do like the Dichtimony between the ancient viovodes and the modern street freaks, but that's not a thing of &quot;Vicissitude VS no Viccisitude&quot; that's a thing of &quot;Wealth and taste VS nutjobs in crazy countercultures&quot;. <br /> <br /> I like the old clan discipline spread, I like the snobbery, but I think it's a mistake to seriously push what should be a small bloodline into the Real OG Tzmisce. <br /> Running Tzmisce without Vicissitude is like running Tremere without Thaumaturgy (Which might be the case given what V5 so far has given us with that discipline). Sure, you can have good fun with a Thaumaturgy-less Tremere, but you're meant to be an odd-job among odd-jobs, not the norm. <br /> <br /> From what I've read about Tokyo, I'm honestly a lot more interested in Kyoto. I imagine this 'hunger abating feeling' is a Koldunic Krania/Thaumaturgy ritual designed to impose order on others, and the lack of elders in the city stops people from breaking it. That said, I really don't like the thematics of disapearing all the elders. Neonates should be chaffing under their rule, not enjoying care-free lives without elder oppression. V5's politics becoming a lot 'easier' is one of the biggest turnoffs and I'd like to see things return to getting worse, not better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T03:58:42-07:00","id":1397261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397258#post1397258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce without vicissitude don't really have an identity beyond &quot;Ventrue but with racism&quot; although they occasionally get into an interesting territory of &quot;Ventrue but with racism and magic&quot;. Old clan Tzmisce are &quot;Ventrue with racism that like animals and aren't really that good with people&quot; or perhaps you can look at it as &quot;Tremere but with animals and nobody else in his chantry&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is your opinion as a fan, it definitely means that we should make Old Clan Tzimisce in Japan and other locations. Make &quot;territorial aristocratic noble&quot; something not linked to any specific area.<br /> <br /> Besides, Carmilla is Austrian and Lord Ruthven (the original Polidori one) is Scottish.<br /> <br /> And Old Clan Tzimisce have Dominate in place of Vicissitude so they actually are very good with ordering people around. They just aren't very good at getting people to like them when obeying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've said it before and I'll say it again but I think the &quot;Old Clan&quot; is a misguided bit of writing by authors who read &quot;Dracula is a Tzmisce&quot; and got a bit carried away there. I do like the Dichtimony between the ancient viovodes and the modern street freaks, but that's not a thing of &quot;Vicissitude VS no Viccisitude&quot; that's a thing of &quot;Wealth and taste VS nutjobs in crazy countercultures&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I've always felt Dracula could have been a Gangrel but the Gangrel have never had a noble aristocratic heritage that could have made them a much more interesting Clan. As such, Dracula being a Tzimisce is easily the most interesting thing about them and makes the character interpretation in V:TM more interesting. However, the fact is the Necroscope vampires are ALL extremely Slavic tyrants so people acting like, &quot;They're like the Whampyri&quot; make no sense.<br /> <br /> Because the Necroscope Whampyri are even MORE stereotypically Eastern European than the Old Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the old clan discipline spread, I like the snobbery, but I think it's a mistake to seriously push what should be a small bloodline into the Real OG Tzmisce.<br /> Running Tzmisce without Vicissitude is like running Tremere without Thaumaturgy (Which might be the case given what V5 so far has given us with that discipline). Sure, you can have good fun with a Thaumaturgy-less Tremere, but you're meant to be an odd-job among odd-jobs, not the norm. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, <b>if I were to hope for a retcon</b>, I would hope that they just give the Old Clan Tzimisce Vicissitude and make the distinction between them one of sects. The New Clan are the Sabbat and the Old Clan are the ones who were rebelled against but survived better than the Lasombra's Elders while not joining the Camarilla (fucking Tremere). The Dark Ages kind of ruined the OC Tzimisce's thing when they had Vicissitude spread among all the Voivoides and the Eldest.<br /> <br /> So they might as well have it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I've read about Tokyo, I'm honestly a lot more interested in Kyoto. I imagine this 'hunger abating feeling' is a Koldunic Krania/Thaumaturgy ritual designed to impose order on others, and the lack of elders in the city stops people from breaking it. That said, I really don't like the thematics of disapearing all the elders. Neonates should be chaffing under their rule, not enjoying care-free lives without elder oppression. V5's politics becoming a lot 'easier' is one of the biggest turnoffs and I'd like to see things return to getting worse, not better. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, 300 years means that there's still a shit ton of Elders. That just means that they're Elders who can be killed with shotguns to the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T03:59:48-07:00","id":1397262,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> will have to wait for the book to arrive, and to have fully read it, before answering fully, I will note however that the Wiki you cite does make it clear that the differences may be from actions by the translators/editors, not a previous draft. Either way, I would be working on insufficient data to respond more fully now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:03:26-07:00","id":1397263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397262#post1397262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> will have to wait for the book to arrive, and to have fully read it, before answering fully, I will note however that the Wiki you cite does make it clear that the differences may be from actions by the translators/editors, not a previous draft. Either way, I would be working on insufficient data to respond more fully now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The translators added some Norse mythology references but I don't think they wrote whole scenes. I appreciate you taking the time to discuss this, though. I am quite appreciative of your in-depth discussion and looking up the material you mentioned.<br /> <br /> :thumbs up:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:18:28-07:00","id":1397264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397261#post1397261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)If this is your opinion as a fan, it definitely means that we should make Old Clan Tzimisce in Japan and other locations. Make &quot;territorial aristocratic noble&quot; something not linked to any specific area.<br /> <br /> Besides, Carmilla is Austrian and Lord Ruthven (the original Polidori one) is Scottish.<br /> <br /> And Old Clan Tzimisce have Dominate in place of Vicissitude so they actually are very good with ordering people around. They just aren't very good at getting people to like them when obeying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)I've always felt Dracula could have been a Gangrel but the Gangrel have never had a noble aristocratic heritage that could have made them a much more interesting Clan. As such, Dracula being a Tzimisce is easily the most interesting thing about them and makes the character interpretation in V:TM more interesting. However, the fact is the Necroscope vampires are ALL extremely Slavic tyrants so people acting like, &quot;They're like the Whampyri&quot; make no sense.<br /> <br /> Because the Necroscope Whampyri are even MORE stereotypically Eastern European than the Old Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3)Honestly, <b>if I were to hope for a retcon</b>, I would hope that they just give the Old Clan Tzimisce Vicissitude and make the distinction between them one of sects. The New Clan are the Sabbat and the Old Clan are the ones who were rebelled against but survived better than the Lasombra's Elders while not joining the Camarilla (fucking Tremere). The Dark Ages kind of ruined the OC Tzimisce's thing when they had Vicissitude spread among all the Voivoides and the Eldest.<br /> <br /> So they might as well have it too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 4)I dunno, 300 years means that there's still a shit ton of Elders. That just means that they're Elders who can be killed with shotguns to the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) My opinion is the OC, like the True Brujah, are a mistake.<br /> <br /> 2) Norman Gangrel iirc from Dark Ages where that, and it is an idea that could have gone further. Yes the Whampyri are also flawed, but they are less so than Dracula, but this goes back to a previous statement, and I don't have the book(s) to go further yet<br /> <br /> 3)That could work.<br /> <br /> 4) Ancilla are less scary than 'proper' elders, the killing them with a shotgun thing does take away from the oppressive power of the ancients, at least imho, but then I like the methusalehs as walking apocalypses aspect of previous editions, so that's a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-18-2020, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:23:31-07:00","id":1397265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397263#post1397263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The translators added some Norse mythology references but I don't think they wrote whole scenes. I appreciate you taking the time to discuss this, though. I am quite appreciative of your in-depth discussion and looking up the material you mentioned.<br /> <br /> :thumbs up:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We shall both see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:40:40-07:00","id":1397266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) My opinion is the OC, like the True Brujah, are a mistake. </div> </div> </div>And my opinion is you're very wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:44:56-07:00","id":1397267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397266#post1397266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And my opinion is you're very wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> fair enough, I know they wont be gone, I just don't want them muscling out the new clan, and I want the new clan to be recognisable, which so far with the implications of merged disciplines and amalgam powers, is in doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T05:32:29-07:00","id":1397273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397261#post1397261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is your opinion as a fan, it definitely means that we should make Old Clan Tzimisce in Japan and other locations. Make &quot;territorial aristocratic noble&quot; something not linked to any specific area.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be opposed to that, partly, but I really, really like Vicissitude, because it's <i>art</i>. And I really like the &quot;doctor&quot; Tzmisce (Only instead of tools he's lugging around, it's his jar of dirt)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There are so many different kinds of things you could do with Vicissitude. It's as versatile/potentially more versatile than pre-V5 thaumaturgy. You can be any kind of doctor as a Tzmisce (Auspex/Animalism help with the mental side of things; Using dominate would be a hack move) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Here's a few things you could be with Vicissitude off the top of my head.<br /> -Actually improving someone's health through using vicissitude to improve upon mundane surgical procedures.<br /> -plastic surgeon<br /> -Artificial aging specialist<br /> -Masquerade compliant body modifier (Tattoos, piercings)<br /> -Taxidermist<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-Avant garde platic surgeon<br /> -Masquerade defying body modifier<br /> -Monster creator (and all the different specialisties you could have within that)<br /> -Physical Performance enhancer</span></span></span><br /> -Animal specialist<br /> -Brain shaping (there are no rules for it but think of the possibilities both mundane and vicissitude enhanced)<br /> -Dentist<br /> -Eye doctor (Frog eyes for all!)<br /> -Gender specialist<br /> -Drug specialist*<br /> -Performance enhancement. (No, that wasn't a dick euphemism, but it can be)<br /> -Mastering Weird shit like bioluminescence or suckers or web spinners.<br /> -Furniture designer<br /> -Clothing designer<br /> -Engineer<br /> -Architect<br /> -Tool creation specialists (Again, many subdivisions)<br /> -Prosthetic/Cybernetic* specialist<br /> -Magic/Vicissitude specialist<br /> -Genetic modification (Probably an elder thing)<br /> -Zulo specialist*<br /> -Bloodform Specialist.*<br /> -Flight specialist<br /> Edit:<br /> -Super Cool aquarium guy<br /> -&quot;Exotic fossil&quot; trader. <br /> <br /> *No current rules for these, but there could/should be.<br /> <br /> And that's just the ideas that came into my head as I wrote this.<br /> Tzmisce without Vicissitude is like Tremere without Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-18-2020, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:21:07-07:00","id":1397322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397273#post1397273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be opposed to that, partly, but I really, really like Vicissitude, because it's <i>art</i>. And I really like the &quot;doctor&quot; Tzmisce (Only instead of tools he's lugging around, it's his jar of dirt)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There are so many different kinds of things you could do with Vicissitude. It's as versatile/potentially more versatile than pre-V5 thaumaturgy. You can be any kind of doctor as a Tzmisce (Auspex/Animalism help with the mental side of things; Using dominate would be a hack move) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Here's a few things you could be with Vicissitude off the top of my head.<br /> -Actually improving someone's health through using vicissitude to improve upon mundane surgical procedures.<br /> -plastic surgeon<br /> -Artificial aging specialist<br /> -Masquerade compliant body modifier (Tattoos, piercings)<br /> -Taxidermist<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-Avant garde platic surgeon<br /> -Masquerade defying body modifier<br /> -Monster creator (and all the different specialisties you could have within that)<br /> -Physical Performance enhancer</span></span></span><br /> -Animal specialist<br /> -Brain shaping (there are no rules for it but think of the possibilities both mundane and vicissitude enhanced)<br /> -Dentist<br /> -Eye doctor (Frog eyes for all!)<br /> -Gender specialist<br /> -Drug specialist*<br /> -Performance enhancement. (No, that wasn't a dick euphemism, but it can be)<br /> -Mastering Weird shit like bioluminescence or suckers or web spinners.<br /> -Furniture designer<br /> -Clothing designer<br /> -Engineer<br /> -Architect<br /> -Tool creation specialists (Again, many subdivisions)<br /> -Prosthetic/Cybernetic* specialist<br /> -Magic/Vicissitude specialist<br /> -Genetic modification (Probably an elder thing)<br /> -Zulo specialist*<br /> -Bloodform Specialist.*<br /> -Flight specialist<br /> Edit:<br /> -Super Cool aquarium guy<br /> -&quot;Exotic fossil&quot; trader.<br /> <br /> *No current rules for these, but there could/should be.<br /> <br /> And that's just the ideas that came into my head as I wrote this.<br /> Tzmisce without Vicissitude is like Tremere without Thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I really like your ideas for possible uses of Vicissitude. Regarding your &quot;artificial aging specialist&quot; idea, I myself have been entertaining the idea of a humanist Tzimisce who uses Vicissitude to help them mingle among mortals in order to study them, like an anthropologist; as you've noted, the ability to simulate aging makes maintaining the Masquerade (not interfering with &quot;the experiment&quot;) easier, and being able to adopt different physical types would allow you to personally experience the social conditions of a particular group from their perspective.<br /> <br /> But as for the other part...<br /> <br /> I think that simply proves a weakness of the Tremere clan identity rather than a strength of Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> People in this thread have been able to provide tons of examples of different archetypes Tzimisce can fulfill without Vicissitude, with at most the adjustment of a single Discipline and often not even that. Can you say the same for the Tremere? Can you take away Thaumaturgy as a clan Discipline and find ANYTHING interesting about the Tremere, without someone being able to retort &quot;X Clan can do that WAY better&quot;? The best they have managed is the Telyavelic Tremere AFAIK, which is still just Thaumaturgy-with-spirit-stuff.<br /> <br /> That they have taken the time to expand the Tzimisce identity beyond JUST Vicissitude is a credit to the clan. The Tremere are more handicapped in that &quot;vampire wizard&quot; is pretty much hardwired into their existence, and they don't really have any identity beyond &quot;splashing into other classes&quot; (to reference D&amp;D for a moment).<br /> <br /> P.S. And again, I say all that as someone who doesn't hate the Tremere and likes Thaumaturgy more than plenty of people on these forums. I just think that making an entire clan's identity wrap around one trick is a detriment to their identity and lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-18-2020, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:32:16-07:00","id":1397324,"title":"","content":"without Thaum, Tremere are absurdly good businessmen. The ventrue are old money types: slow to change, they dont take risks, and they downplay their wealth. <br /> <br /> The tremere are agressive go-getters that are always looking at new industries, they make predictions and take risks, and they show off how much cash they make with conspicuos items and show off their portfolio whenever they can. They make a competition out of it. <br /> <br /> if they didnt have Thaum, they'd still be very different from Venture, Toreador and lasomra. If Tzmisce didn't have Vicissitude they'd be ventrue clones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:53:37-07:00","id":1397330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397324#post1397324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">without Thaum, Tremere are absurdly good businessmen. The ventrue are old money types: slow to change, they dont take risks, and they downplay their wealth. <br /> <br /> The tremere are agressive go-getters that are always looking at new industries, they make predictions and take risks, and they show off how much cash they make with conspicuos items and show off their portfolio whenever they can. They make a competition out of it. <br /> <br /> if they didnt have Thaum, they'd still be very different from Venture, Toreador and lasomra. If Tzmisce didn't have Vicissitude they'd be ventrue clones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Discipline spread is still completely different, leading to an entirely different approach. Auspex means a focus on manipulating people through secrets rather than direct mental/emotional manipulation. Animalism means less human minions, possibly a preference for the countryside rather than the city: they the declining countryside gentry. And they still have the Disciplines to be transvampirists, just more exclusively mental/spiritual. They kinda become the Mekhet of VtR.<br /> <br /> And that's just Discipline spread, before adding the flavour of their clan flaw and history. I'm not serious about taking shots at the Tremere, or any clan really, but <b>if</b> a head has to roll, I'd pick Ventrue. Almost their entire identity is &quot;the (min-max) boss&quot; clan. Every other &quot;noble&quot; clan has more flavour, and just needs to be willing to take one social Discipline out-of-clan.<br /> <br /> I'd still take Tzimisce without Vicissitude AND no replacement clan Discipline over the Ventrue with three clan Disciplines. Not everything is about mechanical optimization.<br /> <br /> Also, tell me what level of Koldunic Sorcery I need, and I will give you a Tzimisce version of Blackbeard from PotC4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. I think the closest truth to the Tzimisce and Ventrue being similar is their clan flaws: one is a &quot;picky eater &quot; the other a &quot;picky sleeper.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-18-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:59:03-07:00","id":1397331,"title":"","content":"I'll admit that I haven't been filling following this thread but I don't think calling any clan an 'X clone' is ever really accurate and that applies to the Tzimisce as well.<br /> <br /> Even if you remove their flesh-crafting, the Tzimisce are distinct from the Ventrue for similar reasons as to why the Lasombra are distinct from the Ventrue even without shadow-mancy.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue were historically the warrior elite and are now old money and mercantile guilders. They've adapted to traditional institutional power and the power of the almighty dollar. The Tzimisce on the other hand are old school landed nobility.<br /> <br /> Their souls are in the land, quite literally. Their weakness alone says as much but their disciplines and outlook support it as well. They have animalism to command the beasts of the land. They have Auspex to expand their awareness over all the bounds of their territories. They mastered Koldunic Sorcery to further prove their ties to the land.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce behave like landed aristocracy. They are the land and the land is them. Whatever comes from the land is owed to them and as such all the people of their lands owe them everything, including their lives. They take up the mantle of the supernatural-religious aura that nobility and aristocracy have worked to develop for millennia which I think is quite distinct from the social darwinism and subtle control of the Lasombra or the Nobless Oblige and mercantile stewardship of the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:00:47-07:00","id":1397333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere are more handicapped in that &quot;vampire wizard&quot; is pretty much hardwired into their existence</div> </div> </div> </div>You're hilarious. How many clans can just be construed as so called &quot;tropes&quot; from their disciplines or just archetypes alone? Brujah = fighter class, Noseferatu = rogue, Toreador = bards, Venture = Paladin, Gangrel = rangers etc... see where I'm going? That notion you put out is contrived. Besides that the Tremere have already been hamfisted from their niche as the magical users of the Camarilla anyway and now we see the results of it as you insinuate- when the Tremere are ungracefuly cou de' graced, they became bland directionless railroaded due to the Second Inquisition somehow ganking their chantry that can't be seen by mortals and periodically mystically teleports for the sole reason of being undetectable- but somehow it just got drone striked.. <br /> <br /> Even then the Tremere has one of the most in-depth lore of any clans due to how they even got to achieve Vampirism and how they rose through sheer strategy and paramilitary style effectiveness. Thaumaturgy doesn't &quot;shape&quot; the Tremere, its what the Tremere shaped as a genius improvisation when they realized their Awakened magic was sundered with their turn to become undead due to the lost of their Quintessence. Why would you think only &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; only shapes the Tremere when we already have so many write-ups proving more than just that? Tremere pre-V5 where keyed strategists, tight-knit while still having inter-house conflict, intriguers galore, and one of the top Camarilla clans, taking on major clans in their beginning, and diablerizing a major character to ascend into higher legitimacy.. <br /> <br /> If it weren't even obvious enough most of the Tremere are intelligent scholars or just generally people with highly specialized skills because that's who the Tremere embrace into the clan. They have much, much more going for them obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:19:38-07:00","id":1397337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397333#post1397333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're hilarious. How many clans can just be construed as so called &quot;tropes&quot; from their disciplines or just archetypes alone? Brujah = fighter class, Noseferatu = rogue, Toreador = bards, Venture = Paladin, Gangrel = rangers etc... see where I'm going? That notion you put out is contrived. Besides that the Tremere have already been hamfisted from their niche as the magical users of the Camarilla anyway and now we see the results of it as you insinuate- when the Tremere are ungracefuly cou de' graced, they became bland directionless railroaded due to the Second Inquisition somehow ganking their chantry that can't be seen by mortals and periodically mystically teleports for the sole reason of being undetectable- but somehow it just got drone striked.. <br /> <br /> Even then the Tremere has one of the most in-depth lore of any clans due to how they even got to achieve Vampirism and how they rose through sheer strategy and paramilitary style effectiveness. Thaumaturgy doesn't &quot;shape&quot; the Tremere, its what the Tremere shaped as a genius improvisation when they realized their Awakened magic was sundered with their turn to become undead due to the lost of their Quintessence. Why would you think only &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; only shapes the Tremere when we already have so many write-ups proving more than just that? Tremere pre-V5 where keyed strategists, tight-knit while still having inter-house conflict, intriguers galore, and one of the top Camarilla clans, taking on major clans in their beginning, and diablerizing a major character to ascend into higher legitimacy.. <br /> <br /> If it weren't even obvious enough most of the Tremere are intelligent scholars or just generally people with highly specialized skills because that's who the Tremere embrace into the clan. They have much, much more going for them obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that's why I made clear that I'm not serious about attacking the Tremere. I just think these attacks are as &quot;serious&quot; as those leveled against Tzimisce-without-Vicissitude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I enjoy the Tremere lore a great deal (especially given how much it leans on the Tzimisce <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> See, the problem with the Tremere isn't that they're &quot;vampire wizards,&quot; it's that they are &quot;bland vampire D&amp;D stereotype wizards.&quot; I think the Tremere clan would have a much cooler identity if, for example, they were like a vampiric version of the Traditions; different practitioners of different blood magics, like Dur-an-Ki and Necromancy, as Houses within the clan. Then their clan identity would be more than one uber Discipline, but the internal struggles between radically different philosophies and magical theories instead of one broadly unified &quot;paradigm&quot; under a rigid hierarchy.<br /> <br /> And, TO REITERATE, I enjoy the Tremere's Hermetic themes and the hierarchical blood-cult that would come with it. But it does make it harder to play a Tremere outside the &quot;D&amp;D wizard&quot; stereotype without being an intentionally sub optimal choice, as their clan flavour is largely built on it exclusively.<br /> <br /> And note that your defence of the Tremere appeals as much to clan flavour that, strictly speaking, is more than just Thaumaturgy. The same type of argument CTPhipps and I make defending Tzimisce-without-Vicissitude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, I'm not gonna call Vicissitude-obsessed Tzimisce &quot;flesh monkeys&quot; or &quot;degenerates.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm going to call them &quot;Asakku&quot; ;P<br /> <br /> P.S. as noted, I'm working on setting up a DAV20 game, and included has been making character sheets for potential &quot;casual players.&quot; I've got 20 now, mostly by taking the 10 sheets based on &quot;clan stereotypes&quot; and flipping them. I can provide examples later to prove my point, but almost every clan can play more than one &quot;class.&quot; Tremere? Just a fighter/wizard instead of a single class <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Again, I *could* do otherwise, but why pick Tremere otherwise, if you aren't specifically in love with their lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-18-2020, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:47:29-07:00","id":1397339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397273#post1397273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be opposed to that, partly, but I really, really like Vicissitude, because it's <i>art</i>. And I really like the &quot;doctor&quot; Tzmisce (Only instead of tools he's lugging around, it's his jar of dirt)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There are so many different kinds of things you could do with Vicissitude. It's as versatile/potentially more versatile than pre-V5 thaumaturgy. You can be any kind of doctor as a Tzmisce (Auspex/Animalism help with the mental side of things; Using dominate would be a hack move) </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this is part of <i>why</i> I think Vicissitude should be simplified mechanically: because it <i>doesn't really work</i> as a static list of powers one to five.<br /> <br /> For example, how does &quot;I spend a blood and turn into a monstrous form&quot; fit the Vicissitude aesthetic? To me that feels like pure Protean/Serpentis: Vicissitude thematically is about careful surgery and gradual changes over time, not something that happens in an instant.<br /> <br /> My vision of V5 Vicissitude is straight Protean powers for Malleable Visage and &quot;warform&quot; (covers Zulo, Xaviar's man-bat thing, and Typhonic Beast), then a special Tzimisce-specific amalgam that lets you apply any of your Protean powers to other people through long and careful (and agonizing) surgery. That way Tzimisce can still have their combat potential (like shifting immediately into Zulo) without diluting the &quot;eldritch surgeon&quot; feel of fleshcrafting\u2014by having the instant combat buffs be raw Protean instead, same as the Gangrel and Setite ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:00:53-07:00","id":1397342,"title":"","content":"Whats with this weird thing among the WoD fanbase to incessantly coin almost ANYTHING with D&amp;D? Beside just both being tabletops, nothing within the spectrum of WoD is even nearly related to DnD. The Tremere are unique on their own and gauge nothing that is found in DnD. For christsake if I remember correctly in DnD you can only cast a spell a few times in a day and that's it completely. People who compare the Tremere to &quot;DnD Wizards&quot; can't even get that right since the entirety of Tremere magic relies on Blood-Magic alone, while the various &quot;Wizards/Spellcasters&quot; in DnD are entirely different (tbh I wouldn't even know that well since I barely even care for DnD). Even the Hermetics, the Awakened Tradtion faction they descended from are more developed than anything you can find in DnD by any margin. So tell me, how exactly are the Tremere &quot;bland&quot;?<br /> <br /> Also what you even suggest doesn't even make a splick of sense, why would the Tremere do different practices of Blood Magic within their clan when they all descended from one of the Mage factions most proud in how they did magic? Not only that the Tremere wouldn't need any other Magic practices in their clan because their tactical rigidness and maneuvering with their former Quintessence based Paradigm adapted to Vitae based magic is what happened them survive all these centuries. Again you tack it on as if the discipline MAKES the Tremere, but they are much more than that regardless. They don't need MORE &quot;magic&quot; based disciplines because that wouldn't be necessary. I'd even bet in an alternate universe where the Tremere ACTUALLY did have multiple magic disciplines, you'll just complain that the Tremere have too much and their snowflakey.<br /> <br /> You say you like hierarchy and Hermetic based Tremere, but then go against that by suggesting this paramilitary style clan would bother with differing Blood Magics and them not doing that is somehow &quot;bland DnD&quot;.. wut? The Tremere don't operate like a circus act (which they became in V5), they have one paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And note that your defence of the Tremere appeals as much to clan flavour that, strictly speaking, is more than just Thaumaturgy. The same type of argument CTPhipps and I make defending Tzimisce-without-Vicissitude</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the fact is that the fiats of both arguments are ironically different. You and CTPhipps want to atomize the Tzimisce to a mere &quot;Dracula&quot; stereotype and incinerate Vicissitude for their bloodline faction (that is essentially Trujah for the Tzimisce), while going on to say &quot;Tremere with only Thaumaturgy&quot; makes them a bland DnD stereotype of a sort. The fundamental difference is that Tremere are one clan entirely, while you want Tzimisce's bloodline faction to take the forefront when there isn't real sensical reason for it. The main branch of Tzimisce won't just drop Vicissitude en masse for no practical reason, its stupidity for that to even happen.<br /> <br /> You have to realize this: Old Clan Tzimisce and the Tzimisce are NOT the same, which is why the argument for &quot;Tzimisce without Vicissitude&quot; is a tired one. Tremere are what MAKE Thaumaturgy the way it is due to the way they are, so it IS part of their clan flavor- not without it as you put it. They shape it, not the other way around. The same way the Tzimisce are what MAKE Vicissitude be the way it is through the way they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-18-2020, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T13:26:51-07:00","id":1397360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397342#post1397342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the fact is that the fiats of both arguments are ironically different. You and CTPhipps want to atomize the Tzimisce to a mere &quot;Dracula&quot; stereotype and incinerate Vicissitude for their bloodline faction (that is essentially Trujah for the Tzimisce),</div> </div> </div> </div>Shaknaka, I'm going to report you to another mod if you repeat this nonsense again. I've said repeatedly I've never wanted to get rid of Vicissitude and posted what I think was going to happen to keep it and you've continued to spread this lie. You're doing it deliberately now and it's starting to tick me off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T13:51:48-07:00","id":1397366,"title":"","content":"My opinion on the various subjects?<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think that the Tremere can be done without Thaumaturgy because the Clan is based around an Archetype and if you remove that then they are losing something central. I think some Discipline are more important than others to a Clan. The Gangrel need Protean, the Nosferatu need Obfuscate, and the Toreador need Presence. I don't think Malkavians need Dominate or Ventrue need Potence but it adds to their character.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>No one actually wants to get rid of Vicissitude.</b> This is a lie being deliberately spread and I wonder who is responsible. However, every person who claims it is someone who is engaged in deliberate misinformation and it's not cool. Some people don't think the Tzimisce NEED Vicissitude and prefer the Old Clan version without it but that's different from wanting to get rid of it. All indications are the publishers may be combining the Discipline with another but it's not going away and anyone who says that is lying.<br /> <br /> 3. I don't think that the Tremere are in any way D&amp;D wizards because &quot;functional&quot; magic goes far beyond Dungeons and Dragons. I know this as a fantasy author. Ritualism and Paths are fundamentally different mechanically as well.<br /> <br /> 4. One of the major arguments here is what exactly is the importants of fluff vs. crunch. The Tremere, IN ADDITION To having Thaumaturgy, are also possessed of an extremely fascinating Clan Culture. Indeed, the Tremere and Tzimisce are the two most developed Clans in terms of NPCs, Clan Culture, and history. A large part of this being the focus given them during the Omen War during the Dark Ages. The Tremere may need Thaumaturgy but what makes them awesome is their rigid heirarchies, past sins, feuds, and houses. The same with the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 5. The shitposting has got to stop. I'm happy to keep my tongue but fundamentally <b>no one on these forums should ever put down another fan's favorite faction.</b> If you like the Brujah or you like the Baali, if you like the Sabbat or the True Hand, you are welcome here in the OPP forums. People who love High Humanity Salubri Healers are just as much vampire fans as Thin Blood Alchemists and Path of Caine Sabbat. Literally, all fans are welcome (except of <i>World of Darkness: Gypsies</i> and <i>Eternal Hearts</i>--you stay away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> 6. I don't think the Old Clan are necessarily as defined by a lack of Vicissitude as the New Clan is defined by it. If you gave the Old Clan Vicissitude then they'd not actually change that much as the lack of it was just important in the DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND book. Elsewhere, it's not really important with the Inconnu members of the faction or its history/factions since they became the basis (retroactively) of the Dark Age Tzimisce despite those having a heavy focus on Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> 7. I think what attracts me most to the Tzimisce in general (and not just the Old Clan) is the NPCs: Radu, Vladimir Rustovich, Dracula, Lambach Ruthven, and Shaagra are some of the most interesting characters in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:32:00-07:00","id":1397379,"title":"","content":"First I just wanna throw it out there that Tremere Thaumaturgy encapsulates the mostly european occult philosophy/faith of Hermeticism. Of which european and middle eastern alchemy stems, which in turn evolved into modern science. Your archtypical DnD wizard draws inspiration from Hermeticism/Odin (the latter inspiring gandalf) but the DnD wizard does not really explicitly attach itself to this and is rather muddled/philosophically agnostic, whilst the Tremere explicitly do attach themselves, just as the settites are explicitly attached to Gnosticism. In WoD, the beliefs of the mage are more prominent than the results. If the Tremere could not use magic, their philosophy would still shape them. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude 1-5 is fine. Balance wise you should rea\u013aly hold off on making a mod permanent unless you can spend several turns shaping (a quick grab and yank shouldnt be permanent on a vampire) <br /> <br /> Vicissitude 4 and 5 would make a lot more sense if you could take the concepts and apply it to others. Say Zulo is an art of canibalizing viscera and turning it into an explosive muscular/bone growth. While the human body needs organs to live and can't really pull this off to the degree of vampires (+3/3/3 would certainly kill them) The Tzmisce can provide minor boosts (+1/1/1) to ghouls without serious health risks (appearance probably goes to 1, your organs are at a far greater risks of failure if you dont have blood) or boost a ghoul/vampire with .+2/2/2 for a short time (The vampire loses the boost on rising the next night, the ghoul dies after an uncertain time unless treated)<br /> <br /> bloodform, meanwhile... That's when you go beyond the need to shape with your hands. Thats some peak body knowledge right there. lots of ideas, but a big one would be to set your zulo ghouls up to disolve to blood when they die for the sake of keeping secrets. <br /> <br /> Vis 1-5 are like the limits of what you can do. I'd say you learn specific procedures like rituals and... ever notice this happens when the tzmisce come up? we all get carried away. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude becoming protean would be really silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:38:35-07:00","id":1397382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397379#post1397379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vicissitude becoming protean would be really silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to explain how because literally it would be, &quot;Alternate Powers under an Umbrella Discipline.&quot; It would be called Protean because Protean means shape-changing.<br /> <br /> You could just as easily put Protean under Vicissitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:53:46-07:00","id":1397385,"title":"","content":"If you just go by the names it makes a bit of sense to merge them (they do connotate different things, but they are similar enough) But y'know, North Korea isn't a republic. <br /> <br /> Should we merge Dominate with Presence? Does sailing make for good plane piloting? Is makeup the same thing as cosmetic surgery?<br /> <br /> <i>also the 5 power limit makes it really, really unwise to merge disciplines. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T15:20:42-07:00","id":1397393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397385#post1397385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just go by the names it makes a bit of sense to merge them (they do connotate different things, but they are similar enough) But y'know, North Korea isn't a republic.<br /> <br /> Should we merge Dominate with Presence? Does sailing make for good plane piloting? Is makeup the same thing as cosmetic surgery?<br /> <br /> <i>also the 5 power limit makes it really, really unwise to merge disciplines. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>If there was the option of having multiple powers of the same Discipline, I'd absolutely say merge Dominate and Presence and rename it &quot;Majesty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sadly, you can't so it's the odd Discipline out.<br /> <br /> I also think they should remove the barrier and allow people to have as many alternate powers of a Discipline as they want.<br /> <br /> Personally, I approve of Tzimisce having access to Protean and Gangrel having access to Vicissitude. Gangrel are supposed to be master-shapeshifters, why shouldn't they be able to look like other people as well as animals? Also, what loser among the Tzimisce can't become a wolf or mist?<br /> <br /> But we won't know until the Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-18-2020, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T23:42:26-07:00","id":1397460,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't meant to make shit up as they go along. They're not mages. They're not supposed to be picking and choosing how they 'level up' every time as if they had skyrim's perk tree out in front of them. <br /> <br /> The old system of going 1,2,3,4,5 was elegant, and you could do whatever you wanted at 6+ because of six and above were for old characters that knew exactly what they were doing (Lore wise we could say ratings of 1-5 are normal and level 6 + Transcendant wonder powers where your soul excedes the normal confines of reality and the imposed 1-5 discipline plan; Getting a six in anything is essentially 'breaking free' and was reason enough to kill for) <br /> <br /> Fluff wise, it's bad, mechanically, it's bad. It just leads to choice paralysis (and leaves no incentive to diablerise) Not to mention many multi-feature powers in VTM have been split up so you can &quot;have fun choosing&quot; between something that used to be a complete plackage (you'd spend three levels in auspex just getting what used to be auspex 1) or in the case of new ones you must choose between hyper specific alternatives (Celerity 3: Do I learn to move really really fast specifically towards a person or do I learn to move that fast in any direction but not attack? Because clearly we're roleplaying in a videogame) <br /> <br /> Loosely speaking It's better to have 30 linear disciplines (with seven in regular use and I'd say another 2 aren't rare) that have five powers each that you don't cherrypick*, than it is to have 10 disciplines (9 in regular use with 1 not rare) with a pick and mix of 15 powers each (150 total) <br /> <br /> *Ironically Sorcery is simplified in V5 when it's the one thing that by it's nature should be complicated. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overchoice#:~:text=Overchoice%20or%20choice%20overload%20is,his%201970%20book%2C%20Future%20Shock.\" target=\"_blank\">It seems researchers would agree with me</a>; Choice like this is bad. <br /> <br /> Having protean and having players struggling to pick between protean powers and viccissitude powers and serpentis powers and Visceraticka powers and Thanatosis powers (if that still exists) and having them plan out an order for them to get the powers they want is a far bigger pain than just choosing between Protean, Vicissitude, Serpentis, Visceraticka and thanatosis (A choice made when you choose your clan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T23:53:50-07:00","id":1397462,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the idea of vampires being &quot;typical&quot; and having a 1-2-3-4-5 system that's universal is ridiculous. They're supernatural entities gaining power FROM THE BLOOD. It should be customized and personalized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having protean and having players struggling to pick between protean powers and viccissitude powers and serpentis powers and Visceraticka powers and Thanatosis powers (if that still exists) and having them plan out an order for them to get the powers they want is a far bigger pain than just choosing between Protean, Vicissitude, Serpentis, Visceraticka and thanatosis (A choice made when you choose your clan) </div> </div> </div>I think it's far more fun as you can customize your vampire much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T00:21:05-07:00","id":1397467,"title":"","content":"It isn't.<br /> The physical disciplines have a clear progression of 1,2,3,4,5<br /> Auspex, Dominate, obfuscate, chimestry, Vicissitude have perfectly logical progressions from 1-5<br /> Presence is a bit of an outlier in having a loose logic to the order. Obtenebration is about the same. These are rare weaknesses.<br /> Thaumaturgy and necromancy work by their own rules, and they make perfect sense (except the primary/secondary path system)<br /> Protean... Well, you can admire that it's consistent with it's relatives (Serpentis, Visceraticka, Thanatosis) in that the first power is sensory, the second power is a weapon/tool, the third power is a survival skill, the fourth is a useful transformation and the 5th is a big travel-centric transformation (Thanatosis might be a bit of an outlier in some cases). Protean is literally about being able to change fast and frequently so it isn't that big of a deal that it doesn't have a perfect progressive linup.<br /> <br /> I've not gone through every disciplines but more of them are in the second category than the third and very few powers are in a protean-like very-loose setup. <br /> <br /> How does getting power from the blood justify a choice of super jump or nasty punch? That's way sillier. V5 powers are so absurdly specific that I can't really see this argument going your way. .<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> And again, you might personally like choice, but most people, especially new people, will suffer from overchoice. A lot of people avoid casters in DnD because they don't want to build spell lists, they don't gain joy from building a spell plan after hours of reading through disconnected powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-19-2020, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T01:28:12-07:00","id":1397470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397467#post1397467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't.<br /> The physical disciplines have a clear progression of 1,2,3,4,5</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. They have an utterly arbitrary progression most of them. Like what does Mist have to do with Bats, Sleeping in the Earth, and Claws vs. Red Eyes.<br /> <br /> This is a matter of opinion but Zulo Form and Giant Man Bat are not really related to Skin Changing either.<br /> <br /> Hence why its good to have options.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T01:58:49-07:00","id":1397473,"title":"","content":"The skill tree disciplines is a horrible design<ul><li>It doesnt allow you to pick more than 5 powers per discipline so it\u00b4s a limitating factor</li> <li>It is clear wich powers are superior becuase a lot of powers are just fillers leading to dominant strategies</li> <li>Everything is nerfed and high cost to use due rouse checks being fucking random.</li> <li>Few bucks allows you to buy a raufoss that deals agg+5 and allows you to attack at distance wich is way more than what any discipline can do</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Defined 1-5 levels for simplicity shake with is the great advantaje of masquerade over other gamelines + combo disciplines for those who want customization should have been the way to go","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 06-19-2020, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T02:31:40-07:00","id":1397478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397470#post1397470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they don't. They have an utterly arbitrary progression most of them. Like what does Mist have to do with Bats, Sleeping in the Earth, and Claws vs. Red Eyes.<br /> <br /> This is a matter of opinion but Zulo Form and Giant Man Bat are not really related to Skin Changing either.<br /> <br /> Hence why its good to have options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're picking on the outliers, not the norm.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Common</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Uncommon</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Clan Specific</span><br /> <br /> <b>Perfect progression:<br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Celerity, Fortitude, Potence.</span> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Some thaumaturgy paths</span>)<br /> Super logical progression that're arguably or near-perfect<br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate</span>, <span style=\"color:#800080\">Chimestry</span>, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, </span><span style=\"color:#800080\">Vicissitude</span><br /> Seemingly Flawed partial progression:<br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Animalism</span><span style=\"color:#800080\">, Dementation, Quietus</span> </b>(version depending)<br /> <b>Mostly arbitrary</b> (But still abiding by certain princibles, like the first power being broadly applicable and the latter powers being highly specialised, impressive and very powerful).<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#008000\">Presence</span>, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Protean</span> <span style=\"color:#800080\">and Serpentis</span>, <span style=\"color:#800080\">Obtenebration</span>. </b><br /> <br /> Out of the common Eight disciplines, three are perfect, three are really good (if not perfect), and two need work. To my knowledge there is a grand total of one canonical bloodline that doesn't have at least two common disciplines in-clan (Kiasyd, I won't count Maegar) and, honestly, clan specifics are weird things that can do with more leeway.<br /> <br /> What's better; To have choose your own unique set of powers, or to use the same powers everyone else has in a way suited uniquely to you?<br /> Consider the impact this would have on clan culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T03:38:53-07:00","id":1397489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397462#post1397462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the idea of vampires being &quot;typical&quot; and having a 1-2-3-4-5 system that's universal is ridiculous. They're supernatural entities gaining power FROM THE BLOOD. It should be customized and personalized.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's far more fun as you can customize your vampire much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is going to disagree with you. They say Vampires and their special powers are so free to use because it is a fix standard what you can use when at which disciple and only the mightiest and the thin bloods can go to change something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T05:14:26-07:00","id":1397494,"title":"","content":"In one view, we could say that vampires aren't developing powers, they're unlocking potential. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Havent mentioned it, but I feel kinda resentful that one can describe the price as 'of the old clan' and expect someone in the camarilla know what that means. They're supposed to be a rare fringe bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T06:41:21-07:00","id":1397497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397494#post1397494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havent mentioned it, but I feel kinda resentful that one can describe the price as 'of the old clan' and expect someone in the camarilla know what that means. They're supposed to be a rare fringe bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I suspect that the term may refer to the clan as whole or that it means Tzimisce Antitribu. Assuming they even are Tzimisce, although the alternatives are dubious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-19-2020, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T10:33:10-07:00","id":1397547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397494#post1397494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havent mentioned it, but I feel kinda resentful that one can describe the price as 'of the old clan' and expect someone in the camarilla know what that means. They're supposed to be a rare fringe bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Spencer said, I doubt most Camarilla know the difference between &quot;Old Clan Tzimisce&quot; and &quot;Normal Tzimisce&quot;, or have any idea what a &quot;Koldun&quot; is.<br /> <br /> My guess is that &quot;the Old Clan&quot; is just a euphemism for the clan as a whole, like how Lasombra are &quot;Magisters&quot; or Torries are &quot;the Clan of Roses&quot;. Even non-Tzimisce refer to the Tzimisce Antediluvian as &quot;the Eldest&quot;, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T11:26:28-07:00","id":1397554,"title":"","content":"It isn't a euphemism as far as I know; those are listed, and Camarilla being non-religious (as a whole) aren't telling their neonates about Antideluvians. So it's just an assertion that old clan Tzmisce are super well known and popular...<br /> <br /> they could've easily rolled with with &quot;...of the Old Clan, A bloodline of the Tzmisce that have eschewed the fleshshaping discipline of Vicissitude&quot; and it would've worked fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T11:40:51-07:00","id":1397556,"title":"","content":"they should just stop presenting fluff through in-character expository dialogue/monologues,<br /> it's off-putting most of the time,<br /> it even ruins the image we have about vampires (especially elders),<br /> makes them sound all cringy for supposedly charismatic social predators","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T12:27:35-07:00","id":1397557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397554#post1397554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't a euphemism as far as I know; those are listed, and Camarilla being non-religious (as a whole) aren't telling their neonates about Antideluvians. So it's just an assertion that old clan Tzmisce are super well known and popular...<br /> <br /> they could've easily rolled with with &quot;...of the Old Clan, A bloodline of the Tzmisce that have eschewed the fleshshaping discipline of Vicissitude&quot; and it would've worked fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where has it been listed? The clan hasn't been written up for V5. And the detail that they eschewed Vicissitude isn't really pertinent to the scant instances the &quot;Old Clan&quot; is mentioned. In the case of topic of this thread, the point is that Shibasaki doesn't have an issue with Tremere in spite of her clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T12:50:44-07:00","id":1397560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397497#post1397497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I suspect that the term may refer to the clan as whole or that it means Tzimisce Antitribu. Assuming they even are Tzimisce, although the alternatives are dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Old Clan are the Tzimisce Antitribu. They're not hidden like the True Brujah.<br /> <br /> Even then, a Tremere would know about the Old Clan where another vampire wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T13:11:35-07:00","id":1397563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397557#post1397557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where has it been listed? The clan hasn't been written up for V5. And the detail that they eschewed Vicissitude isn't really pertinent to the scant instances the &quot;Old Clan&quot; is mentioned. In the case of topic of this thread, the point is that Shibasaki doesn't have an issue with Tremere in spite of her clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>In every edition till now every clan has came with a number of nicknames and the Tzmisce as a whole have never so far been called the 'Old clan'. Sure, maybe they could throw it in there, they did give &quot;Velocitus&quot; to celerity after all (I'll let you guess my thoughts on that) but &quot;old clan&quot; has always been a bunch of double weirdo tzmisce that don't fleshcraft, it'd be really weird if the whole clan started calling itself after a tiny group within them. Imagine you started calling the United States of America as California, or started thinking all of Britain became Wales, or perhaps the entirity of italy became Vatican city. Perhaps the Entirity of the LGBTQ community decided they'll go by just L. Old clan means Old clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-19-2020, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[