e non-vicissitide bloodline,<br /> first time I saw it was in v20<br /> <br /> weren't they called Ordea League before?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember them from DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND despite the fact the Old Clan Tzimisce are mostly Inconnu not Black Hand. Presumably the ones in the True Hand REALLY hate Vicissitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T14:36:10-07:00","id":1397581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397573#post1397573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember them from DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND despite the fact the Old Clan Tzimisce are mostly Inconnu not Black Hand. Presumably the ones in the True Hand REALLY hate Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>ah yeah, totally forgot about that one...I wonder why","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:51:51-07:00","id":1397745,"title":"","content":"Based on the Tokyo bit and an offhand reference in the story included in Chicago by Night, it\u2019s pretty clear to me that \u201cOld Clan\u201d now just means Tzimisce outside the Sabbat. This is the logical conclusion of both V5 design principles and some general trends going back to V3, which veered pretty hard away from how Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand presented things, including the idea that Vicissitude wasn\u2019t something the clan always had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:53:47-07:00","id":1398264,"title":"","content":"Yay, I finally finished reading all the topic.<br /> <br /> 1. A cookie for me<br /> 1b. I hate CTPhipps because now I want to read Necroscope and I don't have the time (\u256f\u00b0\u25a1\u00b0\uff09\u256f\ufe35 \u253b\u2501\u253b<br /> <br /> 2. There're a lot of things I'd like to say about the clans since there's a really deep discussion about them. But it's kinda late and I'm sleepy so that's not for now.<br /> <br /> 3. A thing I explicitly love of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> 's writeups is that what is not said but only implied is often more interesting than what is said.<br /> Like when, in BJD he nonchalantly hinted the Wan-kuei offed the Della Passaglia since they had outlived their utility (you stupid sexy Flanders...)<br /> There's a little detail here than no one pointed up.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, <b>there is a strong Camarilla presence in Tokyo</b>, but I\u2019ve no idea if they send word back to the Inner Circle or the Justicars. I know in this age, everywhere is accessible, but Tokyo and Japan in general are so technology-dependent, it now feels utterly cut off with Inquisition eyes on our emails and messages. This makes the city pretty autonomous.<br /> [...]<br /> <br /> If anyone is <b>in charge </b>of this domain it\u2019s Mayumi Shibasaki. <b>She doesn\u2019t rule</b>, technically, but ensures <b>order is kept</b> and <b>tribute flows upstream</b>. <b>She\u2019s of the Old Clan</b>, so she says, but <b>has no issues with the Tremere</b>. Like I said, Tokyo is weird. </div> </div> </div>Nowhere it says that Shibasaki is Prince (or Daimyo? Do we still have regional titles in V5?).<br /> It says that she doesn't rule, so she's no prince.<br /> Actually is even says that even if there's a strong Camarilla (enforced Traditions, working Elysium etc) they <u>may</u> not report to the top brass. It says she's tecnically in charge of the domain, but not that she's in charge. Again, Shibasaki is no prince.<br /> She makes sure the order is kept (and this means enforcing the Traditions, but you don't really need a prince for that, only someone with a head on their shoulders and a serious case of &quot;don't fuck with me&quot;) and that tribute flows... I think in this case it means either blood or Boons, and really you don't need a prince for that either (flowing Boons only need a working Elysium). Shibasaki is an Elder, and a very connected one, and loves order.<br /> Also it says she's of the Old Clan. Now, I find unlikely they started calling all the Tzim, the Old Clan. I don't totally rule it out since I remember somewhere (probably TbN or DA Europe) the Transylvania being called &quot;the old country&quot;, but for now let's keep Shibaraki in the Old Clan camp. Our beloved Dominate/Animalism/Auspex overlords.<br /> She's Old Clan, but doesn't hate Tremere. Why, since all the old and Elder Tzimisce seems to have a feud with the Warlocks?<br /> (the young too, but they don't know why)<br /> It could be that Shibaraki's politic is to be above Clans politicking.<br /> <br /> So, we have a city where an Elder of the Old Clan Tzimisce is the one keeping the order, but not claiming praxis. She's powerful, since no one defies her will (but she still not claims praxis). Also she seems to not harbour resentment over Tremere or just doesn't care about them.<br /> And finally the city follows the Camarilla's Traditions (but may be out of the Ivory Tower's chain of command).<br /> <br /> Now, to me it seems like a Inconnu Monitor of the Old Clan Tzimisce just stepped in and decided to do something more than just overseeing. She keeps the society working, but stops petty squabbles for praxis, ensuring order. And for whatever reason 300 yo Elders relocate (or are forced to relocate) somewhere else while a weird &quot;energy&quot; (Blood Magic? Spirits? A frigging high-level Discipline [my money on Animalism]?) keeps the average Joe Leech from frenzing in the streets.<br /> The city may be autonomous or not. It doesn't say anywhere that it is.<br /> Personally I think that the city is firm in the Camarilla camp.<br /> But in the case it isn't, the Camarilla's Inner Circle may be tolerating it because they plainly don't care as long as the Traditions are enforced, <i><u>OR</u></i> they are buying time before making their move (unlikely since the system seems in place and working by a lot of time) <u><i>OR</i></u> they don't dare to make a move against the Inconnu as long as they don't claim outright indipendence for the city (a-la Los Angeles).<br /> The point is that there's a Inconnu that decided to stop monitoring and is doing &quot;something&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3b. I may be totally off course with the above statement, but I still love the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":24483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","user":"SalamanDer","date":".  typos 06-23-2020, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:46:40-07:00","id":1398520,"title":"","content":"Matthew Dawkins, who wrote that bit, has confirmed that she\u2019s meant to be the Tzimisce prince of Tokyo. Also, Old Clan seems to be the generic designator for Tzimisce outside the Sabbat and not a reference to what the term meant in previous editions. Remember this edition has done away with the generic term <i>antitribu</i>.<br /> <br /> So she\u2019s probably a run-of-the-mill Tzimisce who happens to be prince of Tokyo, because why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:56:08-07:00","id":1398521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398520#post1398520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matthew Dawkins, who wrote that bit, has confirmed that she\u2019s meant to be the Tzimisce prince of Tokyo. Also, Old Clan seems to be the generic designator for Tzimisce outside the Sabbat and not a reference to what the term meant in previous editions. Remember this edition has done away with the generic term <i>antitribu</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a 5th Edition addition.<br /> <br /> Old Clan was always what the Tzimisce were called outside of the Sabbat. Unlike the Lasombra, they never had an Antitribu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So she\u2019s probably a run-of-the-mill Tzimisce who happens to be prince of Tokyo, because why not. </div> </div> </div>Mind you, 99.99% of all Tzimisce not part of the Sabbat are going to be Old Clan Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T21:32:39-07:00","id":1398528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398521#post1398521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't a 5th Edition addition.<br /> <br /> Old Clan was always what the Tzimisce were called outside of the Sabbat. Unlike the Lasombra, they never had an Antitribu.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you, 99.99% of all Tzimisce not part of the Sabbat are going to be Old Clan Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Anarch Tzimisce in V20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T23:55:22-07:00","id":1398535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398528#post1398528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the Anarch Tzimisce in V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the .01 percent. The non-Tzimisce were depicted as almost all part of either the Inconnu or True Black Hand as well as Old Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T08:02:20-07:00","id":1398601,"title":"","content":"It's also hinted that there's one Tzimisce Archon. One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T14:17:35-07:00","id":1398641,"title":"","content":"Now, in V20, &quot;Old clan&quot; are listed as a Tzmisce bloodline without vicissitude. It's a bloodline, not a cultural classification. <br /> <br /> Also I've always thought they'd look at allegiance like this:<br /> <br /> Autark: You mean he has his own place? Admirable. <br /> Anarch: If they can get wild dogs to respect their territory, I can respect them<br /> Camarilla: NO, NO, NO! <br /> Sabbat: A messy lot. Some refinement, more vulgarity. <br /> Inconnu: Like a normal Tzmisce but more mysterious<br /> TBH: Like a normal Tzmisce but with a cool clubhouse.<br /> Laibon: An exotic guest! We can trade notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T15:14:30-07:00","id":1398650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398641#post1398641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in V20, &quot;Old clan&quot; are listed as a Tzmisce bloodline without vicissitude. It's a bloodline, not a cultural classification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, superior beings as they may be, they don't hate their poorer less refined brethren.<br /> <br /> *sips tea while wearing monocle*<br /> <br /> Merely believe they need culling.<br /> <br /> JK.<br /> <br /> I think that the in-story justification is the Old Clan Tzimisce were original &quot;normal&quot; Tzimisce with Vicissitude but used Blood Sorcery to remove it due to realizing it was being used by the Eldest to control them. This is conjecture from a bunch of clues, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:33:49-07:00","id":1398729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398650#post1398650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Merely believe they need culling.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of vampires from nearly all clans have the idea that a lot of their members should be culled. Protect the brand, reduce competition. I think the only exception is the Nosferatu, who want as many bloodbags between themselves and the niktuku as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T16:19:51-07:00","id":1398891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1397366#post1397366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on the various subjects?<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think that the Tremere can be done without Thaumaturgy because the Clan is based around an Archetype and if you remove that then they are losing something central. I think some Discipline are more important than others to a Clan. The Gangrel need Protean, the Nosferatu need Obfuscate, and the Toreador need Presence. I don't think Malkavians need Dominate or Ventrue need Potence but it adds to their character.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>No one actually wants to get rid of Vicissitude.</b> This is a lie being deliberately spread and I wonder who is responsible. However, every person who claims it is someone who is engaged in deliberate misinformation and it's not cool. Some people don't think the Tzimisce NEED Vicissitude and prefer the Old Clan version without it but that's different from wanting to get rid of it. All indications are the publishers may be combining the Discipline with another but it's not going away and anyone who says that is lying.<br /> <br /> 3. I don't think that the Tremere are in any way D&amp;D wizards because &quot;functional&quot; magic goes far beyond Dungeons and Dragons. I know this as a fantasy author. Ritualism and Paths are fundamentally different mechanically as well.<br /> <br /> 4. One of the major arguments here is what exactly is the importants of fluff vs. crunch. The Tremere, IN ADDITION To having Thaumaturgy, are also possessed of an extremely fascinating Clan Culture. Indeed, the Tremere and Tzimisce are the two most developed Clans in terms of NPCs, Clan Culture, and history. A large part of this being the focus given them during the Omen War during the Dark Ages. The Tremere may need Thaumaturgy but what makes them awesome is their rigid heirarchies, past sins, feuds, and houses. The same with the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 5. The shitposting has got to stop. I'm happy to keep my tongue but fundamentally <b>no one on these forums should ever put down another fan's favorite faction.</b> If you like the Brujah or you like the Baali, if you like the Sabbat or the True Hand, you are welcome here in the OPP forums. People who love High Humanity Salubri Healers are just as much vampire fans as Thin Blood Alchemists and Path of Caine Sabbat. Literally, all fans are welcome (except of <i>World of Darkness: Gypsies</i> and <i>Eternal Hearts</i>--you stay away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> 6. I don't think the Old Clan are necessarily as defined by a lack of Vicissitude as the New Clan is defined by it. If you gave the Old Clan Vicissitude then they'd not actually change that much as the lack of it was just important in the DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND book. Elsewhere, it's not really important with the Inconnu members of the faction or its history/factions since they became the basis (retroactively) of the Dark Age Tzimisce despite those having a heavy focus on Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> 7. I think what attracts me most to the Tzimisce in general (and not just the Old Clan) is the NPCs: Radu, Vladimir Rustovich, Dracula, Lambach Ruthven, and Shaagra are some of the most interesting characters in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree almost a 100% with this post. Thanks a lot for having written it.<br /> <br /> Except...<br /> 5) I have both Eternal Hearts and WoD: G... and have several times thought about re-reading them to dissect them and try to find a sliver of something good in their pages. I guess I should renounce my heresy and commit to stop sinning... (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> 7) I don't know who Shaagra is, but I love all the other Tzimisce characters you have mentioned. Oh, I specially love... the Dracon? The one that lived in Constantinople with the Tzimisce monks...?<br /> <br /> (Have I mentioned I absolutely LOVE the Tismanu, the Slavic vampire priests in The Ordo Dracul and would LOVE to translate them into Masquerade terms?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T17:28:41-07:00","id":1398902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398891#post1398891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Have I mentioned I absolutely LOVE the Tismanu, the Slavic vampire priests in The Ordo Dracul and would LOVE to translate them into Masquerade terms?)</div> </div> </div> </div>To which sect would they belong? Geographically, I would think Sabbat or independent Tzimisce, but I can't see them being tolerated by either. Maybe in the Camarilla as principals of faith?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:55:57-07:00","id":1398930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398902#post1398902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To which sect would they belong? Geographically, I would think Sabbat or independent Tzimisce, but I can't see them being tolerated by either. Maybe in the Camarilla as principals of faith?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure... They would be interesting as Principals of Faith, that's for sure... Time to check my Ordo Dracul sourcebook and my Vampire Translation Guide...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:17:05-07:00","id":1399115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1398521#post1398521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a 5th Edition addition.<br /> <br /> Old Clan was always what the Tzimisce were called outside of the Sabbat. Unlike the Lasombra, they never had an Antitribu.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not that simple, as the \u201cOld Clan\u201d was originally presented as a separate bloodline with different disciplines, which the line has been walking back from since then. It is an evolution of the concept to say that the Old Clan is a political designation like Red Nosferatu or Hellenic Brujah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, 99.99% of all Tzimisce not part of the Sabbat are going to be Old Clan Tzimisce. </div> </div> </div>If the Old Clan are the non-Sabbat Tzimisce, why would they only make up 99.99% of Tzimisce outside the Sabbat? That figure seems about 0.01% off.<br /> <br /> In any case, the real innovation in V5 seems to be finally getting over the notion, which every prior edition kept trying to sell us, that the Tzimisce are universally too edgelordy to be interested in Camarilla membership, even though that\u2019s the obvious allegiance for those who reject the Sabbat and prefer to play up their clan\u2019s noble heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-26-2020, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:23:24-07:00","id":1399116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399115#post1399115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Old Clan are the non-Sabbat Tzimisce, why would they only make up 99.99% of Tzimisce outside the Sabbat? That figure seems about 0.01% off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Sabbat Tzmisce are infected with Vicissitude and thus slaves of the Eldest. There's also no Camarilla Tzimisce because they have nothing to offer that the Inconnu or Black Hand doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:31:05-07:00","id":1399119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399116#post1399116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the Sabbat Tzmisce are infected with Vicissitude and thus slaves of the Eldest. There's also no Camarilla Tzimisce because they have nothing to offer that the Inconnu or Black Hand doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s just repeating stuff from last edition, none of which may still be true. I will absolutely astonished if the Old Clan designation in V5 has anything to do with what disciplines they practice. Also, the Inconnu and Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra are not about to factor into Tzimisce sect choices in V5, as they have not been mentioned to date, and one of the main design principles of V5 is decoupling clan from sect, so that they follow the same rules regardless of their allegiance, and so that characters of any clan can be in any sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T13:06:20-07:00","id":1399125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399115#post1399115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, the real innovation in V5 seems to be finally getting over the notion, which every prior edition kept trying to sell us, that the Tzimisce are universally too edgelordy to be interested in Camarilla membership, even though that\u2019s the obvious allegiance for those who reject the Sabbat and prefer to play up their clan\u2019s noble heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, the innovation is the fact that &quot;noble heritage&quot; can work in the Camarilla (assuming it's the case, which I highly doubt)<br /> <br /> in previous editions (specifically Revised and 2nd ed), Camarilla was not the choice for those who wanted to keep playing Kings,<br /> for that, you had to go sabbat or independant,<br /> <br /> not only the Tzimisce, but also the Ventrue,<br /> those who held onto their feudal mindsets became ventrue antitribu and allied to the Tzimisce<br /> <br /> and, contrary to what most players think, the sabbat Tzimisce still played kings,<br /> which is probably why alot of antitribu still sold out to the lasombra despite the abuses<br /> <br /> even in modern nights, you had neofeudalists,<br /> and other tzimisce officials pushing to allow tzimisce to hold domain officially,<br /> if it weren't for the lasombra, they would've gotten it<br /> <br /> <br /> I get why people get confused about this,<br /> but it's important to remember that the Camarilla party line was to hide from humanity, and the sabbat one was to lord over it,<br /> <br /> most sabbat shared that stance, they just didn't agree on the timing,<br /> some wanted it now, others were fine waiting for the right time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-26-2020, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T19:38:27-07:00","id":1399194,"title":"","content":"Yep, the Tzimisce and most of the Sabbat want to usher in the time when Vampires ruled semi-openly before the everything got fudged when they utilized mortal inquisitors to kill eachother- which allowed the manipulated proxied hunters to wizen up to what was going on and begin the &quot;First&quot; Inquisition in the Dark Ages. Atleast from what I remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T23:23:58-07:00","id":1399518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399125#post1399125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, the innovation is the fact that &quot;noble heritage&quot; can work in the Camarilla (assuming it's the case, which I highly doubt).</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s the sect most concerned with purity of lineage, tradition, and aristocracy. Most of the Traditions serve no purpose other than to enshrine the traditional rights of elders as exclusive to princes within their domain. Princedom in the Camarilla isn\u2019t quite the unaccountable autarchy it was in the medieval era, but it\u2019s the next best thing, and the Camarilla remains the most feudal sect in terms of structure. <br /> <br /> Ruling openly over mortals isn\u2019t what I was talking about, nor do I see that as important to the Tzimisce clan identity. Even then, the Camarilla holds the most influence over mortal institutions. The Sabbat\u2019s throwback institutions were never ostensibly about rulership but holy knighthood etc. it was always the Church to the Camarilla\u2019s secular aristocracy. The entire orientation was different, along with the politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T00:06:38-07:00","id":1399525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399518#post1399518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s the sect most concerned with purity of lineage, tradition, and aristocracy. Most of the Traditions serve no purpose other than to enshrine the traditional rights of elders as exclusive to princes within their domain. Princedom in the Camarilla isn\u2019t quite the unaccountable autarchy it was in the medieval era, but it\u2019s the next best thing, and the Camarilla remains the most feudal sect in terms of structure.<br /> <br /> Ruling openly over mortals isn\u2019t what I was talking about, nor do I see that as important to the Tzimisce clan identity. Even then, the Camarilla holds the most influence over mortal institutions. The Sabbat\u2019s throwback institutions were never ostensibly about rulership but holy knighthood etc. it was always the Church to the Camarilla\u2019s secular aristocracy. The entire orientation was different, along with the politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of points:<br /> <br /> 1. The big issue for the Tzimisce is the Tremere's place enshrined in its halls.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat's use of clerical investiture was meant to be IRONIC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T02:39:08-07:00","id":1399534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399518#post1399518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ruling openly over mortals isn\u2019t what I was talking about, nor do I see that as important to the Tzimisce clan identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>it isn't important? ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> see? Tzimisce are just Ventrue with Vicissitude)<br /> <br /> alright, let's say you are right and it isn't important,<br /> then explain these to me:<br /> <br /> - where did sabbat get their &quot;lord over humanity&quot; shtick? was it the lasombra? cause it sure wasn't the Brujah<br /> - what's the purpose of the oradea league? (Independants)<br /> - what's with Tzimisce neofeudalists<br /> - Tzimisce having whole villages of ghouls<br /> - Tzimisce ruling over latin america as Aztec gods?<br /> - that regency canditate that wanted offically recognized domains for Tzimisce?<br /> - the voivodes and whatever equivalent they have to the amici noctis<br /> <br /> how is that not important to their identity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat\u2019s throwback institutions were never ostensibly about rulership but holy knighthood etc. it was always the Church to the Camarilla\u2019s secular aristocracy. The entire orientation was different, along with the politics. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you're talking about the clergy or something else,<br /> <br /> neofeudalists aren't part of the clergy,<br /> neither are paths of enlightenment, black hand, the amici noctis, the loyalists, the blood cults and whatever elder holds authority without being a Bishop<br /> <br /> and the sabbat consistory is not restricted to clergy members<br /> <br /> not that it matters, since, unlike the Camarilla, the clergy doesn't recognize the masquerade in any official capacity,<br /> so neofeudalists and cults and shit are...well, legal,<br /> the Archbishops can't and don't act against them on grounds of protecting the masquerade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-28-2020, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T03:07:55-07:00","id":1399545,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't see what Ventrue and Tzimisce have in common other than they're both &quot;noble&quot; clans. It seems a very shallow comparison.<br /> <br /> Like saying, &quot;Giovanni are just Ventrue with Necromancy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T03:28:41-07:00","id":1399550,"title":"","content":"Manners? check. <br /> Conservatism? check. <br /> castles? check<br /> a lot of servants? check<br /> a weakness centred around needing to keep things close to you? check. <br /> <br /> I don't see how you can insist they are so different. <br /> <br /> and obviously, the Giovanni are Tremere with necromancy, not ventrue. All the other slight differences there are in relation to the two disciplines and their impact on behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T11:53:35-07:00","id":1399632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manners? check.<br /> Conservatism? check.<br /> castles? check<br /> a lot of servants? check<br /> a weakness centred around needing to keep things close to you? check</div> </div> </div> </div>That can literally be half the clans of VTM though. <br /> Tzimisce are wildly different from the Venture, maybe Old Clan is similar to the Venture.. but other than that I don't see the similarities despite surface level things you mentioned. Actually scratch VTM clans, almost any Vampire in fiction can have those things you mentioned. But the Tzimisce have wildly different modus operandi than the Venture entirely. Besides the Venture nowadays aren't really the lordly type, their more &quot;merchants&quot; now in the Final Nights with their supreme influence and build up in modern corporatism/finance. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T12:42:43-07:00","id":1399637,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that the 'Prince' of Tokyo isn't a Cainite at all. Just masquerading as one in order to join the Camarilla and have access to their resources. End of the day the SI don't care what type of vampire you are when they set you on fire. <br /> <br /> As flawed KotE was, I still don't think it is right to throw out the concept and I still think there is room for the second breath etc. to be included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T12:59:51-07:00","id":1399639,"title":"","content":"Not really. Sure, any individual vampire can be a well mannered conservative with a castle and lots of servants who needs to keep things close. But we have clans specifically to capture archtypes: The Ventrue are predominantly Old money types, the Tremere are new money types, Toreador are the 'liberal elite' that poor conservatives are trained to hate so much, Gangrel are rural, Nosferatu are the people who got rich through unpleasant means... and brujah are a mess in more ways than one.Malkavians stand out because they are literally anything; only united by their weakness) <br /> <br /> They basically captured every kind of person and you could slap whatever culture you wanted over them. That's kinda why these clans are the biggest and most successful. Clans that came after that have small differences but you can basically slap them to one of the seven main clan archtypes. The Tzmisce are old money (like Ventrue), the Lasombra are new money (like Tremere),<br /> <br /> There are differences, of course there are differences. But without Vicissitude the Tzmisce are essentially &quot;Ventrue but introverts&quot;. Even though the ventrue have moved on to embracing CEOs, they're still largely embracing old money CEOs. New money type CEOs are for Tremere and Lasombra to embrace. The Ventrue comes from an old family of lawyers and the Tzmisce comes from an old family of doctors; they're still very similar people in terms of social standing and values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:05:57-07:00","id":1399642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399525#post1399525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A couple of points:<br /> <br /> 1. The big issue for the Tzimisce is the Tremere's place enshrined in its halls.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat's use of clerical investiture was meant to be IRONIC.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Apparently not, as there are in fact Tzimisce in the Camarilla. It could be a sticking point for the few remaining elders old enough to remember the origins of that feud, but then it didn\u2019t keep them from sharing the Sabbat with a bunch of a Tremere. The idea that inter-clan beefs from centuries ago can never be resolved smells of a static view of the setting I find impossible to buy into. It can make for some interesting drama, but as a blanket prohibition I don\u2019t buy it, and I don\u2019t think the designers do either.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes and no. Even leaving aside the general incoherence of the Sabbat\u2019s portrayal over the years, the fact is that, while the use of Christian clerical titles is ironic in the sense that the Sabbat is an unholy cult of monsters, it\u2019s also not ironic in the sense that the Sabbat is still fundamentally a religious cult at every level.<br /> <br /> <br /> And to address a completely different assertion from a previous page, if the Tzimisce clan identity relies on openly ruling over mortals, then they\u2019re fucked. It\u2019s that simple. In the 21st century that just ain\u2019t gonna happen. The fact that they did it on the Dark Ages, and some would love to go back to that, really doesn\u2019t set them apart as a clan, nor does it update them effectively to the present day. Nor does it allow for clan to be independent of sect, which isn\u2019t going to work in this edition. And in any case, we already know for a fact that there are Camarilla Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-28-2020, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:19:05-07:00","id":1399647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399637#post1399637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that the 'Prince' of Tokyo isn't a Cainite at all. Just masquerading as one in order to join the Camarilla and have access to their resources. End of the day the SI don't care what type of vampire you are when they set you on fire.<br /> <br /> As flawed KotE was, I still don't think it is right to throw out the concept and I still think there is room for the second breath etc. to be included.</div> </div> </div> </div>The author has confirmed it more than once. She\u2019s Tzimisce and a Camarilla prince, unless in your home game you decide otherwise. <br /> <br /> The status of the Wan Gui is uncertain at best. While there were some good ideas in there, it would still take a complete ground-up rewrite to avoid the racist trainwreck of KotE, and right now it\u2019s safer to avoid mentioning them.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, the Tzimisce have a lot of the body-horror elements of anime vampires, so it\u2019s an apt choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:43:52-07:00","id":1399655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399639#post1399639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are differences, of course there are differences. But without Vicissitude the Tzmisce are essentially &quot;Ventrue but introverts&quot;. Even though the ventrue have moved on to embracing CEOs, they're still largely embracing old money CEOs. New money type CEOs are for Tremere and Lasombra to embrace. The Ventrue comes from an old family of lawyers and the Tzmisce comes from an old family of doctors; they're still very similar people in terms of social standing and values.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it. The Tzimisce are closer to the Tremere (ducks) than the Giovanni are to the Tremere. They're a bunch of mad scientists and noblemen in Castles. Also, they have a fundamentally different relationship with the land than the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> It's all about money and influence with the Ventrue while the Tzimisce control the people, animals, and very forces of nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:53:34-07:00","id":1399658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399647#post1399647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The author has confirmed it more than once. She\u2019s Tzimisce and a Camarilla prince, unless in your home game you decide otherwise. <br /> <br /> The status of the Wan Gui is uncertain at best. While there were some good ideas in there, it would still take a complete ground-up rewrite to avoid the racist trainwreck of KotE, and right now it\u2019s safer to avoid mentioning them.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, the Tzimisce have a lot of the body-horror elements of anime vampires, so it\u2019s an apt choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is a shame. Old WW stuff had loads of problems some of which have been 'fixed' by later material. I'll homebrew as suggested although this just adds another reason for me not to invest too much in V5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On topic Old Clan Tzimisce does make sense due to the feudal lord link with Japanese feudalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:57:51-07:00","id":1399660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399658#post1399658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that is a shame. Old WW stuff had loads of problems some of which have been 'fixed' by later material. I'll homebrew as suggested although this just adds another reason for me not to invest too much in V5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On topic Old Clan Tzimisce does make sense due to the feudal lord link with Japanese feudalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that V5 is acknowledging the international fanbase of V:TM more. One of the mistakes of previous games was essentially, &quot;Africa is MYSTERRIOUS&quot;, &quot;Russia is COMPLETELY BLOCKED OFF&quot;, &quot;South America is all Sabbat! FLEE!&quot;, and &quot;Asia is full of alien monsters who will kill all Kindred!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's Eurocentrism was just over the top. Like you couldn't take a plane to Tokyo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T14:18:40-07:00","id":1399665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399660#post1399660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also the fact that V5 is acknowledging the international fanbase of V:TM more. One of the mistakes of previous games was essentially, &amp;quot;Africa is MYSTERRIOUS&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Russia is COMPLETELY BLOCKED OFF&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;South America is all Sabbat! FLEE!&amp;quot;, and &amp;quot;Asia is full of alien monsters who will kill all Kindred!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It's Eurocentrism was just over the top. Like you couldn't take a plane to Tokyo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but you cant take a car from Chicago to Milwaukee without getting done over by Werewolves either.<br /> <br /> I personally think the core concept ala vampire via the crow (second breath) is good and should be no different to the drowned legacies etc. being introduced. Perhaps make it worldwide rather than just Asia. I don't like the just ignore it approach.<br /> <br /> RE: the other examples Russia was a WtA setting that shouldnt have crossed over and I think they generally ran out of ideas at the time in regards to South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T14:24:35-07:00","id":1399666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399660#post1399660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;South America is all Sabbat! FLEE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>??...what happened to Argentina and Brazil being Camarilla?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020