ies-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:28:13-07:00","id":1399683,"title":"","content":"I've always considered the Cam to be a mostly international sect.<br /> <br /> -The Ashirra is a subsect. It was older, but it was subsumed by the Camarilla peacefully (well, Like, individual vampires skirmishing was certainly a thing, but there was no Ashirra VS cam grand war) This happened Likely during the Assamite war.<br /> -India is a mix of old-school fiefs and Camarilla domains. Thank the British empire. (The Ashirra Mughals get significant credit. Also the Dutch do things)<br /> -The Camarilla has a big presence in coastal asian cities. Inland china might be the Domain of the KJ, but those juicy megacities on the coast are all Camarilla domains.<br /> -Africa largely depends on how colonized the area was. Again, Inland africa and areas with less colonization and/or urbanization is mostly old-school fiefs.<br /> <br /> -I hadn't put much thought into South America. I don't think it really matters which territories are Sabbat and what's Camarilla. Maybe it's Canada throwing me off where it's like &quot;Catholic places are Sabbat but also Canada&quot; like... what? I've only ever played werewolf in SA. I'd like to think all across SA, some cities are Camarilla, and some are Sabbat, and it doesn't really matter what country you're in; it's all city based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:14:01-07:00","id":1399688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399665#post1399665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think the core concept ala vampire via the crow (second breath) is good and should be no different to the drowned legacies etc. being introduced. Perhaps make it worldwide rather than just Asia. I don't like the just ignore it approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic concept isn\u2019t terrible, but the idea that Asian vampires are completely different because <i>Asians</i> are completely different plays into some pretty terrible orientalism. There\u2019s also the problem that they\u2019re cobbled together by white people from vaguely Asian stuff they\u2019re not all that familiar with and don\u2019t actually have anything to do with Asian vampire media (which actually looks a lot more like the standard Kindred). <br /> <br /> And to top it off, they were a retcon to begin with, as in the first two editions the Asian vampires <i>were </i>Kindred, just different clans and sects than the ones found in Europe. Sort of like what the Laibon and Drowned Legacies appear to be: different branches of the same family tree. That\u2019s a lot better foundation to build on, as it turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T00:50:11-07:00","id":1399750,"title":"","content":"Asian vampire media <i>is </i>western vampires to my knowledge. Not Asian vampires the same as westerners, Vampires from the west coming east to steal Chinese women and Japanese men. (In fairness, dracula was a sex tourist too) or they depicted european inspired vampires in european inspired fantasy<br /> <br /> <br /> Hoping vampires are more considered ghosts (and the cathayans take inspiration from there) and the other Asian bloodsuckers I can think of are... changing breed territory. Perhaps there's an island with a strong vampire tradition, but Vampires as we think of them are a western thing in Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T01:05:06-07:00","id":1399753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399750#post1399750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asian vampire media <i>is </i>western vampires to my knowledge. Not Asian vampires the same as westerners, Vampires from the west coming east to steal Chinese women and Japanese men. (In fairness, dracula was a sex tourist too) or they depicted european inspired vampires in european inspired fantasy<br /> <br /> Hoping vampires are more considered ghosts (and the cathayans take inspiration from there) and the other Asian bloodsuckers I can think of are... changing breed territory. Perhaps there's an island with a strong vampire tradition, but Vampires as we think of them are a western thing in Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend SLEEPING DOG's DLC expansion, NIGHTMARE IN NORTH POINT. It contains very interesting merging of Western and Eastern undead.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://sleepingdogs.fandom.com/wiki/Nightmare_in_North_Point\" target=\"_blank\">https://sleepingdogs.fandom.com/wiki...in_North_Point</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T01:10:06-07:00","id":1399754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399688#post1399688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic concept isn\u2019t terrible, but the idea that Asian vampires are completely different because <i>Asians</i> are completely different plays into some pretty terrible orientalism. There\u2019s also the problem that they\u2019re cobbled together by white people from vaguely Asian stuff they\u2019re not all that familiar with and don\u2019t actually have anything to do with Asian vampire media (which actually looks a lot more like the standard Kindred).<br /> <br /> And to top it off, they were a retcon to begin with, as in the first two editions the Asian vampires <i>were </i>Kindred, just different clans and sects than the ones found in Europe. Sort of like what the Laibon and Drowned Legacies appear to be: different branches of the same family tree. That\u2019s a lot better foundation to build on, as it turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with your comments regarding poor racist stereotyping and writers taking assumptions with other cultures. However this is prevalent throughout WW's early work elsewhere and not just limited to KotE.<br /> <br /> In addition, I acknowledge that they were themselves a retcon from the Gaki etc. but I note that the Gaki, whilst mechanically similar for the splat, were not Kindred in the Cainite sense. With a bit of mechanical tinkering and some sympathetic/appropriate fluff these could be the KotE (second breath creation etc.) that they should have been before the anime/exalted retcon. However, I see no reason why this type of vampire should be limited to Asia although I would suggest that Asia probably be a safer place for them to exist due to the lack of Scourges in that area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T01:23:30-07:00","id":1399755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399750#post1399750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asian vampire media <i>is </i>western vampires to my knowledge. Not Asian vampires the same as westerners, Vampires from the west coming east to steal Chinese women and Japanese men. (In fairness, dracula was a sex tourist too) or they depicted european inspired vampires in european inspired fantasy<br /> <br /> <br /> Hoping vampires are more considered ghosts (and the cathayans take inspiration from there) and the other Asian bloodsuckers I can think of are... changing breed territory. Perhaps there's an island with a strong vampire tradition, but Vampires as we think of them are a western thing in Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would also add to this by stating that I have visited Cluj-Napoca in Romania and had a very similar experience as their concept of vampires does not include Dracula. Their vampire myths are the strigoi.<br /> <br /> WtO had the Risen book which was more mechanically aligned with VtM than KotE and you could potentially do a link the Wan Kuei due to the reasonably close creation. Risen had access to all physical disciplines like celerity, fortitude etc. The only issue with them was that they kept getting sucked by into Oblivion before you could get any mileage out of them so again would need a little work to make them more VtM appropriate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T01:28:37-07:00","id":1399756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399755#post1399755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would also add to this by stating that I have visited Cluj-Napoca in Romania and had a very similar experience as their concept of vampires does not include Dracula. Their vampire myths are the strigoi.<br /> <br /> WtO had the Risen book which was more mechanically aligned with VtM than KotE and you could potentially do a link the Wan Kuei due to the reasonably close creation. Risen had access to all physical disciplines like celerity, fortitude etc. The only issue with them was that they kept getting sucked by into Oblivion before you could get any mileage out of them so again would need a little work to make them more VtM appropriate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, there's also the Moroi. The Moroi are ghosts but they're SEXY GHOSTS.<br /> <br /> Ghosts who go visit mortals, are physical, drain their life force, usually sex them up, and then leave them dead.<br /> <br /> They also can be the children of Strigoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/ony