ther Asian bloodsuckers I can think of are... changing breed territory. Perhaps there's an island with a strong vampire tradition, but Vampires as we think of them are a western thing in Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really comes down to how you define 'vampire'. I mean the definition of ' returned dead that steal life from the living' handily covers the game concepts of both Kindred and Hungry Ghosts and easi;y covers a hundred different real world concepts from strigoi to pontianak to yara-ma-yha-who to yuki-onna to bean-sidhe. <br /> <br /> I mean there are a ton of south east asian horror movies that I would consider 'vampire' movies because they feature kuntilanak, leyak, krasue, aswang.....others may not and may call them generic ' horror' movies because no one grows long canines or turns into a bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T03:30:22-07:00","id":1399771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399760#post1399760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, the whole &quot;sharing blood&quot; th