/www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T05:33:28-07:00","id":1399795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399788#post1399788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think how you described it was awesome, FYI, so really you just confuse the hell out of me. What is it you found so problematic?<br /> <br /> Vampires should come in massively varied, bizarre, and strange varieties even if they're all the same race. Honestly, I think vampires are often treated as way too similar. They should have amazing varieties of powers, weaknesses, and curses.<br /> <br /> Have vampires from South America who can turn into water, are killed by gold, and are immune to sunlight but take damage from plants.<br /> <br /> Have a bloodline that can become immaterial, must sleep in coffins, and are created by pouring their sires blood on gravesites so they rise from the dead days afterward.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clan system infers that the vampire is a descendant of Caine. Legacy in this instance, or something similar would be much better for these other types of vampire?<br /> <br /> However, I don't mind these other types vampires being assumed to be a Clan IC by these 'ignorant western Cainites TM' in order to get them to interact with each other. However they should have their own origins which is sympathetic to their locale.<br /> <br /> As have been IMPRESSED upon me by friends in Hong Kong and Tawain--they bought a book called VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE to play Western-style vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T05:49:02-07:00","id":1399796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399795#post1399795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Clan system infers that the vampire is a descendant of Caine. Legacy in this instance, or something similar would be much better for these other types of vampire?<br /> <br /> However, I don't mind these other types vampires being assumed to be a Clan IC by these 'ignorant western Cainites TM' in order to get them to interact with each other. However they should have their own origins which is sympathetic to their locale.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of humanity dates back to Africa so cultures can spring from different places, grow amazing histories on their own, and change.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think we have enough problems in the real world than to worry about the vampires in one fictional universe having a common ancestor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:14:27-07:00","id":1399802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As have been IMPRESSED upon me by friends in Hong Kong and Tawain--they bought a book called VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE to play Western-style vampires. </div> </div> </div>Nothing is stopping you friends from playing Western-style vampires just like no one is stopping me from playing Hungry Dead in the UK. Your game your rules.<br /> <br /> I believe that Cainites should be a playable option anywhere in the world and I agree that all the silly barriers that WW installed in the first place should be removed/ignored.<br /> <br /> However, what I don't like is the deletion of the Hungry Dead wholesale. They have a place in the WoD and should be fixed properly not retconned out of existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of humanity dates back to Africa so cultures can spring from different places, grow amazing histories on their own, and change.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think we have enough problems in the real world than to worry about the vampires in one fictional universe having a common ancestor. </div> </div> </div>The common ancestor is a huge issue and even worse than the racism cited in KotE. Caine is from western religion and by linking everyone from around the world to it infers that other religions are wrong. <br /> <br /> I note you comments regarding problems in the real world but we are on a WOD forum so?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:20:22-07:00","id":1399803,"title":"","content":"Caine is middle eastern","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:28:45-07:00","id":1399805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399803#post1399803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine is middle eastern</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify I meant western religion based on judeo christian tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:06:15-07:00","id":1399827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399805#post1399805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify I meant western religion based on judeo christian tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Abrahamic faith please. VTM's Caine myth is Jewish/Gnostic and has nothing to do with Christ. Also Islam has been just about as relevant as Christ in VTM<br /> <br /> Besides, Isn't Caine also Cagn (I think that's how it was spelt?) who was around in africa. It's entirely possible he was Cagn before Caine; He wandered a lot after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:23:49-07:00","id":1399833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399802#post1399802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common ancestor is a huge issue and even worse than the racism cited in KotE. Caine is from western religion and by linking everyone from around the world to it infers that other religions are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Except the World of Darkness already states that 90% of the Christian religion is wrong since everyone goes to hell or disintegrates (The Underworld). Also, God is a bastard. Speaking as a Abrahamic religious person in RL, they have no resemblance to anything &quot;real&quot; about our religion. The Caine myth and Noddism is a maltheistic (and with Demon: The Fallen) theistic Satanist view of the world.<br /> 2. A common ancestor for vampires doesn't necessarily mean anything about Buddhism or Daoism or Shinto (or Hinduism) since vampires are not religious figures. They aren't religious figures in Christianity or Judaism either but are just tied to the Caine/Cain myth. The Thousand Hells, for example, can exist in the Underworld or Penumbra but that a bunch of blood drinking homicidal parasites does not in anyway impact the existence of the merits of the Middle Path.<br /> 3. That presumes the Caine myth is true and while it's probable that there IS a Caine in the World of Darkness (and a Lilith), it's not 100% certain that he's THE progenitor of ALL vampires or just another Laibon ancestor that went rogue. And humanity comes from Africa, there's no denying that. If anyone is right about vampirism, it's them.<br /> 4. The Clans can have their own progenitor myth like the Setites but maybe a bit more believably done. Whichever is &quot;right&quot; will be up to the ST. Presumably we could have a Wan Kuei Gehenna plot next time we destroy the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:28:44-07:00","id":1399835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abrahamic faith please. VTM's Caine myth is Jewish/Gnostic and has nothing to do with Christ. Also Islam has been just about as relevant as Christ in VTM </div> </div> </div>True. I'll go with Abrahamic which is a more neutral term.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:51:50-07:00","id":1399842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399802#post1399802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common ancestor is a huge issue and even worse than the racism cited in KotE. Caine is from western religion and by linking everyone from around the world to it infers that other religions are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, those are two unrelated things: common ancestry and common mythology. If you conflate the two, you end up with some very bizarre positions, like saying that real-world humans can\u2019t possibly have a common origin because that would mean the Bible is correct, which would be unfair to Buddhists.<br /> <br /> All the world\u2019s vampires can come from a common origin <i>and </i>the Caine myth can be just one culture\u2019s attempt to explain that origin. It\u2019s also entirely possible that the 13 clans we\u2019re familiar with are just one branch of the tree and that other branches differ far more from them than those clans differ from one another. The books have, from the very beginning, been agnostic about the precise number of clans/Antediluvians in existence, and it\u2019s entirely possible there are unknown branches. I suspect the Drowned Legacies represent this sort of thing, having branched off from the old-world vampires so long ago they were entirely forgotten and evolved independently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-29-2020, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:29:30-07:00","id":1399858,"title":"","content":"Set is a ginger. Red hair, likely with Pale skin and freckles. probably nothing to do with the clan adversion to light. Yet he's an egyptian god (though he is a god of foreigners..)<br /> <br /> I've heard some people in central asia had 'red' hair. How red? unknown. maybe brown is red to some people. <br /> <br /> the second city is thought of as a place in the middle east. yet we have the presence of a red headed anti.<br /> <br /> I think we can only conclude that some of generations 1-3 got around a lot and left a lot of myths behind. Their more static children who couldnt travel the wilderness so freely only shared some of the little they knew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:34:28-07:00","id":1399860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399842#post1399842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, those are two unrelated things: common ancestry and common mythology. If you conflate the two, you end up with some very bizarre positions, like saying that real-world humans can\u2019t possibly have a common origin because that would mean the Bible is correct, which would be unfair to Buddhists.<br /> <br /> All the world\u2019s vampires can come from a common origin <i>and </i>the Caine myth can be just one culture\u2019s attempt to explain that origin. It\u2019s also entirely possible that the 13 clans we\u2019re familiar with are just one branch of the tree and that other branches differ far more from them than those clans differ from one another. The books have, from the very beginning, been agnostic about the precise number of clans/Antediluvians in existence, and it\u2019s entirely possible there are unknown branches. I suspect the Drowned Legacies represent this sort of thing, having branched off from the old-world vampires so long ago they were entirely forgotten and evolved independently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I part of agree. I met once a guy saying both bible and japanese origin myth are correct because the japanese people are not really humans, they are just the mythological elfs that made their asylum here and most of them decided to cover themselves as humans to avoid that the humans go up against them while theyself know that they are as elfes are so much better.<br /> <br /> Anyway back to topic I think that the different vampire myths should be covered in the game and I would really love it, if not everyone is just a cainit but they are really different like the Wan Gui.<br /> <br /> Other thing, Demon Slayer Yaiba had made the oni origin similar to the cainites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:51:17-07:00","id":1399865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399858#post1399858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set is a ginger. Red hair, likely with Pale skin and freckles. probably nothing to do with the clan adversion to light. Yet he's an egyptian god (though he is a god of foreigners..)<br /> <br /> I've heard some people in central asia had 'red' hair. How red? unknown. maybe brown is red to some people.<br /> <br /> the second city is thought of as a place in the middle east. yet we have the presence of a red headed anti.<br /> <br /> I think we can only conclude that some of generations 1-3 got around a lot and left a lot of myths behind. Their more static children who couldnt travel the wilderness so freely only shared some of the little they knew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, it makes perfect sense if Set was an albino.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://genetics.thetech.org/ask/ask67\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://genetics.thetech.org/ask/ask67\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://genetics.thetech.org/ask/ask67\" target=\"_blank\"> https://genetics.thetech.org/ask/ask67 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Curiously, this would also explain movie Thulsa Doom's blue eyes (though that was James Earl Jones wearing contacts).<br /> <br /> And also Set WOULD have a vulnerability to sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T10:02:38-07:00","id":1399872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399756#post1399756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly, there's also the Moroi. The Moroi are ghosts but they're SEXY GHOSTS.<br /> <br /> Ghosts who go visit mortals, are physical, drain their life force, usually sex them up, and then leave them dead.<br /> <br /> They also can be the children of Strigoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope I don't make a lot of mistakes in my project...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> The hungry dead - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Strigoi: The hungry dead Why? I have wanted, for a long time, to create European creatures akin to the Wan Kuei. This is the first beta version. A summary: This </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T10:16:54-07:00","id":1399876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399872#post1399872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope I don't make a lot of mistakes in my project...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> The hungry dead - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Strigoi: The hungry dead Why? I have wanted, for a long time, to create European creatures akin to the Wan Kuei. This is the first beta version. A summary: This </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;jumps thread&gt;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T17:31:32-07:00","id":1399952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399860#post1399860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I part of agree. I met once a guy saying both bible and japanese origin myth are correct because the japanese people are not really humans, they are just the mythological elfs that made their asylum here and most of them decided to cover themselves as humans to avoid that the humans go up against them while theyself know that they are as elfes are so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, I hope that guy got some help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T17:39:54-07:00","id":1399954,"title":"","content":"Ok...coming back in because the snarky dismissive remark apparently wasn't? Honestly it really seemed thats what it was.<br /> <br /> One of ( and certainly not the only) main issues is that I like folkloric vampires. VtM does movie, modern novel and tv vampires which spead by an infectious bloodborne viral effect. In 25 years of research the only folkloric vampire from anywhere in the world which does anything like this is the Yara-Ma-Yha-Who....and thats a much more involved process anyway.<br /> <br /> Sure we could pretend that everyone else is wrong and the only one in thousands of cultures, regions and belief systems who got things correct for every vampire in the world is one irish bloke.<br /> <br /> I like vampires that can rise because they weren't buried with the appropriate honors, or because they were terribly murdered or died in childbirth, or broke sacrosanct beliefs in life.....I like them a lot more than some rando bites you than feeds you blood and then suddenly your a vampire. Now I have no problem with them existing but erasing the types of vampires that I prefer and shoving them into the straight jacket of viral bite modern movie vampire out of a desire to ' simplify' I think does a terrible disservice to the source material and the range of chronicles and stories we can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T18:26:12-07:00","id":1399965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399952#post1399952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, I hope that guy got some help.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to tell sometimes where the racism begins and the batshit lunacy ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399954#post1399954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...coming back in because the snarky dismissive remark apparently wasn't? Honestly it really seemed thats what it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to mine?<br /> <br /> But yes, I strongly favor Clans that are incredibly diverse and the idea that Kindred can represent hundreds of individual and distinct vampire archetypes. The point of V:TM should be that you can have one system to represent countless different kinds of vampires.<br /> <br /> It was the one thing I think Requiem did better than V:TM.<br /> <br /> It's a robust system that you can do virtually any kind of vampire with Discipline+Weakness. I've even had Pendagalan as Kindred show up in my games. You know, the decapitated floating head women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure we could pretend that everyone else is wrong and the only one in thousands of cultures, regions and belief systems who got things correct for every vampire in the world is one irish bloke. </div> </div> </div>Haha. Oh, I see, I *REALLY* misread what you were saying because I love folkloric vampires and think that the Clan System is the best to represent them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T18:51:00-07:00","id":1399970,"title":"","content":"Some Bloodlines I've used in my games:<br /> <br /> * <b>Penanggalan</b>: Their Bloodline discipline allows them to separate their head and go have it flying around. Their weakness is that they can only feed on children and pregnant women. They also cannot reproduce with men. I also had them possess Presence and Auspex.<br /> <br /> * <b>Strigoi</b>: I had them as a Nosferatu bloodline that had Obfuscate, Protean, and Potence. The Strigoi were notable in that they could only be raised from the dead by pouring blood on the graves of evil men and letting it soak into them. The Strigoi's weakness is the fact that they are naturally animalistic and inhuman so they lose Two Points of humanity or Paths when they fail. Mostly they end up as degenerate wights.<br /> <br /> * <b>Draugr</b>: They have Potence, Protean [they become bears as well as can increase their size], and Fortitude. The Draugr carry a horrifying smell of death wherever they go, however, and are always rotting. They are believed to a Cappadocian bloodline. They tend to inhabit graveyards and sewers like the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> * <b>Lamatsu</b>: The serpent bodied lower ones are a Greek bloodline that possesses Protean, Presence, and Thaumaturgy. They believed that Hecate was the first vampire and were practicing<br /> witches. They were believed to be a Lasombra bloodline despite the lack of their disciplines because a mirror revealed their true monstrous form.<br /> <br /> * <b>Gorgons</b>: Pretty much what you'd expect with Medusa allowing a person to be frozen in place at 1st level with a stare and turned to stone at higher levels. Gorgons possess Fortitude, Medusa, and Vicissitude. Their natural forms are hideous but they can assume pleasing ones for a time.<br /> <br /> I think I had Beckett say that there were 13 Known Clans and something like 200 Bloodlines that he knew of, with most having just a couple of dozen members at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:40:21-07:00","id":1399981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399970#post1399970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Bloodlines I've used in my games:<br /> <br /> * <b>Penanggalan</b>: Their Bloodline discipline allows them to separate their head and go have it flying around. Their weakness is that they can only feed on children and pregnant women. They also cannot reproduce with men. I also had them possess Presence and Auspex.<br /> <br /> * <b>Strigoi</b>: I had them as a Nosferatu bloodline that had Obfuscate, Protean, and Potence. The Strigoi were notable in that they could only be raised from the dead by pouring blood on the graves of evil men and letting it soak into them. The Strigoi's weakness is the fact that they are naturally animalistic and inhuman so they lose Two Points of humanity or Paths when they fail. Mostly they end up as degenerate wights.<br /> <br /> * <b>Draugr</b>: They have Potence, Protean [they become bears as well as can increase their size], and Fortitude. The Draugr carry a horrifying smell of death wherever they go, however, and are always rotting. They are believed to a Cappadocian bloodline. They tend to inhabit graveyards and sewers like the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> * <b>Lamatsu</b>: The serpent bodied lower ones are a Greek bloodline that possesses Protean, Presence, and Thaumaturgy. They believed that Hecate was the first vampire and were practicing<br /> witches. They were believed to be a Lasombra bloodline despite the lack of their disciplines because a mirror revealed their true monstrous form.<br /> <br /> * <b>Gorgons</b>: Pretty much what you'd expect with Medusa allowing a person to be frozen in place at 1st level with a stare and turned to stone at higher levels. Gorgons possess Fortitude, Medusa, and Vicissitude. Their natural forms are hideous but they can assume pleasing ones for a time.<br /> <br /> I think I had Beckett say that there were 13 Known Clans and something like 200 Bloodlines that he knew of, with most having just a couple of dozen members at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, but how do you square the fact that all of these need to be embraced which goes against the base concepts of every single one of them?<br /> <br /> I mean they ape some concepts of the original being but utterly ignore vast swathes of what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-29-2020, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:47:01-07:00","id":1399985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399981#post1399981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but how do you square the fact that all of these need to be embraced which goes against the base concepts of every single one of them?<br /> <br /> I mean they ape some concepts of the original being but utterly ignore vast swathes of what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given there's no mythological origin for the Embrace, it's just a thing authors invented so the monsters can self-procreate, I don't see a problem. Mythological fidelity is not an issue when changes are across the board a thing to benefit world-building.<br /> <br /> Mind you, as a writer, I strongly believe world-building coherency for a setting is ultra-important.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather have a Cainite <b>Penanggalan </b>than there's another whole different species of monster somehow existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:48:35-07:00","id":1399986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399965#post1399965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you referring to mine?<br /> <br /> But yes, I strongly favor Clans that are incredibly diverse and the idea that Kindred can represent hundreds of individual and distinct vampire archetypes. The point of V:TM should be that you can have one system to represent countless different kinds of vampires.<br /> <br /> It was the one thing I think Requiem did better than V:TM.<br /> <br /> It's a robust system that you can do virtually any kind of vampire with Discipline+Weakness. I've even had Pendagalan as Kindred show up in my games. You know, the decapitated floating head women.<br /> <br /> Haha. Oh, I see, I *REALLY* misread what you were saying because I love folkloric vampires and think that the Clan System is the best to represent them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we'll need to agree to disagree. I think the viral reproduction model and system of VtM badly serves the vast majority of vampire folklore and mythology and would prefer a wider variety of mechanical systems to represent to full variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:50:57-07:00","id":1399987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399985#post1399985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given there's no mythological origin for the Embrace, it's just a thing authors invented so the monsters can self-procreate, I don't see a problem. Mythological fidelity is not an issue when it's across the board a thing to benefit world-building.<br /> <br /> Mind you, as a writer, I strongly believe world-building coherency for a setting is ultra-important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. We're never going to agree on this. Its just smashing square pegs into round holes and losing too much of importance in the process for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:54:28-07:00","id":1399988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399987#post1399987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. We're never going to agree on this. Its just smashing square pegs into round holes and losing too much of importance in the process for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, we do seem irreconcilable. I don't see why you'd even have Clans in your game. You don't seem to be taking advantage of, &quot;different varieties of vampire&quot; at all. They all seem to be just tiny variations of the same kind of creature the way you describe them. For me, the fun is that you have all these crazy options from the same creature.<br /> <br /> But you do you. Everyone's world is different.<br /> <br /> I mean that sincerely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2020, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T21:07:52-07:00","id":1399995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399988#post1399988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, we do seem irreconcilable. I don't see why you'd even have Clans in your game. You don't seem to be taking advantage of, &quot;different varieties of vampire&quot; at all. They all seem to be just tiny variations of the same kind of creature the way you describe them. For me, the fun is that you have all these crazy options from the same creature.<br /> <br /> But you do you. Everyone's world is different.<br /> <br /> I mean that sincerely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait.....WTF?....I &quot;don't seem to be taking advantage of different types of vampires at all&quot; but your the one who just outlined 6 different beings all with variant origins in folklore, variant reasons for being and you then removed their reasons for existing and most of their flavour in order to make them all into the same type of vampire.....<br /> <br /> In my campaigns I have the viral model vampire, along with the vampire that spontaneously rises, along with the vampire that rises because the human it was made specific preparations before death, the vampire that offended the gods or broke societal mores leaving it unable to rest.....and the vampire that incubates you in its water filled stomach over a series of days until you become what it is. If its a little extra mechanical work on my part its worth it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T00:31:35-07:00","id":1400020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1399995#post1399995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.....WTF?....I &quot;don't seem to be taking advantage of different types of vampires at all&quot; but your the one who just outlined 6 different beings all with variant origins in folklore, variant reasons for being and you then removed their reasons for existing and most of their flavour in order to make them all into the same type of vampire.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Same type of vampire?<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I'm very confused. No, the point is to create the ability for player characters to play as well as interact with various types of folklore monsters as members of the same race in order to interact. To create a wide variety of fascinating and twisted monsters to exist in the setting that have a common origin as well as society. In-universe, the idea that vampires come in a variety of sizes and powers while inspiring the Folklore that is going to be at least largely inaccurate about them. Just like how Romanian, movies, and Stoker folklore is inaccurate about &quot;regular&quot; Kindred.<br /> <br /> It makes the Kindred world all the more diverse and fascinating while avoiding adding like, &quot;There's hundreds of different kinds of supernaturals that are completely unrelated&quot; flaw. Which some people don't see as a flaw but stretches credulity and isolates the kinds of monsters from each other, IMHO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my campaigns I have the viral model vampire, along with the vampire that spontaneously rises, along with the vampire that rises because the human it was made specific preparations before death, the vampire that offended the gods or broke societal mores leaving it unable to rest.....and the vampire that incubates you in its water filled stomach over a series of days until you become what it is. If its a little extra mechanical work on my part its worth it. </div> </div> </div>The rises from the dead because of a curse or sanctified ground thing being a good example as its a rumor in-universe about how Kindred REALLY procreate. Which is totally unrelated to folklore. I think part of this being that I don't think of Kindred as &quot;viral model&quot; because that's not a real thing in folklore and Kindred in the WOD are dead, they're dead diseased. It's a magical transferance based on Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> It's a good thing to establish one single creation method so that its all under one big genus.<br /> <br /> Im glad you've put all the work you've done into yours but I guess I'm a &quot;Common Origins&quot; guy. Sort of like I'd prefer Mutants to be the only source of superpowers or magic or whatnot if I do a comic book setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-30-2020, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T01:51:38-07:00","id":1400025,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't think of anything more boring and homogenizing, but at least I know where your coming from. Yeah, we want very different things out of this hobby. But good to know I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-30-2020, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T02:00:13-07:00","id":1400027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400025#post1400025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly can't think of anything more boring and disrespectful, but at least I know where your coming from. Yeah, we want very different things out of this hobby. But good to know I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how disrespectful enters an equation unless you think things like Hercules and Thor in Marvel comics are disrespectful. At the end of the day, this is just a game about leather jacket vampires looking cool.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, that's the beauty of V:TM. It has room for multiple interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T02:50:48-07:00","id":1400030,"title":"","content":"I don't think it wise to go deep on capturing legendary vampire myths with bloodlines. If anything, those myths were other things that might have been misconstrued as vampires, those things might have been normal vampires that just happened to have some out of clan disciplines, or most likely; People just completely made shit up because they do that sometimes. Some combination could have occured. <br /> <br /> Bloodlines best suit making types of people. You can string three disciplines together and make a personality out of them. <br /> <br /> Potence, Thaumaturgy, Animalism: Warrior cult. <br /> Auspex, potence, obfuscate; Not very social, bit of a stalker. <br /> Protean, presence, Fortitude: Terrifying figure with a god complex (and a masquerade breach waiting to happen) <br /> Necromancy, Presence, Auspex: &quot;i speak with dead people (give me your blood) &quot; (Note: Presence an Necromancy are really kinda the opposite disciplines so I'd only put them together for this kind of character) <br /> <br /> and so on and so forth. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T03:54:30-07:00","id":1400039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400030#post1400030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necromancy, Presence, Auspex: &quot;i speak with dead people (give me your blood) &quot; (Note: Presence an Necromancy are really kinda the opposite disciplines so I'd only put them together for this kind of character)</div> </div> </div> </div>why not complementary?<br /> commanding the living + commanding the dead = commanding everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T04:18:28-07:00","id":1400042,"title":"","content":"A lot of necromancers have dominate for that very purpose. <br /> <br /> Necromancy is a morbid discipline that requires lots of study and practice. You lock yourself away in a lonely place with a good death ressonance where you are unlikely to be disturbed, while you search through books and play with corpses. Even if for some reason you were quite a social necromancer; Taking time to stop smelling of death and putting the charm on gets in the way of study. you want to feed quickly and without hassle. Pressence is the most hassle discipline, especially in VTM where it's also a big blood drain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:57:50-07:00","id":1400104,"title":"","content":"I mean, <i>everything</i> is artificially lumped together under the \u201cvampire\u201d umbrella. There is no original folkloric vampire, strictly speaking. It\u2019s a whole bunch of stuff that modern media have hammered into that shape, which doesn\u2019t faithfully represent <i>any </i>of them. But at the same time, that\u2019s kind of how folklore works in the first place, as those legends were themselves distilled from other stuff. It\u2019s just that pop culture is kind of the folklore of today.<br /> <br /> So while I get it when people say X type of vampire-like creature doesn\u2019t really fit the Kindred mold, doesn\u2019t seem like it should be Embraced, etc., the thing is, that\u2019s no less true across the board. I find it weird that people only focus on, say, <i>Asian</i> vampire creatures but don\u2019t object that European vampire creatures have experienced the same treatment. Is it because deep down they still want the Asian critters to be exotic? Is it because they think the Kindred actually represent European vampire lore? Is it because they (incorrectly, in my view) believe Kindred lore is all worked out with no room for mystery?<br /> <br /> The fact is that vampire media across the globe is becoming increasingly assimilated to this artificial shared mythos. A Korean movie about vampire is going to have them working the same as they do in American movies. It seems I only ever hear white Americans/Europeans insisting things need to be segregated, and that\u2019s not great. I\u2019m not saying <i>every</i> vampire-like thing has to be the same species in the game, but I think we have to be careful about how and where we insist that they <i>shouldn\u2019t </i>be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:29:58-07:00","id":1400109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400104#post1400104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find it weird that people only focus on, say, <i>Asian</i> vampire creatures but don\u2019t object that European vampire creatures have experienced the same treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>except they do?<br /> <br /> gangrel as norse gods, nosferatu/nictuku as folkloric monsters was never popular,<br /> tzimisce as xenomorphs has been the object of many debate,<br /> and peopel almost never talk about nahualli<br /> <br /> the ones that do approave of the &quot;european&quot; treatment are the same that want every vampire to be kindred,<br /> and they keep bloating the fluff with more and more wacky bloodlines, like pokemons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:48:50-07:00","id":1400115,"title":"","content":"Well, the Kindred are what the game is about. It\u2019s the selling point and central conceit. If one rejects that, there\u2019s not much left to talk about. And a big point of that central conceit is that behind the various vampire legends in the world is this creature that doesn\u2019t really conform to any of them. It\u2019s rather like complaining that the werewolves don\u2019t resemble werewolf legends or that the mages aren\u2019t faithful to legends about magicians. All of the WoD stuff is this way, with the idea that the legends were based on the central critter in question, rather than the other way around, which means the legends aren\u2019t authoritative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:52:46-07:00","id":1400117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400109#post1400109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> except they do?<br /> <br /> gangrel as norse gods, nosferatu/nictuku as folkloric monsters was never popular,<br /> tzimisce as xenomorphs has been the object of many debate,<br /> and peopel almost never talk about nahualli<br /> <br /> the ones that do approave of the &quot;european&quot; treatment are the same that want every vampire to be kindred,<br /> <b>and they keep bloating the fluff with more and more wacky bloodlines, like pokemons</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I CHOOSE GORGON!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:55:07-07:00","id":1400118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400115#post1400115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Kindred are what the game is about. It\u2019s the selling point and central conceit. If one rejects that, there\u2019s not much left to talk about. And a big point of that central conceit is that behind the various vampire legends in the world is this creature that doesn\u2019t really conform to any of them. It\u2019s rather like complaining that the werewolves don\u2019t resemble werewolf legends or that the mages aren\u2019t faithful to legends about magicians. All of the WoD stuff is this way, with the idea that the legends were based on the central critter in question, rather than the other way around, which means the legends aren\u2019t authoritative.</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes beyond that too because there's no such thing as a central legendary canon. It's like the &quot;real&quot; King Arthur. Do you know the names of Arthur's three sons?<br /> <br /> I do but few people do because they got written out.<br /> <br /> Every version of a vampire legend is equally valid because....well, THEY KEEP THEIR TRUE NATURE SECRET.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:10:51-07:00","id":1400124,"title":"","content":"I kinda like -These other cultures might've had their own vampires BUT THEN THE EUROPEANS CAME AND DID A COLONIALISM. <br /> <br /> I like vampires as charicatures of the human condition, I don't care for folklore. The Ventrue Parody of a businessman works a lot more for everybody than an authentic well researched myth from Cornwall. The latter might be interesting, but it's not as good. A bit harder to relate to. And then you've got to wonder how these -hyper specific myths from specific places- all got together and hung out in one of the many warsaw museums dedicated to the uprising. The Ventrue work because they work <i>everywhere</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:14:02-07:00","id":1400126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400124#post1400124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda like -These other cultures might've had their own vampires BUT THEN THE EUROPEANS CAME AND DID A COLONIALISM.<br /> <br /> I like vampires as charicatures of the human condition, I don't care for folklore. The Ventrue Parody of a businessman works a lot more for everybody than an authentic well researched myth from Cornwall. The latter might be interesting, but it's not as good. A bit harder to relate to. And then you've got to wonder how these -hyper specific myths from specific places- all got together and hung out in one of the many warsaw museums dedicated to the uprising. The Ventrue work because they work <i>everywhere</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet Samedi rock.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:35:16-07:00","id":1400133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400126#post1400126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet Samedi rock.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but if you made <i>every</i> clan or bloodline into a fun little bundle of culture, it wouldn't work. The Samedi also kinda work because they've got what we white-folks find to be a super-colourful, exotic Caribean flavour to them. we think of shrunken heads and cane swords and the probably the <i>Jamaican</i> gang from Predator 2 that represented a loss of law and order and a crumbling society which would imply the directors were a bit racist.... Fun things that I know very little about. <br /> <br /> But, say, the Telyavic Tremere... What have they got going for them, other than a god of bees? What excites you about the sombre culture of modern day lithuania? How many regional bloodlines could we have and keep things interesting? <br /> <br /> I agree with you, I like Samedi, but if they got bigger, I'd expect them to abandon the Haitian stick and adopt the belief systems of their locality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:08:29-07:00","id":1400138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400115#post1400115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If one rejects that, there\u2019s not much left to talk about. And a big point of that central conceit is that behind the various vampire legends in the world is this creature that doesn\u2019t really conform to any of them. It\u2019s rather like complaining that the werewolves don\u2019t resemble werewolf legends or that the mages aren\u2019t faithful to legends about magicians.</div> </div> </div> </div>first, Mages are not a good example, because they do have two different splats, one of which represents traditional mages (hedge magicians)<br /> <br /> second, I'm not against vampires not conforming to legends (hungry dead don't conform either),<br /> what I'm against is making hungry dead and other &quot;exotic vampires&quot; into other clans/bloodlines,<br /> we already have 7 to 13 clans, which are already hard enough to lump in together due to how different some of them are,<br /> <br /> if we need more &quot;exotic vampires&quot;, we should make them into different splats,<br /> <br /> and by exotic, I don't mean &quot;Asian&quot; or &quot;African&quot;, I mean flesh-eaters, Risen, soul suckers, xenomorphs, blood mages, or anything that would be sufficiently different from a cainite<br /> <br /> if there's flesh-eater vampires that can't bloodbond, let them be a different splat rather than a clan that has an antideluvian that likes steak<br /> <br /> just my two cents","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:14:01-07:00","id":1400139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400138#post1400138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> first, Mages are not a good example, because they do have two different splats, one of which represents traditional mages (hedge magicians)<br /> <br /> second, I'm not against vampires not conforming to legends (hungry dead don't conform either),<br /> what I'm against is making hungry dead and other &quot;exotic vampires&quot; into other clans/bloodlines,<br /> we already have 7 to 13 clans, which are already hard enough to lump in together due to how different some of them are,<br /> <br /> if we need more &quot;exotic vampires&quot;, we should make them into different splats,<br /> <br /> and by exotic, I don't mean &quot;Asian&quot; or &quot;African&quot;, I mean flesh-eaters, Risen, soul suckers, xenomorphs, blood mages, or anything that would be sufficiently different from a cainite<br /> <br /> if there's flesh-eater vampires that can't bloodbond, let them be a different splat rather than a clan that has an antideluvian that likes steak<br /> <br /> just my two cents</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that's needlessly complex when the central appeal of V:TM at least at the beginning was each clan allowed you to play a different kind of vampire. You want to be Nosferatu, you play Nosferatu. You want to be shape-shifting monster Dracula, you play Gangrel. You want to be a Lost Boy or Near Dark, you play Brujah. You want to be Scholomance studying Satanist wizard vampires [which were a thing] you play Tremere.<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> I feel like they didn't go nearly far enough, though. Why not reveal dozens more Clans of local vampire legends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:24:55-07:00","id":1400143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400139#post1400139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like they didn't go nearly far enough, though. Why not reveal dozens more Clans of local vampire legends?</div> </div> </div> </div>because there's a (supposedly universal) vampire society with laws and tradition,<br /> and it's hard to imagine how all these different bloodlines can fit in with the system<br /> <br /> edit: if anything, with how varied clans and bloodlines are,<br /> it's a wonder the sabbat isn't the unifying sect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-30-2020, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:26:55-07:00","id":1400144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400143#post1400143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> because there's a (supposedly universal) vampire society with laws and tradition,<br /> and it's hard to imagine how all these different bloodlines can fit in with the system</div> </div> </div> </div>Groups like the Drowned and Bloodlines I think or perhaps even identifying themselves as Bloodlines of existing clans to &quot;hide&quot; themselves as we saw with the Setites.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:33:23-07:00","id":1400145,"title":"","content":"Because they weren't going for local vampire legends. <br /> <br /> Vampire is a satire. <br /> The core seven clans are each making fun of something in normal mundane life, in particular society's elite parasites; The Ventrue that owns everything, The Toreador is a vile socialite, the Brujah is the guy that owns some and is mad at the elite that he doesn't own more, or he's a union boss, the Tremere are a professional firm, The Gangrel is a rural type, the Nosferatu is the unpleasant guy they deign to work with because he gets them what they need and the Malkavian is the lunatic who could be any of them. <br /> <br /> They were never meant to meet some vampire myth, they were meant to take the piss. They were an exaggerated mockery of people in the real world. That's the core seven. The other clans that came after were half overlapping with the seven, half crude caricature of foreigners from an anglo-american perspective. <br /> <br /> Say it with me again:<br /> Satire <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:40:37-07:00","id":1400147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400145#post1400145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they weren't going for local vampire legends.<br /> <br /> Vampire is a satire.<br /> The core seven clans are each making fun of something in normal mundane life, in particular society's elite parasites; The Ventrue that owns everything, The Toreador is a vile socialite, the Brujah is the guy that owns some and is mad at the elite that he doesn't own more, or he's a union boss, the Tremere are a professional firm, The Gangrel is a rural type, the Nosferatu is the unpleasant guy they deign to work with because he gets them what they need and the Malkavian is the lunatic who could be any of them.<br /> <br /> They were never meant to meet some vampire myth, they were meant to take the piss. They were an exaggerated mockery of people in the real world. That's the core seven. The other clans that came after were half overlapping with the seven, half crude caricature of foreigners from an anglo-american perspective.<br /> <br /> Say it with me again:<br /> Satire</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it but also was, &quot;playing different kinds of vampires from movies and fiction.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T17:56:58-07:00","id":1400219,"title":"","content":"Actually, I\u2019m fine with there being stuff that doesn\u2019t fit into the playable character types. Nothing wrong with pulling the rug out from under what players think they know, and the setting should never feel completely filled in.<br /> <br /> My main problem is when there\u2019s a double-standard and people insist the exotic critters have to be Asian etc. A core principle is that the Kindred are not specifically European and never have been. Non-Kindred critters shouldn\u2019t be restricted to non-European locales or ethnicities, and we have to take care not to fall into the trap of othering and exoticizing those places and people (which WoD unfortunately has quite a history of).<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the same time, it\u2019s not <i>wrong </i>to create types of Kindred based on worldwide vampire legends. That\u2019s what Kindred are, essentially: a critter that incorporates elements of various sources but isn\u2019t beholden to any of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-30-2020, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T19:24:26-07:00","id":1400234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400219#post1400219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I\u2019m fine with there being stuff that doesn\u2019t fit into the playable character types. Nothing wrong with pulling the rug out from under what players think they know, and the setting should never feel completely filled in.<br /> <br /> My main problem is when there\u2019s a double-standard and people insist the exotic critters have to be Asian etc. A core principle is that the Kindred are not specifically European and never have been. Non-Kindred critters shouldn\u2019t be restricted to non-European locales or ethnicities, and we have to take care not to fall into the trap of othering and exoticizing those places and people (which WoD unfortunately has quite a history of).<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the same time, it\u2019s not <i>wrong </i>to create types of Kindred based on worldwide vampire legends. That\u2019s what Kindred are, essentially: a critter that incorporates elements of various sources but isn\u2019t beholden to any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure I referenced folkloric beings from 6 different continents including Europe so you can't be referring to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T05:59:23-07:00","id":1400292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400219#post1400219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Kindred critters shouldn\u2019t be restricted to non-European locales or ethnicities, and we have to take care not to fall into the trap of othering and exoticizing those places and people (which WoD unfortunately has quite a history of).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair; given their metaphysics, I\u2019ve always thought of the Wan Kuei as a type of Risen, with the abilities gained their spiritual paths (the Dharmas) being the primary distinction between Eastern Risen/Wan Kuei and Western Risen.<br /> <br /> Given that Golconda is believed to be a variation on those paths and allowed access to supernatural disciplines beyond generational limits (i.e. even a 16th Gen could theoretically gain \u201cPlot Device/Rank 10\u201d in any discipline if they achieved and maintained Golconda) it doesn\u2019t seem out of place that a Risen following the origins of that path might have similar supernatural gifts.<br /> <br /> In this case the \u201cexotic\u201d isn\u2019t the creature, it is the specific spiritual beliefs of a culture that makes them exotic... and if you really wanted to emphasize that, introduce a Western Risen who has become a Wan Kuei by adopting one of the Dharma paths.<br /> <br /> Side-bar: Original Recipe Mummies could also be seen as variant Risen; they just had a True Mage cast a spell permanently linking the Wraith to its corpse and enabling it to rebuild said corpse using spiritual essence built up in the Dark Umbra. Exotic again being the particulars of how a specific culture interacted with the spiritual concepts of death and resurrection.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if they really are starting work on a Wr5 to coincide with development of the Wraith video game, perhaps the solution to handling the Wan Kuei in an appropriate manner lies in changing the game line they are associated with and making the implied connection to Risen canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:54:06-07:00","id":1400350,"title":"","content":"Sure, I think it can be done. Problems with the specific execution aside, there\u2019s nothing inherently wrong with the Wan Kuei as a critter, as long as they\u2019re not the thing Asia has instead of Kindred because Asia has to be different. If they\u2019re a specific culture of Risen that happens to overlap with Kindred in certain areas, causing them to interact with each other, it could be fine. But then the thing they fundamentally are is also found elsewhere. There\u2019s a thread on this very forum brainstorming that topic.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also be cool with the Wan Kuei culture of the Dharmas etc, being one that includes both types of creature, possibly even others as well, and purports to guide them all to enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 07-01-2020, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T11:34:11-07:00","id":1400359,"title":"","content":"kuei jin are meant to be a mix of different splats: vampires, risen, werewolfs, demons, and their mechanics mirror those of those different splats,<br /> they should've been called Wan Kuei: the Crossover","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:03:30-07:00","id":1400379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400350#post1400350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I think it can be done. Problems with the specific execution aside, there\u2019s nothing inherently wrong with the Wan Kuei as a critter, as long as they\u2019re not the thing Asia has instead of Kindred because Asia has to be different. If they\u2019re a specific culture of Risen that happens to overlap with Kindred in certain areas, causing them to interact with each other, it could be fine. But then the thing they fundamentally are is also found elsewhere. There\u2019s a thread on this very forum brainstorming that topic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree with this.<br /> <br /> Kindred should be worldwide and so should the other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:04:09-07:00","id":1400380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400359#post1400359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kuei jin are meant to be a mix of different splats: vampires, risen, werewolfs, demons, and their mechanics mirror those of those different splats,<br /> they should've been called Wan Kuei: the Crossover</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there an Exalted link in there as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:13:29-07:00","id":1400382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400380#post1400380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't there an Exalted link in there as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted came later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:38:11-07:00","id":1400429,"title":"","content":"They were a big influence on Exalted, and the same developer was central to both. But while the Wan Kuei (I'm glad we've moved past the linguistic absurdity that is &quot;Kuei-jin&quot;) do indeed encompass a whole lot ot stuff, Asian shapeshifters and changeling-like things got their own books as well. There was basically a Year of the Orientalism that purported to show how everything in Asia was strange and mystical and more awesome than you. But the rest didn't make it into a cult classic computer game, so...<br /> <br /> Many of us still recall Ms. Yellow Peril up and transforming into a spawn of Cthulhu. That's... not out of character for the Wan Kuei.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:58:58-07:00","id":1400435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400292#post1400292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair; given their metaphysics, I\u2019ve always thought of the Wan Kuei as a type of Risen, with the abilities gained their spiritual paths (the Dharmas) being the primary distinction between Eastern Risen/Wan Kuei and Western Risen.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Japanese Risen dude in WoD: Tokyo; he is not presented as being different than any other kind of Risen, though he's also managed to last an anomalously long time for one due to the connection to a corporate leadership position that he just won't give up. Nothing precludes Jade Kingdom wraiths from following the same procedure to rising in the Skinlands. The Hungry Dead are something else; simply enough, imagine that instead of turning into a ghost, dying caused you to undergo an effect similar to the Embrace. That is the situation for the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that Golconda is believed to be a variation on those paths and allowed access to supernatural disciplines beyond generational limits (i.e. even a 16th Gen could theoretically gain \u201cPlot Device/Rank 10\u201d in any discipline if they achieved and maintained Golconda) it doesn\u2019t seem out of place that a Risen following the origins of that path might have similar supernatural gifts. </div> </div> </div>Cool ghosts don't enter Golconda<br /> They Transcend and then go away<br /> Who's got the Passions to maintain Golconda?<br /> They've got ghost business to tie up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this case the \u201cexotic\u201d isn\u2019t the creature, it is the specific spiritual beliefs of a culture that makes them exotic... and if you really wanted to emphasize that, introduce a Western Risen who has become a Wan Kuei by adopting one of the Dharma paths.<br /> <br /> Side-bar: Original Recipe Mummies could also be seen as variant Risen; they just had a True Mage cast a spell permanently linking the Wraith to its corpse and enabling it to rebuild said corpse using spiritual essence built up in the Dark Umbra. Exotic again being the particulars of how a specific culture interacted with the spiritual concepts of death and resurrection.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if they really are starting work on a Wr5 to coincide with development of the Wraith video game, perhaps the solution to handling the Wan Kuei in an appropriate manner lies in changing the game line they are associated with and making the implied connection to Risen canon. </div> </div> </div>Risen are extremely purpose-driven and tend to be short-lived, as well as connected vitally to a fetter that houses their Shadow, so anything that makes them stick around and act like another type of monster might as well turn them into an entirely different order of being that is no longer one of the Risen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T18:26:57-07:00","id":1400439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400435#post1400435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Risen are extremely purpose-driven and tend to be short-lived, as well as connected vitally to a fetter that houses their Shadow, so anything that makes them stick around and act like another type of monster might as well turn them into an entirely different order of being that is no longer one of the Risen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this kind of reflects the differences in perspective here.<br /> <br /> Player 1#: Mummies, Risen, and Kuei-Jin are all spirits who come back to inhabit their bodies from the Underworld. So why not make them three variants on the same monster to make a more coherent linked cosmology?<br /> <br /> Player 2#: Because they're DIFFERENT. Why would you want to make them linked? That makes it BORING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:28:39-07:00","id":1400480,"title":"","content":"My view is that Risen is the BASE of a Wan Kuei or Mummy, then weirdness is applied.<br /> <br /> In the case of Mummies it is literally spelled out in the text that a True Mage is involved in casting the Spell of Life that changes the connection between the soul/wraith (mummies are stated to be wraiths in underworld except they lack a Shadow) and their body such that they can reanimate it with spiritual energy they\u2019ve built up in the netherworld.<br /> <br /> For the Wan Kuei I imagine the original purpose was \u201cGet the F- out of Yomi!\u201d which is why they come back nearly mindless (tortured into being barely more than an animal). This may also explain why they have an incorporated Shadow/P\u2019o instead of a Conduit as typical Risen do.<br /> <br /> Then other Wan Kuei get a hold of them and indoctrinate them into a set of mystical paths called Dharmas that channel and unlock supernatural potential and from that they learn to feed on Chi instead of Pathos (frankly, given Mage, all the various supernatural energies from vitae to gnosis to pathos to glamour to sekhem to chi are just specific flavors of what mages call quintessence; so learning to substitute one for the other via magical discipline doesn\u2019t seem that unusual).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:55:53-07:00","id":1400485,"title":"","content":"I think the reason why the Wan Kuei don't count as Risen is because they never /went/ to the Low Umbra at all, their essence/spirit went to Yomi entirely. Yomi is apart of the Middle-Umbra, which explains the differences of Risen and Wan Kuei. Not only that Risen don't lash out as do Wan Kuei do when they return, they still have all their faculties. Wan Kuei as inferenced before can go on rampages if not stopped by other Wan Kuei to be processed back to normalcy or just killed by a Kuei hunter or something else entirely. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> mentioned, the Wan Kuei don't even posses Conduits- instead their more malign self is attached within instead of having to be in a specific object or manifested outward (when a Wraith makes a deal with its Shadow to undergo the process of becoming a Risen, it can forego Conduits altogether IIRC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T07:05:16-07:00","id":1400514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400485#post1400485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the reason why the Wan Kuei don't count as Risen is because they never /went/ to the Low Umbra at all, their essence/spirit went to Yomi entirely. Yomi is apart of the Middle-Umbra, which explains the differences of Risen and Wan Kuei.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the lore on Yomi is that it is a stitched together patchwork of Middle (positive chi) and Low (negative chi) Umbral Realms that the Yama Kings essentially stole from creation to create their own world.<br /> <br /> Yes, that means the Yama Kings are something beyond your run of the mill spirit. That\u2019s the sort of thing you\u2019d need multiple archmages sharing a paradigm in order to wrench the cosmic landscape that far out of whack. The sheer corruption of that act (creating the Yomi World) is also why there\u2019s Demon Chi in addition to just positive and negative varieties.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a reason I always associate the Yama Kings with having been ancient Nephandi at a previous point in their existence when they come up in my campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T19:34:47-07:00","id":1400615,"title":"","content":"Yomi always existed as is in some sort of weird state between the Lower and Middle Umbra, the Yama Kings didn't make Yomi- it was made by the August Personage of Jade. The Yama Kings were part of the Celestial Bureaucracy but turned on their purpose of processing souls regularly, instead opting to harvesting Chi from them. Their the reason why the Wan Xian(?) got corrupted and got cursed in Kuei-Jin. I always consider Yomi to be more of the Middle Umbra however considering how hard it is for Wraiths to even get there and different it is in general from the Lower Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T12:00:10-07:00","id":1400800,"title":"","content":"My thoughts about Yomi have probably been influenced by my experience with M20; IIRC, they talk about &quot;Zones&quot; that can be part of multiple Umbral layers, or their own separate thing entirely that are just &quot;connected&quot; to the rest of the multiverse in some way. The Dreaming from Changeling is regarded as a Zone I think. The idea of it being &quot;made up&quot; of the stuff of Middle and Low Umbra but not really being part of either sounds like a special Zone to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:10:00-07:00","id":1405377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396105-v5-so-what-do-we-think-is-going-on-in-tokyo?p=1400138#post1400138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> first, Mages are not a good example, because they do have two different splats, one of which represents traditional mages (hedge magicians)<br /> <br /> second, I'm not against vampires not conforming to legends (hungry dead don't conform either),<br /> what I'm against is making hungry dead and other &quot;exotic vampires&quot; into other clans/bloodlines,<br /> we already have 7 to 13 clans, which are already hard enough to lump in together due to how different some of them are,<br /> <br /> if we need more &quot;exotic vampires&quot;, we should make them into different splats,<br /> <br /> and by exotic, I don't mean &quot;Asian&quot; or &quot;African&quot;, I mean flesh-eaters, Risen, soul suckers, xenomorphs, blood mages, or anything that would be sufficiently different from a cainite<br /> <br /> if there's flesh-eater vampires that can't bloodbond, let them be a different splat rather than a clan that has an antideluvian that likes steak<br /> <br /> just my two cents</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? If just having a supernatural merit/flaw can simulate a being, does one require making a whole different splat for it?<br /> That said, clan or bloodline has always been mostly a matter of taste for me. But then i'm the guy who always took the Caine mythos as exactly that, mythos, not exactly the absolute fact late 2nd &amp; 3rd editions tried to make out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}